(:entry "api/activate-menu-item" :names ("activate-menu-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Programmatically route the native command through its frame. Separators reject. This is not a claim that graphical OS menu selection or accelerators were exercised. Event metadata and resource state remain distinct; see MENUS guide for checked-command behavior. Native check-item activation toggles the resource before callbacks. A normal item can carry native command integer -1, so EVENT-CHECKED-P may be true even for a normal item; use CHECKED-P on a known check resource for actual state." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:activate-menu-item item)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU-ITEM is a live normal/check item.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native handled boolean; NIL for a disabled item.")) ("Description" (:p "Programmatically route the native command through its frame. Separators reject. This is not a claim that graphical OS menu selection or accelerators were exercised. Event metadata and resource state remain distinct; see MENUS guide for checked-command behavior. Native check-item activation toggles the resource before callbacks. A normal item can carry native command integer -1, so EVENT-CHECKED-P may be true even for a normal item; use CHECKED-P on a known check resource for actual state.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxFrame::ProcessCommand"))))
(:entry "api/activate-toolbar-tool" :names ("activate-toolbar-tool") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR ID for a realized action tool." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:activate-toolbar-tool toolbar id)")) ("Arguments" (:p "TOOLBAR ID for a realized action tool.")) ("Returns" (:p "NIL if disabled, T if accepted, independent of native handled result.")) ("Description" (:p "TOOLBAR ID for a realized action tool.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Native OnLeftClick path with check toggle before callbacks. :menu events; same-toolbar recursive activation and protected lifetime/loop entry reject. Callback conditions re-signal after native dispatch. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxToolBar::OnLeftClick / ToggleTool (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/activity-indicator" :names ("activity-indicator") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Window-owned native busy animation with verified initial state. Appearance/cadence and visibility remain port policy; no task is run by the control." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:activity-indicator")) ("Arguments" (:p "Required :parent WINDOW; optional :running-p generalized boolean defaults NIL, plus subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed ACTIVITY-INDICATOR WINDOW subtype.")) ("Description" (:p "Window-owned native busy animation with verified initial state. Appearance/cadence and visibility remain port policy; no task is run by the control.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. Native-backed CLOS subclasses/defaults/AFTER hooks and managed failure/root rollback. No native animation/timer/pointer adoption, progress percentage or artwork/styles. Requires wxUSE_ACTIVITYINDICATOR and wxUSE_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT, plus existing TIMER/core/base/adv. See docs/ACTIVITY-INDICATORS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxActivityIndicator::Create/Start/Stop/IsRunning, wxWidgets3.2.12; installed class exported from adv.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:activity-indicator :parent parent :running-p nil)") (:p "Direct subclass slot/default initargs and native-ready AFTER hooks; one concrete native widget kind, managed rollback on later initialization failure."))))
(:entry "api/activity-running-p" :names ("activity-running-p" "(setf activity-running-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or set native animation state. Starts are not cumulative and one NIL write stops. Repeated state requests are idempotent; state is not a promise of visible animation while hidden or while the GUI loop is blocked." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:activity-running-p indicator)")) ("Arguments" (:p "ACTIVITY-INDICATOR; SETF accepts a generalized boolean.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native T/NIL activity state; writer returns supplied value.")) ("Description" (:p "Read or set native animation state. Starts are not cumulative and one NIL write stops. Repeated state requests are idempotent; state is not a promise of visible animation while hidden or while the GUI loop is blocked.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Reader callback-safe; all access GUI-thread/lifetime checked. Writes reject event callbacks; defer via owner-bound UI action. Synchronous writes protect receiver/ancestors and gate nested native GUI/modal/clipboard/safe-idle entry through InputOperation. Native state readback must match request. See docs/ACTIVITY-INDICATORS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxActivityIndicator::IsRunning/Start/Stop, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:activity-running-p indicator) t)") (:p "Non-NIL calls native Start; NIL calls Stop; both verify state. Returns input generalized boolean. Callback writes reject, including another indicator; use owner-bound deferral. Parent/session teardown owns animation cleanup."))))
(:entry "api/add-child" :names ("add-child") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Add a child window to the layout. Non-start minor-axis alignment requires EXPAND NIL. Borders apply uniformly on four sides." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-child parent child &key (proportion 0) (border 8) (expand t) (align :start))")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT has a row/column; CHILD belongs to it; PROPORTION >= 0, BORDER >= 0, EXPAND boolean, ALIGN :START/:CENTER/:END.")) ("Returns" (:p "CHILD.")) ("Description" (:p "Add a child window to the layout. Non-start minor-axis alignment requires EXPAND NIL. Borders apply uniformly on four sides.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSizer::Add"))))
(:entry "api/add-notebook-page" :names ("add-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Setup-time AddPage, outside RUN/pumps/callbacks. Reject duplicate membership, wrong parent/type, containing sizer and incomplete page initialization. Pre-root canonical wrapper before publication; callback errors after adoption do not remove a successful page. Direct attached-page destruction is forbidden; destroy notebook/ancestor instead. First-page selection/callback count and native caption processing are port-specific." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-notebook-page book page &key (label \"\") select)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BOOK notebook, PAGE fully initialized panel parented directly to BOOK; :LABEL defaults empty, :SELECT defaults NIL.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied PAGE wrapper.")) ("Description" (:p "Setup-time AddPage, outside RUN/pumps/callbacks. Reject duplicate membership, wrong parent/type, containing sizer and incomplete page initialization. Pre-root canonical wrapper before publication; callback errors after adoption do not remove a successful page. Direct attached-page destruction is forbidden; destroy notebook/ancestor instead. First-page selection/callback count and native caption processing are port-specific.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; NOTEBOOK receivers and fixed setup-time PANEL pages only. Invalid handles/indices/ownership signal. No removal, reordering, reparenting, icons, arbitrary styles or other book controls. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md. Also specializes on AUI-NOTEBOOK with dynamic owned PANEL pages, maximum256 and caption<=4096UTF8 bytes. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBookCtrlBase::AddPage, wxNotebook native implementation (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/add-spacer" :names ("add-spacer") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Add fixed layout-axis spacing and relayout the parent." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-spacer parent size)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT has a row/column; SIZE is nonnegative.")) ("Returns" (:p "PARENT.")) ("Description" (:p "Add fixed layout-axis spacing and relayout the parent.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBoxSizer::AddSpacer"))))
(:entry "api/add-stc-marker" :names ("add-stc-marker") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native MarkerAdd. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-stc-marker control line marker)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; LINE native line.; MARKER native marker.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native integer result.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native MarkerAdd. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/add-stc-selection" :names ("add-stc-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native AddSelection. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-stc-selection control caret anchor)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; CARET native position.; ANCHOR native position.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native integer result.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native AddSelection. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/add-stretch" :names ("add-stretch") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Add flexible layout-axis spacing and relayout the parent." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-stretch parent &key (proportion 1))")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT has a row/column; PROPORTION is positive (default 1).")) ("Returns" (:p "PARENT.")) ("Description" (:p "Add flexible layout-axis spacing and relayout the parent.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSizer::AddStretchSpacer"))))
(:entry "api/add-toolbar-separator" :names ("add-toolbar-separator") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR. No action ID or state." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-toolbar-separator toolbar)")) ("Arguments" (:p "TOOLBAR. No action ID or state.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after addition.")) ("Description" (:p "TOOLBAR. No action ID or state.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Quiescent, before realization. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxToolBar::AddSeparator (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/add-toolbar-tool" :names ("add-toolbar-tool") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR ID LABEL; :art (:information default), :kind (:normal default) and :help (empty default)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-toolbar-tool toolbar id label &key (art :information) (kind :normal) (help \"\"))")) ("Arguments" (:p "TOOLBAR ID LABEL; :art (:information default), :kind (:normal default) and :help (empty default).")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied positive ID.")) ("Description" (:p "TOOLBAR ID LABEL; :art (:information default), :kind (:normal default) and :help (empty default).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Quiescent, before realization. IDs unique within toolbar; normal/check tools only. Seven stock art choices; UTF-8/NUL validation. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxToolBar::AddTool / wxArtProvider::GetBitmap (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/add-tree-root" :names ("add-tree-root") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Require empty tree; create/select root silently under native event blockers and publish checked token/view. Empty text valid. Failed Lisp view publication deletes new native item." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:add-tree-root tree value)")) ("Arguments" (:p "TREE control, VALUE string without NUL.")) ("Returns" (:p "Canonical TREE-ITEM root view.")) ("Description" (:p "Require empty tree; create/select root silently under native event blockers and publish checked token/view. Empty text valid. Failed Lisp view publication deletes new native item.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; managed tree-control/items only. Native tokens validate owner/lifetime; no raw IDs/adoption, multiselect, item data, icons, label editing, sorting, drag/drop, virtual models or arbitrary styles. Same-tree writes and nested native loops defer during tree callbacks. wxQt tree construction is explicitly unavailable pending generation-safe asynchronous event translation.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTreeCtrl::AddRoot (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/allow-next-key-event" :names ("allow-next-key-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Calls DoAllowNextEvent on current CHAR_HOOK context; keeps hook consumption independent from normal key generation." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:allow-next-key-event context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Current borrowed CHAR_HOOK EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "CONTEXT.")) ("Description" (:p "Calls DoAllowNextEvent on current CHAR_HOOK context; keeps hook consumption independent from normal key generation.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/append-grid-columns" :names ("append-grid-columns") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:append-grid-columns grid &optional count)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, optional COUNT (default1), each count1..256.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::AppendCols"))))
(:entry "api/append-grid-rows" :names ("append-grid-rows") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:append-grid-rows grid &optional count)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, optional COUNT (default1), each count1..256.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::AppendRows"))))
(:entry "api/append-item" :names ("append-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Append native text silently, preserving selected index/NIL. Empty strings/duplicates allowed. Native failure signals; no transactional rollback claim. LIST-CONTROL accepts a proper list of NUL-free cell strings matching columns, stored mode only, max100000 rows and1MiB total row text; returns appended zero-based row." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:append-item control values)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL list-box, VALUE string without NUL.")) ("Returns" (:p "The appended zero-based index.")) ("Description" (:p "Append native text silently, preserving selected index/NIL. Empty strings/duplicates allowed. Native failure signals; no transactional rollback claim. LIST-CONTROL accepts a proper list of NUL-free cell strings matching columns, stored mode only, max100000 rows and1MiB total row text; returns appended zero-based row.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session, LIST-BOX receivers only. Unsorted single selection, native-owned text values; no item client data, multi-selection, sorting, arbitrary styles, virtual list/data-view/tree support. Invalid indices/types/handles signal.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxItemContainer::Append(const wxString&) (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/append-tree-item" :names ("append-tree-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Append in native order, preserving selection silently. Native parent owner is inferred and checked; empty/duplicate text valid." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:append-tree-item parent value)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT live TREE-ITEM, VALUE string without NUL.")) ("Returns" (:p "New canonical TREE-ITEM child view.")) ("Description" (:p "Append in native order, preserving selection silently. Native parent owner is inferred and checked; empty/duplicate text valid.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; managed tree-control/items only. Native tokens validate owner/lifetime; no raw IDs/adoption, multiselect, item data, icons, label editing, sorting, drag/drop, virtual models or arbitrary styles. Same-tree writes and nested native loops defer during tree callbacks. wxQt tree construction is explicitly unavailable pending generation-safe asynchronous event translation.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTreeCtrl::AppendItem (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/application-handler" :names ("application-handler") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Borrowed native identity with inherited binding, dispatch, liveness and enabled state. Direct construction and subclass construction are rejected; explicit destruction signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup owns the native wxApp." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:application-handler")) ("Arguments" (:p "No public constructor; obtain the session view with CURRENT-APPLICATION-HANDLER.")) ("Returns" (:p "An EVENT-HANDLER subclass representing the managed wxApp.")) ("Description" (:p "Borrowed native identity with inherited binding, dispatch, liveness and enabled state. Direct construction and subclass construction are rejected; explicit destruction signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup owns the native wxApp.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "One cached view in the active main-thread session. No native wxApp subclassing, replacement or ownership transfer; native session bindings exist but OS delivery remains unverified. Saved views reject native access outside the session.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxApp / wxAppConsole::GetInstance and wxTheApp, managed instance only (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:current-application-handler)") (:p "Obtain the cached borrowed application view. Direct MAKE-INSTANCE, subclass construction and MAKE-EVENT-HANDLER construction are forbidden; only session cleanup owns native wxApp destruction."))))
(:entry "api/aui-notebook" :names ("aui-notebook") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed dynamic panel-page container, native programmatic tab splitting and fixed top/close styles, with at most256 pages. Mouse reordering is available while one group exists; split books use checked programmatic movement. Direct subclasses/default initargs/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure/root rollback." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:aui-notebook")) ("Arguments" (:p "Required :parent WINDOW and subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK WINDOW subtype.")) ("Description" (:p "Native-backed dynamic panel-page container, native programmatic tab splitting and fixed top/close styles, with at most256 pages. Mouse reordering is available while one group exists; split books use checked programmatic movement. Direct subclasses/default initargs/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure/root rollback.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:aui-notebook :parent parent)") (:p "One concrete native widget kind; validated parent, no native pointer adoption."))))
(:entry "api/begin-stc-undo-action" :names ("begin-stc-undo-action") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native BeginUndoAction. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:begin-stc-undo-action control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native BeginUndoAction. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bind-event" :names ("bind-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Register an observer without replacing any existing generic or control-specific registration. Signed 32-bit IDs are supported except -1 (reserved as native wxID_ANY; use NIL). LAST-ID requires ID and an ordered inclusive range. Observer bindings automatically Skip; contextual bindings start unskipped and control native Skip explicitly; relative callback order follows wxWidgets and is not a Lisp API guarantee. Failed registration releases temporary roots. Contextual access is limited to the innermost callback and expires at return, including on errors. A native entry-owned wxObject token adapter represents non-NIL user data without a Lisp/native pointer. EVENT-USER-DATA reads the per-binding value in snapshots/current contexts; there is no public mutation API for an existing association. ABI37 adds :NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGING/:NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGED notify-family observers/contexts. Only CHANGING veto affects navigation. Native page callbacks protect the originating book/ancestors and reject same-book recursive selection, modal and clipboard entry. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits. ABI39 tree selection changing/changed are native-only wxTreeEvent notify types. EVENT-TREE-ITEM captures canonical view identity, not frozen text/validity; same-tree writes and nested native loops defer until callback return. Native report-list and tree interaction kinds documented in REPORT-TREE-VIEWS are readonly notify payloads; expansion/collapse veto is available only for native before-events. No owned/synthetic/cloned views events." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bind-event source kind function &key id last-id with-context user-data)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is an EVENT-HANDLER/window; KIND is :CLICK, :TEXT-CHANGE, :TOGGLE, :SELECTION, :CLOSE, :QUERY-END-SESSION, :END-SESSION, :IDLE, :MENU or a registered command/notify name. FUNCTION takes one immutable EVENT. ID defaults NIL (any); LAST-ID defaults NIL (exact ID when ID is given). WITH-CONTEXT defaults NIL; when true FUNCTION takes (EVENT CONTEXT) instead of just EVENT. USER-DATA defaults NIL and associates any EQ-preserved Lisp value with this registration; callback arity is unchanged.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new independent EVENT-BINDING.")) ("Description" (:p "Register an observer without replacing any existing generic or control-specific registration. Signed 32-bit IDs are supported except -1 (reserved as native wxID_ANY; use NIL). LAST-ID requires ID and an ordered inclusive range. Observer bindings automatically Skip; contextual bindings start unskipped and control native Skip explicitly; relative callback order follows wxWidgets and is not a Lisp API guarantee. Failed registration releases temporary roots. Contextual access is limited to the innermost callback and expires at return, including on errors. A native entry-owned wxObject token adapter represents non-NIL user data without a Lisp/native pointer. EVENT-USER-DATA reads the per-binding value in snapshots/current contexts; there is no public mutation API for an existing association. ABI37 adds :NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGING/:NOTEBOOK-PAGE-CHANGED notify-family observers/contexts. Only CHANGING veto affects navigation. Native page callbacks protect the originating book/ancestors and reject same-book recursive selection, modal and clipboard entry. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits. ABI39 tree selection changing/changed are native-only wxTreeEvent notify types. EVENT-TREE-ITEM captures canonical view identity, not frozen text/validity; same-tree writes and nested native loops defer until callback return. Native report-list and tree interaction kinds documented in REPORT-TREE-VIEWS are readonly notify payloads; expansion/collapse veto is available only for native before-events. No owned/synthetic/cloned views events.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR. Stale/deleting receivers reject registration/queuing. Invalid event kinds, IDs and payload options signal Lisp errors; wrong receiver types use CLOS dispatch errors. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Contexts support scoped Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto. Arbitrary native events, native control-specific notify subclasses, arbitrary native userData pointers, external handler adoption and worker-thread dispatch remain unbound. Session bindings accept only the borrowed application view or an isolated owned handler; windows reject. Real OS delivery remains unverified. Skipped application END_SESSION callbacks can reach process-exiting defaults. Session bindings on attached pushed handlers reject so a window tail cannot route them to app defaults. Callback-local roots preserve current user data after self/peer unbind until return. Snapshots preserve the EQ reference after unbind/session end, not a deep copy of mutable contents. RADIO-BOX :radio-selection is a native-only command kind with copied/current index and native label metadata. Snapshot reads survive source/session cleanup; borrowed contexts require the exact innermost current callback. No owned/synthetic/cloned radio events. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md. :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE copies native checked/text metadata (text normally empty, including explicit notify; no inferred label); no owned/synthetic/clone. Snapshots survive cleanup, contexts expire. See docs/TOGGLE-BUTTONS.md. COMBO-BOX uses new native-only :COMBO-SELECTION and existing :TEXT-CHANGE. Physical native selections may emit multiple command/text notifications; explicit setters emit only their requested kind. See docs/COMBO-BOXES.md. WEB-VIEW adds native-only :WEB-MESSAGE, :WEB-SCRIPT-RESULT, :WEB-LOADED and :WEB-ERROR command snapshots with read-only payloads. JSON messages accept all frames/origins and carry no authentication; script result EVENT-EXTRA-LONG identifies its ticket and EVENT-INTEGER reports success1/error0. No owned/synthetic/cloned web events. GRID exposes selected immutable native notify event kinds160..170, scoped native validation and copied current cell values; see docs/GRID-EDITING.md. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md and docs/GRID.md. Native-only notify AUI100..104 kinds :aui-page-changing/:aui-page-changed/:aui-page-close/:aui-page-closed/:aui-drag-done. Selection/oldselection/targetID copied; payload writers and owned/synthetic/cloned forms reject. Scoped changing/close veto; closed index is former index, not current page. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. ABI57 raw key/mouse/focus/context-menu/size, STC and AUI native kinds have copied read-only payload metadata and reject owned/synthetic construction/cloning. Ordinary observers automatically Skip; scoped handlers explicitly Skip unhandled native input. STC styling has the exact innermost same-control STYLENEEDED StartStyling/SetStyling exception. AUI close/changing veto is native-scoped and CLOSED has former index/captured target ID. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md, docs/STYLED-TEXT.md and docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. AUI private tab-local PAGE_CHANGING events are translated by native wxAuiNotebook before Lisp delivery; public event-selection uses global catalogue indices. DRAG-DONE follows native paths/early returns without an exact count or ordering-transaction guarantee. AUI/native input/STC context IDs and timestamps are read-only. ABI58 :THREAD is a native base-family wxThreadEvent with copied immutable EVENT-TEXT, GUI-only callback dispatch and normal context lifetime. QUEUE-THREAD-EVENT alone permits worker posting after GUI binding; other GUI operations retain their thread rules. No owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::Bind member-method overload with wxEvent receiver and optional entry-owned numeric wxObject userData adapter; built-ins and registered command/notify tags (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/binding-active-p" :names ("binding-active-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query active-session registration and reap stale generic callback roots. Root pruning also runs at returned RUN/pump/notifying-setter boundaries and after explicit destruction. During a blocking RUN, native window closure may retain roots until a Lisp boundary or explicit unbinding. This does not change the control-specific callback-root contract." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:binding-active-p binding)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BINDING is an EVENT-BINDING.")) ("Returns" (:p "T if still registered on a live receiver, NIL after unbinding or receiver destruction/requested disposal.")) ("Description" (:p "Query active-session registration and reap stale generic callback roots. Root pruning also runs at returned RUN/pump/notifying-setter boundaries and after explicit destruction. During a blocking RUN, native window closure may retain roots until a Lisp boundary or explicit unbinding. This does not change the control-specific callback-root contract.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR. Stale/deleting receivers reject registration/queuing. Invalid event kinds, IDs and payload options signal Lisp errors; wrong receiver types use CLOS dispatch errors. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Contexts support scoped Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto. Arbitrary native events, native control-specific notify subclasses, arbitrary native userData pointers, external handler adoption and worker-thread dispatch remain unbound.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge registration/weak-lifetime predicate for wxEvtHandler bindings."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap" :names ("bitmap") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Session-owned wxBitmap constructed from exactly one IMAGE or SOURCE; SOURCE copies BITMAP or native STATIC-BITMAP. Native backing pixel/logical/DIP size and scale remain distinct." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:bitmap")) ("Arguments" (:p "Session-owned wxBitmap constructed from exactly one IMAGE or SOURCE; SOURCE copies BITMAP or native STATIC-BITMAP. Native backing pixel/logical/DIP size and scale remain distinct.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Session-owned wxBitmap constructed from exactly one IMAGE or SOURCE; SOURCE copies BITMAP or native STATIC-BITMAP. Native backing pixel/logical/DIP size and scale remain distinct.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBitmap, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:bitmap :image image)") (:p "Concrete native-backed resource/control; subclass initargs/defaults/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-alive-p" :names ("bitmap-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query active-session bitmap validity; NIL after explicit disposal." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-alive-p object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Query active-session bitmap validity; NIL after explicit disposal.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-dip-size" :names ("bitmap-dip-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap GetDIPSize." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-dip-size object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "(width height) in DIP.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native wxBitmap GetDIPSize.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-image" :names ("bitmap-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Convert native bitmap to image. Native alpha premultiplication/rounding can discard RGB under transparent pixels; this is not lossless archival conversion." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-image object &key (class 'image))")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap &key class")) ("Returns" (:p "A new independently owned IMAGE.")) ("Description" (:p "Convert native bitmap to image. Native alpha premultiplication/rounding can discard RGB under transparent pixels; this is not lossless archival conversion.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-logical-size" :names ("bitmap-logical-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap GetLogicalSize; platform units differ from backing pixels." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-logical-size object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "(width height) in native logical units.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native wxBitmap GetLogicalSize; platform units differ from backing pixels.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-scale-factor" :names ("bitmap-scale-factor") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap GetScaleFactor." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-scale-factor object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "Native double-float scale factor.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native wxBitmap GetScaleFactor.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-size" :names ("bitmap-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxBitmap dimensions; native static display readback may resample for DPI." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-size object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "(width height) in backing pixels.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native wxBitmap dimensions; native static display readback may resample for DPI.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/bitmap-value" :names ("bitmap-value" "(setf bitmap-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy native GetBitmap; caller must dispose result. SETF invokes native SetBitmap and retains an independent native value. Native DPI resampling may change backing pixels and scale." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:bitmap-value control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "static-bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "A new owned BITMAP on each read.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy native GetBitmap; caller must dispose result. SETF invokes native SetBitmap and retains an independent native value. Native DPI resampling may change backing pixels and scale.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:bitmap-value object) value)") (:p "Invoke the native mutation with copied/checked data; return supplied value. See supported scope."))))
(:entry "api/button" :names ("button") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxButton with click handler support." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:button")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass: WXLAMBDA:WINDOW.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance of this class or a subclass (WINDOW itself is abstract).")) ("Description" (:p "CLOS wrapper for wxButton with click handler support.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Construction requires an active main-thread application session. Concrete classes create their native widgets in inherited INITIALIZE-INSTANCE methods; subclass AFTER hooks can use them. Native handles cannot be supplied as initargs. Lisp subclassing does not imply native C++ virtual callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxButton (wxWidgets 3.2); this is a Lisp wrapper, not a native subclass.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:button :parent parent :label \"Button\")") (:p "PARENT is required; LABEL defaults to Button. Class :DEFAULT-INITARGS and custom slot initargs are honored; native creation precedes subclass AFTER hooks."))))
(:entry "api/calendar-date" :names ("calendar-date" "(setf calendar-date)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Local civil date without exposed time-of-day/timezone/Unix/universal-time. Gregorian leap/day/range validation; native construction/readback must preserve requested date. Native getter with no supported committed date signals NATIVE-ERROR." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:calendar-date control &key notify)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DATE-PICKER; SETF exact (year month day), optional :notify generalized boolean defaults NIL. Reader accepts/ignores :notify for SETF protocol.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native committed date tuple; writer returns supplied list.")) ("Description" (:p "Local civil date without exposed time-of-day/timezone/Unix/universal-time. Gregorian leap/day/range validation; native construction/readback must preserve requested date. Native getter with no supported committed date signals NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session, live native lifetime, Gregorian dates1900..2100 and representable native local calendar dates only. Fixed inclusive1900-01-01..2100-12-31 range; native range/value readback required. Default native date editor style; no NIL/time/timezone/range/style APIs. Input callback/composite-child/propagation guards and early generic Destroy suppression. Requires core/base/adv, wxUSE_DATEPICKCTRL and wxUSE_DATETIME. See docs/DATE-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDatePickerCtrl::GetValue/SetValue and bounded wxDateTime date adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:calendar-date picker :notify t) '(2030 12 31))") (:p "Silent by default; explicit notify emits exactly one native date-change event even unchanged. Same-picker callback writes reject; silent cross-picker synchronization allowed. Callback errors re-signal with committed state retained. List not retained."))))
(:entry "api/call-with-application" :names ("call-with-application") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Initialize a main-thread GUI session, call FUNCTION, and clean up on normal return or unwinding. RUN is explicit." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:call-with-application function)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FUNCTION is a zero-argument function.")) ("Returns" (:p "The values returned by FUNCTION.")) ("Description" (:p "Initialize a main-thread GUI session, call FUNCTION, and clean up on normal return or unwinding. RUN is explicit.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "The Lisp must run on its initial/main thread; nested or repeated application sessions are rejected. Setup/native failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; body conditions propagate.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEntryStart / wxEntryCleanup"))))
(:entry "api/cancel-stc-autocomplete" :names ("cancel-stc-autocomplete") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native AutoCompCancel. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:cancel-stc-autocomplete control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native AutoCompCancel. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/cancel-stc-call-tip" :names ("cancel-stc-call-tip") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native CallTipCancel. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:cancel-stc-call-tip control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native CallTipCancel. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/cancel-ui-action" :names ("cancel-ui-action") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove queued work and release its Lisp closure root. Cannot interrupt active work; owner expiry may already have pruned it." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:cancel-ui-action action)")) ("Arguments" (:p "UI-ACTION ticket.")) ("Returns" (:p "T if a queued entry was removed, NIL if not pending/executing/completed/already removed.")) ("Description" (:p "Remove queued work and release its Lisp closure root. Cannot interrupt active work; owner expiry may already have pruned it.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session. FIFO safe idle delivery via RUN/full event polling only; no recursive action delivery during modal loops; nested RUN/pumps reject. Optional weak owner drops stale/pending-destruction work. Errors pause retained following work and re-signal at outer RUN/poll. At most1024 pending actions. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md for safe structural exception, cancellation, root release and supported scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge-specific queue removal."))))
(:entry "api/cancel-ui-timer" :names ("cancel-ui-timer") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Stop native notifications, remove coalesced due work and release its root. Current periodic function can cancel itself; cannot interrupt an executing function." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:cancel-ui-timer timer)")) ("Arguments" (:p "UI-TIMER ticket.")) ("Returns" (:p "T if a registration was removed, NIL if already absent.")) ("Description" (:p "Stop native notifications, remove coalesced due work and release its root. Current periodic function can cancel itself; cannot interrupt an executing function.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session. Interval1..86400000ms, at most256 logical registrations; periodic default/optional one-shot, weak window owner or session lifetime. Coalesced safe-idle delivery under RUN/full polling, excluded from nested modal/native/callback/other safe work. wxUSE_TIMER required; OSX start currently verified only for wxWidgets3.2.12. See docs/UI-TIMERS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTimer::Stop/destructor at a safe non-Notify point."))))
(:entry "api/canvas-client-size" :names ("canvas-client-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Get native client size through ToDIP. Integer scaling may round by a pixel. Resize repaints retained data but does not rewrite the model; applications can rebuild geometry from this value. Reports retained native paint failure before returning." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:canvas-client-size canvas)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Live DRAWING-CANVAS.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh (width height) client dimensions in DIP.")) ("Description" (:p "Get native client size through ToDIP. Integer scaling may round by a pixel. Resize repaints retained data but does not rewrite the model; applications can rebuild geometry from this value. Reports retained native paint failure before returning.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session, live managed DRAWING-CANVAS, no DC/native object adoption or Lisp paint callback. Native scene staging, rendering/export and Input lifetime/reentry guards; writes/export reject event callbacks. Copied bounded data only; font/paint/DPI appearance is native. See docs/DRAWING-CANVAS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::GetClientSize/ToDIP(wxSize), wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/canvas-content" :names ("canvas-content" "(setf canvas-content)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Items are (:rect x y width height rgb), (:ellipse x y width height rgb), (:line x1 y1 x2 y2 rgb stroke-width), (:text x y string point-size rgb), or (:bitmap x y width height pixels). RGB bytes0..255, coordinates/endpoints ±10000, non-bitmap extents1..10000, line widths1..32, text6..72 points in native Swiss/sans family. Text is NUL/CR/LF-free, total65536 UTF-8 bytes; bitmaps1..256 per axis use exact simple RGB byte vectors, total2MiB. On-screen geometry uses DIP; no alpha/native resource handles. ABI60 adds :RGBA-BITMAP with copied straight RGBA bytes (4 per pixel), the same1..256 extent and2MiB aggregate scene cap; native alpha composition and screen DIP sizing apply." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:canvas-content canvas)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DRAWING-CANVAS. SETF value is a proper plist with exactly :background RGB and :items, containing at most512 bounded primitives.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh normalized deep scene copy, including strings/RGB lists/pixel vectors. SETF returns supplied object.")) ("Description" (:p "Items are (:rect x y width height rgb), (:ellipse x y width height rgb), (:line x1 y1 x2 y2 rgb stroke-width), (:text x y string point-size rgb), or (:bitmap x y width height pixels). RGB bytes0..255, coordinates/endpoints ±10000, non-bitmap extents1..10000, line widths1..32, text6..72 points in native Swiss/sans family. Text is NUL/CR/LF-free, total65536 UTF-8 bytes; bitmaps1..256 per axis use exact simple RGB byte vectors, total2MiB. On-screen geometry uses DIP; no alpha/native resource handles. ABI60 adds :RGBA-BITMAP with copied straight RGBA bytes (4 per pixel), the same1..256 extent and2MiB aggregate scene cap; native alpha composition and screen DIP sizing apply.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session, live managed DRAWING-CANVAS, no DC/native object adoption or Lisp paint callback. Native scene staging, rendering/export and Input lifetime/reentry guards; writes/export reject event callbacks. Copied bounded data only; font/paint/DPI appearance is native. See docs/DRAWING-CANVAS.md. Getter validates native lifetime and reports retained native paint errors. Invalid staging preserves prior scene; successful paint/new content clears paint error. Input/output objects are independent copies.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bounded wxDC geometry/text/bitmap operations with private wxColour/wxFont/wxImage/wxBitmap adapters, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:canvas-content canvas) '(:background (245 248 252) :items ((:rect 20 20 100 40 (30 140 190)))))") (:p "Validate/copy bounded scene, stage and replace all native items/bitmaps and request refresh, then synchronize the stored Lisp scene before reporting callback errors. Reject event callbacks and same-canvas native operation recursion; defer via owner-bound UI action or safe UI timer body."))))
(:entry "api/checkbox" :names ("checkbox") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for a two-state wxCheckBox." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:checkbox")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass: WXLAMBDA:WINDOW.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance of this class or a subclass (WINDOW itself is abstract).")) ("Description" (:p "CLOS wrapper for a two-state wxCheckBox.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Construction requires an active main-thread application session. Concrete classes create their native widgets in inherited INITIALIZE-INSTANCE methods; subclass AFTER hooks can use them. Native handles cannot be supplied as initargs. Lisp subclassing does not imply native C++ virtual callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCheckBox (wxWidgets 3.2); this is a Lisp wrapper, not a native subclass.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:checkbox :parent parent :label \"\" :checked nil)") (:p "PARENT is required; LABEL defaults to empty, CHECKED to NIL. Class :DEFAULT-INITARGS and custom slot initargs are honored; native creation precedes subclass AFTER hooks."))))
(:entry "api/checked-p" :names ("checked-p" "(setf checked-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read boolean control/resource state. Menu normal/separator items reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:checked-p control &key notify)")) ("Arguments" (:p "RECEIVER is a live two-state CHECKBOX, TOGGLE-BUTTON or check MENU-ITEM. Optional NOTIFY affects writes; reads ignore it.")) ("Returns" (:p "T or NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Read boolean control/resource state. Menu normal/separator items reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCheckBox::GetValue; wxMenuItem::IsChecked / Check; wxToggleButton::GetValue/SetValue (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:checked-p checkbox :notify notify) new-value)") (:p "Store generalized boolean state; reads normalize it to T/NIL, while SETF returns the supplied value. :NOTIFY T emits a synchronous toggle event. Writers are generic functions with VALUE first, followed by the receiver. For menu items :NOTIFY T rejects before mutation; silent resource changes are allowed during callbacks. TOGGLE-BUTTON is silent by default; :NOTIFY T commits then emits exactly one :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE event even unchanged. Same-button callback writes reject; escaping callback errors do not roll state back. See docs/TOGGLE-BUTTONS.md."))))
(:entry "api/choice" :names ("choice") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxChoice with selection handler support." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:choice")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass: WXLAMBDA:WINDOW.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance of this class or a subclass (WINDOW itself is abstract).")) ("Description" (:p "CLOS wrapper for wxChoice with selection handler support.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Construction requires an active main-thread application session. Concrete classes create their native widgets in inherited INITIALIZE-INSTANCE methods; subclass AFTER hooks can use them. Native handles cannot be supplied as initargs. Lisp subclassing does not imply native C++ virtual callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxChoice (wxWidgets 3.2); this is a Lisp wrapper, not a native subclass.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:choice :parent parent :items nil :selection nil)") (:p "PARENT is required; ITEMS defaults to NIL, SELECTION to NIL. Class :DEFAULT-INITARGS and custom slot initargs are honored; native creation precedes subclass AFTER hooks."))))
(:entry "api/clear-grid-selection" :names ("clear-grid-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Clear native selection." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clear-grid-selection grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Clear native selection.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::ClearSelection"))))
(:entry "api/clear-items" :names ("clear-items") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Clear all items/selection silently; allowed in list event callbacks. Temporary native event blocker restores managed pushed-handler stack. LIST-CONTROL clears stored rows or sets virtual count0, retaining columns." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clear-items control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL list-box.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after success.")) ("Description" (:p "Clear all items/selection silently; allowed in list event callbacks. Temporary native event blocker restores managed pushed-handler stack. LIST-CONTROL clears stored rows or sets virtual count0, retaining columns.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session, LIST-BOX receivers only. Unsorted single selection, native-owned text values; no item client data, multi-selection, sorting, arbitrary styles, virtual list/data-view/tree support. Invalid indices/types/handles signal.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxItemContainer::Clear (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/clear-stc-document-style" :names ("clear-stc-document-style") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native ClearDocumentStyle. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clear-stc-document-style control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native ClearDocumentStyle. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/clear-stc-indicator-range" :names ("clear-stc-indicator-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native GetLength, IndicatorClearRange. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clear-stc-indicator-range control start length)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; START native position.; LENGTH native nonnegative.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native GetLength, IndicatorClearRange. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/clear-stc-selections" :names ("clear-stc-selections") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native ClearSelections. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clear-stc-selections control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native ClearSelections. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/clear-stc-styles" :names ("clear-stc-styles") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native StyleClearAll. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clear-stc-styles control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native StyleClearAll. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/client-to-screen" :names ("client-to-screen") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native ClientToScreen; input±1000000 logical units." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:client-to-screen object x y)")) ("Arguments" (:p "window x y")) ("Returns" (:p "Two-element converted coordinate list.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native ClientToScreen; input±1000000 logical units.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/clipboard-text" :names ("clipboard-text" "(setf clipboard-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Briefly opens the clipboard, reads wxTextDataObject with Unicode/legacy text support, closes and restores PRIMARY preference. Availability can change; a supported-text transfer failure signals rather than returning NIL. Explicit UTF-8 lengths copy native storage. NUL text rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clipboard-text )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments; standard system clipboard only.")) ("Returns" (:p "An independent Lisp string, including empty, or NIL when no native text format is available.")) ("Description" (:p "Briefly opens the clipboard, reads wxTextDataObject with Unicode/legacy text support, closes and restores PRIMARY preference. Availability can change; a supported-text transfer failure signals rather than returning NIL. Explicit UTF-8 lengths copy native storage. NUL text rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session. Already-open/reentrant access rejects. Native callback conditions re-signal after cleanup; no native clipboard/data object receiver, selection ranges or binary formats. Native port conversion/line endings apply. ABI37 rejects entry during notebook navigation/page callbacks; defer to later application work. ABI38 also rejects entry while a list-origin selection/activation callback is active. ABI39 also defers entry during tree operations/selection callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxClipboard::Get/Open/Close/IsSupported/GetData, wxTextDataObject::GetText (wxWidgets 3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:clipboard-text) value)") (:p "Generic writer specialized on STRING. Rejects NUL; replaces all previous formats with text and returns the same VALUE object. SetData ownership/failure cleanup accounts for MSW/OLE. Does not flush automatically. Native write failures/callback conditions do not imply rollback of prior clipboard state. See FLUSH-CLIPBOARD for persistence."))))
(:entry "api/clipboard-text-available-p" :names ("clipboard-text-available-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Advisory query on the standard clipboard; opens/closes and restores native PRIMARY preference. Does not read clipboard contents. A later read can differ." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clipboard-text-available-p )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "T when Unicode or legacy text is supported, NIL otherwise.")) ("Description" (:p "Advisory query on the standard clipboard; opens/closes and restores native PRIMARY preference. Does not read clipboard contents. A later read can differ.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; unavailable/open/busy failures signal NATIVE-ERROR. Callback conditions take precedence after cleanup. No async format query. ABI37 rejects entry during notebook navigation/page callbacks; defer to later application work. ABI38 also rejects entry while a list-origin selection/activation callback is active. ABI39 also defers entry during tree operations/selection callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxClipboard::Get/Open/Close/IsSupported (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/clock-time" :names ("clock-time" "(setf clock-time)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Time-of-day components only, independent of date and timestamp. Reject NIL, invalid list shape/ranges, fractions and leap second60. Native getter with no valid supported time signals NATIVE-ERROR; writes require native readback match." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clock-time control &key notify)")) ("Arguments" (:p "TIME-PICKER; SETF exact (hour minute second) and optional :notify generalized boolean defaults NIL. Reader accepts/ignores :notify for SETF protocol.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native committed time tuple; writer returns supplied list.")) ("Description" (:p "Time-of-day components only, independent of date and timestamp. Reject NIL, invalid list shape/ranges, fractions and leap second60. Native getter with no valid supported time signals NATIVE-ERROR; writes require native readback match.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and live WINDOW lifetime. Required (hour minute second), hour0..23 and minute/second0..59, whole seconds only. Fixed local2012-01-01 native construction with component roundtrip/readback, no date/timezone/Unix/universal-time/scheduling API. Default native editor style/locale display. Input origin/composite/propagation and early Destroy guards; core/base/adv plus wxUSE_TIMEPICKCTRL/wxUSE_DATETIME required. See docs/TIME-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTimePickerCtrl::GetValue/SetValue and bounded wxDateTime component adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:clock-time picker :notify t) '(0 0 0))") (:p "Silent by default; notify emits exactly one native time-change event even unchanged. Same-picker callback writes reject; silent cross-picker synchronization supported. Input list not retained; original callback errors re-signal after native setter returns with committed time retained."))))
(:entry "api/clone-event" :names ("clone-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Call native Clone for exact wxCommandEvent/wxNotifyEvent/wxCloseEvent/wxIdleEvent with supported tags, clear native origin, preserve supported values and reject borrowed userdata/client pointers. Source and clone are independently mutable/disposable. Capture effective command GetString before clearing origin, so lazy wxEVT_TEXT payload becomes detached value data." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:clone-event context &rest initargs &key class &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a live OWNED-EVENT or current innermost EVENT-CONTEXT. CLASS and subclass slot initargs are forwarded; payload overrides reject.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new detached OWNED-EVENT or subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Call native Clone for exact wxCommandEvent/wxNotifyEvent/wxCloseEvent/wxIdleEvent with supported tags, clear native origin, preserve supported values and reject borrowed userdata/client pointers. Source and clone are independently mutable/disposable. Capture effective command GetString before clearing origin, so lazy wxEVT_TEXT payload becomes detached value data.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session. Expired/suspended contexts and unsupported native classes reject. Snapshots have no method. No origin retention, arbitrary native ownership or source transfer. Non-NIL borrowed binding userData still rejects cloning, even after self-unbind; the presence guard does not dereference a freed native adapter. Notebook native page events cannot be synthesized, queued, processed as owned events or contextually cloned in ABI37. ABI38 simple listbox command kinds support owned/synthetic dispatch and text/selection payloads; no automatic list-model mutation. Derived tree selection kinds cannot be synthesized/owned/cloned in ABI39. Native WEB-VIEW message/script-result/loaded/error kinds reject owned/synthetic construction and detached cloning; copied immutable snapshots remain readable after delivery. ABI57 raw key/mouse/focus/context-menu/size, STC and AUI native kinds have copied read-only payload metadata and reject owned/synthetic construction/cloning. Ordinary observers automatically Skip; scoped handlers explicitly Skip unhandled native input. STC styling has the exact innermost same-control STYLENEEDED StartStyling/SetStyling exception. AUI close/changing veto is native-scoped and CLOSED has former index/captured target ID. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md, docs/STYLED-TEXT.md and docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::Clone with bounded detached ownership (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/close-window" :names ("close-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously generate the frame close request via wxWindow::Close(force). A vetoed request returns NIL. A consuming contextual callback may return acceptance T without deleting anything, even for FORCE. Set Skip true to delegate to native default closing when appropriate. Callback conditions re-signal at this Lisp boundary; a handled nested condition does not stop RUN. Use DESTROY-WINDOW for explicit destruction. A callback can explicitly mutate CanVeto through SETF EVENT-CAN-VETO-P; FORCE is not an immutable capability limit." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:close-window frame &key force)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME is a live FRAME. Optional FORCE defaults NIL; true initializes native CanVeto false.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native close acceptance as T/NIL; not a destruction/liveness guarantee.")) ("Description" (:p "Synchronously generate the frame close request via wxWindow::Close(force). A vetoed request returns NIL. A consuming contextual callback may return acceptance T without deleting anything, even for FORCE. Set Skip true to delegate to native default closing when appropriate. Callback conditions re-signal at this Lisp boundary; a handled nested condition does not stop RUN. Use DESTROY-WINDOW for explicit destruction. A callback can explicitly mutate CanVeto through SETF EVENT-CAN-VETO-P; FORCE is not an immutable capability limit.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required for native context or frame operations. Expired/suspended contexts and invalid/deleting frames signal NATIVE-ERROR. Saved snapshots need no session. Close and registered notify families permit checked veto. Other native control-specific notify subclasses, validated OS session delivery and arbitrary event classes remain open. Closing a protected active-modal ancestor rejects until SHOW-MODAL returns; modal dialog close itself uses cancellation.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Close(bool), wxFrame receivers only (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/combo-box" :names ("combo-box") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Editable single-line fixed unsorted choices with generic TEXT/SETF, SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT. Native CmpNoCase duplicate/case-only choices reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:combo-box")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT (or :parent for MAKE-INSTANCE); :items finite proper list0..256 nonempty single-line strings, :value default empty, :selection NIL/index. A non-NIL index and nonempty initial value conflict. Factory accepts :class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New COMBO-BOX or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Editable single-line fixed unsorted choices with generic TEXT/SETF, SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT. Native CmpNoCase duplicate/case-only choices reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and native lifetime guards. Strings reject NUL/CR/LF. No readonly/sort/item-mutation/text-position API, native adoption or full class parity. See docs/COMBO-BOXES.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxComboBox::Create/GetSelection/SetSelection/GetCount/GetString; wxTextEntry::GetValue/ChangeValue (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:combo-box :parent panel :items '(\"Inbox\" \"Archive\") :selection 0)") (:p "Direct subclass slots/default initargs, native-ready AFTER hooks and managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/complete-stc-autocomplete" :names ("complete-stc-autocomplete") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native GetReadOnly, AutoCompComplete. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:complete-stc-autocomplete control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native GetReadOnly, AutoCompComplete. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/current-application-handler" :names ("current-application-handler") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Borrow the bridge application event handler without constructing or taking ownership of wxApp. Native main-thread/session validation runs on every lookup, including cached lookups." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:current-application-handler )")) ("Arguments" (:p "None.")) ("Returns" (:p "The EQ-identical APPLICATION-HANDLER view for the current session.")) ("Description" (:p "Borrow the bridge application event handler without constructing or taking ownership of wxApp. Native main-thread/session validation runs on every lookup, including cached lookups.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR. One session per process. No external application adoption; native session bindings exist but OS delivery remains unverified.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAppConsole::GetInstance / wxTheApp, bridge-managed application only (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/date-picker" :names ("date-picker") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Required date control with native wxDP_DEFAULT|wxDP_SHOWCENTURY formatting/presentation. No raw adoption or uncreated wrapper." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:date-picker")) ("Arguments" (:p "Required :parent WINDOW; optional :date exact (year month day) defaults (2000 1 1), plus subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed DATE-PICKER WINDOW subtype.")) ("Description" (:p "Required date control with native wxDP_DEFAULT|wxDP_SHOWCENTURY formatting/presentation. No raw adoption or uncreated wrapper.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session, live native lifetime, Gregorian dates1900..2100 and representable native local calendar dates only. Fixed inclusive1900-01-01..2100-12-31 range; native range/value readback required. Default native date editor style; no NIL/time/timezone/range/style APIs. Input callback/composite-child/propagation guards and early generic Destroy suppression. Requires core/base/adv, wxUSE_DATEPICKCTRL and wxUSE_DATETIME. See docs/DATE-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDatePickerCtrl::Create/SetRange, wxWidgets3.2.12; installed native component adv.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:date-picker :parent parent :date '(2028 2 29))") (:p "Direct subclasses/default initargs and native-ready AFTER hooks with managed failure/root rollback; one concrete native kind per ancestry."))))
(:entry "api/defer-ui-action" :names ("defer-ui-action") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Queue strongly rooted work without inline execution. One action per safe native idle iteration after callback/native stacks return. Captured borrowed event contexts expire; capture snapshots/values instead." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:defer-ui-action function &key owner)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FUNCTION of no arguments and optional :OWNER window (default NIL, session-owned).")) ("Returns" (:p "An immutable UI-ACTION ticket. Function return values are ignored.")) ("Description" (:p "Queue strongly rooted work without inline execution. One action per safe native idle iteration after callback/native stacks return. Captured borrowed event contexts expire; capture snapshots/values instead.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session. FIFO safe idle delivery via RUN/full event polling only; no recursive action delivery during modal loops; nested RUN/pumps reject. Optional weak owner drops stale/pending-destruction work. Errors pause retained following work and re-signal at outer RUN/poll. At most1024 pending actions. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md for safe structural exception, cancellation, root release and supported scope. Lisp function/owner type errors and native queue/lifecycle errors reject; failed enqueue removes its Lisp root.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWakeUpIdle / managed wxApp::ProcessIdle safe point, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/define-stc-marker" :names ("define-stc-marker") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native MarkerDefine. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:define-stc-marker control marker symbol)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; MARKER native marker.; SYMBOL native marker-symbol.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native MarkerDefine. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/delete-all-stc-markers" :names ("delete-all-stc-markers") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native MarkerDeleteAll. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-all-stc-markers control marker)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; MARKER native marker.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native MarkerDeleteAll. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/delete-grid-columns" :names ("delete-grid-columns") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-grid-columns grid position &optional count)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, POSITION, optional COUNT (default1), each count1..256.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::DeleteCols"))))
(:entry "api/delete-grid-rows" :names ("delete-grid-rows") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-grid-rows grid position &optional count)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, POSITION, optional COUNT (default1), each count1..256.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::DeleteRows"))))
(:entry "api/delete-item" :names ("delete-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete silently. Deleting the selected row clears selection; an earlier deletion shifts selected index down one, preserving the same item. No stable IDs or automatic domain-model updates. LIST-CONTROL deletes a stored report row only; virtual rows use item-count SETF." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-item control index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL list-box, INDEX existing zero-based item index.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after success.")) ("Description" (:p "Delete silently. Deleting the selected row clears selection; an earlier deletion shifts selected index down one, preserving the same item. No stable IDs or automatic domain-model updates. LIST-CONTROL deletes a stored report row only; virtual rows use item-count SETF.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session, LIST-BOX receivers only. Unsorted single selection, native-owned text values; no item client data, multi-selection, sorting, arbitrary styles, virtual list/data-view/tree support. Invalid indices/types/handles signal.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxItemContainer::Delete (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/delete-list-column" :names ("delete-list-column") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete an existing column while item count0; return CONTROL." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-list-column control index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control index)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Delete an existing column while item count0; return CONTROL.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::DeleteColumn"))))
(:entry "api/delete-notebook-page" :names ("delete-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete page and descendants; wrappers become invalid. Explicit deletion does not manufacture user-close veto/CLOSE/CLOSED sequence." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-notebook-page book index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK and current zero-based INDEX.")) ("Returns" (:p "T.")) ("Description" (:p "Delete page and descendants; wrappers become invalid. Explicit deletion does not manufacture user-close veto/CLOSE/CLOSED sequence.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::DeletePage, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/delete-pending-events" :names ("delete-pending-events") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete queued native events without invoking callbacks; bindings and other handler queues remain intact. Synchronize wxApp pending-handler membership after deletion. Transferred input wrappers remain consumed; later queueing/posting still works." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-pending-events handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live non-application EVENT-HANDLER/window.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after deleting the target queue, including an empty queue.")) ("Description" (:p "Delete queued native events without invoking callbacks; bindings and other handler queues remain intact. Synchronize wxApp pending-handler membership after deletion. Transferred input wrappers remain consumed; later queueing/posting still works.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session at a non-dispatch boundary required. Borrowed APPLICATION-HANDLER, RUN/pump/callback use and invalid/stale receivers reject. No application-wide deletion, count, cancellation rollback or per-handler pending query/processing is supplied. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md. ABI58 :THREAD is a native base-family wxThreadEvent with copied immutable EVENT-TEXT, GUI-only callback dispatch and normal context lifetime. QUEUE-THREAD-EVENT alone permits worker posting after GUI binding; other GUI operations retain their thread rules. No owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::DeletePendingEvents plus native pending-handler-list synchronization (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/delete-stc-marker" :names ("delete-stc-marker") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native MarkerDelete. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-stc-marker control line marker)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; LINE native line.; MARKER native marker.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native MarkerDelete. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/delete-tree-item" :names ("delete-tree-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invalidate/delete whole subtree. Preserve an outside selection, otherwise choose surviving parent/root silently; deleting root leaves empty. Revision-prune invalid cached views." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:delete-tree-item item)")) ("Arguments" (:p "ITEM live TREE-ITEM.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after success.")) ("Description" (:p "Invalidate/delete whole subtree. Preserve an outside selection, otherwise choose surviving parent/root silently; deleting root leaves empty. Revision-prune invalid cached views.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; managed tree-control/items only. Native tokens validate owner/lifetime; no raw IDs/adoption, multiselect, item data, icons, label editing, sorting, drag/drop, virtual models or arbitrary styles. Same-tree writes and nested native loops defer during tree callbacks. wxQt tree construction is explicitly unavailable pending generation-safe asynchronous event translation.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTreeCtrl::Delete and internal delete notifications (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/destroy-bitmap" :names ("destroy-bitmap") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Release native session-owned bitmap; displays retain independent native values." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:destroy-bitmap object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "bitmap")) ("Returns" (:p "BITMAP.")) ("Description" (:p "Release native session-owned bitmap; displays retain independent native values.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/destroy-event" :names ("destroy-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Release this independent native event. Copies already queued/processing remain valid; repeated destruction rejects. Session cleanup releases undisposed owned events, even if the Lisp wrapper was collected." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:destroy-event event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a live OWNED-EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after immediate native deletion.")) ("Description" (:p "Release this independent native event. Copies already queued/processing remain valid; repeated destruction rejects. Session cleanup releases undisposed owned events, even if the Lisp wrapper was collected.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required; dead/invalid native resource or failed wrapper signals NATIVE-ERROR. No snapshot/context destruction or transfer of an event already owned by wxWidgets. A source consumed by TRANSFER-EVENT is no longer bridge-owned and cannot be destroyed through its former wrapper.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge unique ownership of supported wxEvent instances (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/destroy-event-handler" :names ("destroy-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Destroy an owned standalone native handler. Outside callbacks deletion is immediate; during callbacks identity becomes invalid immediately and deletion is queued on the application after the current native dispatch stack. Repeated destruction is an error. Window and application identities are borrowed and reject this operation; use DESTROY-WINDOW for windows. Only session cleanup destroys the application. Destroying a linked standalone handler during a callback now rejects; outside callbacks native destruction splices reciprocal neighbors. Unlinked callback destruction retains existing deferral. Attached handlers are removed from their managed window before outside-callback deletion; linked/attached callback destruction rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:destroy-event-handler handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is an owned standalone EVENT-HANDLER.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after successful native deletion.")) ("Description" (:p "Destroy an owned standalone native handler. Outside callbacks deletion is immediate; during callbacks identity becomes invalid immediately and deletion is queued on the application after the current native dispatch stack. Repeated destruction is an error. Window and application identities are borrowed and reject this operation; use DESTROY-WINDOW for windows. Only session cleanup destroys the application. Destroying a linked standalone handler during a callback now rejects; outside callbacks native destruction splices reciprocal neighbors. Unlinked callback destruction retains existing deferral. Attached handlers are removed from their managed window before outside-callback deletion; linked/attached callback destruction rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR, including after cleanup. Invalid/stale native handles signal NATIVE-ERROR except HANDLER-ALIVE-P, which returns NIL for destroyed/unknown IDs during an active session. Unsupported Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Generic observer/contextual bindings cover built-ins and registered command/notify names, including on the borrowed application view. Arbitrary native classes, validated OS session delivery, pushed handler chains and native virtual overrides remain unbound. Explicit destruction removes the canonical standalone wrapper root after successful native request.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::~wxEvtHandler (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline), owned standalone handlers only."))))
(:entry "api/destroy-image" :names ("destroy-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Release native session-owned image; stale/double disposal rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:destroy-image object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image")) ("Returns" (:p "IMAGE.")) ("Description" (:p "Release native session-owned image; stale/double disposal rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/destroy-menu-resource" :names ("destroy-menu-resource") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Delete a resource through its native owner, invalidating descendants and wrapper handles. Menu/bar deletion removes it from its parent; frame lifetime also cleans remaining descendants. Structural callback/pump/RUN deletion rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:destroy-menu-resource resource)")) ("Arguments" (:p "RESOURCE is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "T on successful explicit destruction.")) ("Description" (:p "Delete a resource through its native owner, invalidating descendants and wrapper handles. Menu/bar deletion removes it from its parent; frame lifetime also cleans remaining descendants. Structural callback/pump/RUN deletion rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxFrame::SetMenuBar / wxMenuBar::Remove / wxMenu::Destroy and destructors"))))
(:entry "api/destroy-window" :names ("destroy-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request destruction; first explicitly unbind handlers to release Lisp closures. Child handles become invalid when native destruction occurs. During native-to-Lisp callbacks the target becomes invalid immediately and native destruction is deferred using application CallAfter so dispatch/setter stacks can return safely. Generic bindings are reaped at Lisp boundaries; control-specific closures still require explicit unbinding or session cleanup." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:destroy-window window)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after the destruction request.")) ("Description" (:p "Request destruction; first explicitly unbind handlers to release Lisp closures. Child handles become invalid when native destruction occurs. During native-to-Lisp callbacks the target becomes invalid immediately and native destruction is deferred using application CallAfter so dispatch/setter stacks can return safely. Generic bindings are reaped at Lisp boundaries; control-specific closures still require explicit unbinding or session cleanup.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR. The active modal dialog and all its ancestors cannot be destroyed until SHOW-MODAL returns, even after END-MODAL reports native nonmodal state. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Destroy"))))
(:entry "api/dialog" :names ("dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Shared bounded modal protocol and ordinary managed window lifetime." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:dialog")) ("Arguments" (:p "Abstract WINDOW subclass, base of supported TEXT-ENTRY-DIALOG, SINGLE-CHOICE-DIALOG, MESSAGE-DIALOG and FILE-DIALOG.")) ("Returns" (:p "No direct construction.")) ("Description" (:p "Shared bounded modal protocol and ordinary managed window lifetime.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice/generic-message/generic-file scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides. Native validity includes the receiver and all native ancestors: bridge pending-destruction markers and the public wxApp scheduled-deletion list reject use even before IsBeingDeleted becomes true. SHOW-MODAL preflight must not enter a loop beneath an ancestor already queued for deletion.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDialog modal base; no general wxDialog constructor.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:dialog) ; signals an error") (:p "Abstract class; direct construction rejects before native allocation. Use exactly one supported concrete dialog family; unsupported/mixed managed ancestry rejects."))))
(:entry "api/dialog-message" :names ("dialog-message") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read immutable message body. Title is separately mutable through DIALOG-TITLE; no message-body writer in this slice." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:dialog-message dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is a live MESSAGE-DIALOG.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native message body string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read immutable message body. Title is separately mutable through DIALOG-TITLE; no message-body writer in this slice.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMessageDialogBase::GetMessage on wxGenericMessageDialog"))))
(:entry "api/dialog-modal-p" :names ("dialog-modal-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native modal state. False after END-MODAL is not permission to destroy the dialog/ancestor before SHOW-MODAL returns." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:dialog-modal-p dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native IsModal as T/NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native modal state. False after END-MODAL is not permission to destroy the dialog/ancestor before SHOW-MODAL returns.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice/generic-message/generic-file scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDialog::IsModal"))))
(:entry "api/dialog-selection" :names ("dialog-selection" "(setf dialog-selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write the single-choice selection index; NIL and out-of-range values reject. No item-list replacement API is added." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:dialog-selection dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is live. Receiver is SINGLE-CHOICE-DIALOG; VALUE is an integer from 0 through item count minus one.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native selected integer index.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write the single-choice selection index; NIL and out-of-range values reject. No item-list replacement API is added.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSingleChoiceDialog::GetSelection / SetSelection")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:dialog-selection dialog) value)") (:p "Select an existing index and return VALUE."))))
(:entry "api/dialog-selection-text" :names ("dialog-selection-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the last accepted native selection-string cache, not a string derived from the current selected index. SetSelection changes the index but GetStringSelection can remain empty until an actual OK-button transfer; a previous accepted cache can remain after index changes or raw END-MODAL. No cache synchronization is promised." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:dialog-selection-text dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is a live SINGLE-CHOICE-DIALOG.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native GetStringSelection string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the last accepted native selection-string cache, not a string derived from the current selected index. SetSelection changes the index but GetStringSelection can remain empty until an actual OK-button transfer; a previous accepted cache can remain after index changes or raw END-MODAL. No cache synchronization is promised.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSingleChoiceDialog::GetStringSelection"))))
(:entry "api/dialog-title" :names ("dialog-title" "(setf dialog-title)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write native dialog title; scalar callback updates are allowed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:dialog-title dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is live. VALUE is a Unicode string without NUL, possibly empty.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native title string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write native dialog title; scalar callback updates are allowed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice/generic-message/generic-file scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTopLevelWindow::GetTitle / SetTitle")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:dialog-title dialog) value)") (:p "Assign native title and return VALUE."))))
(:entry "api/dialog-value" :names ("dialog-value" "(setf dialog-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write native text-entry dialog value. Native GetValue is stored dialog data and need not expose live edit-buffer changes. SETF crosses the notifying callback boundary; callback conditions follow the existing Lisp condition protocol." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:dialog-value dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is live. Receiver is TEXT-ENTRY-DIALOG; VALUE is a Unicode string without NUL, possibly empty.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native stored value string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write native text-entry dialog value. Native GetValue is stored dialog data and need not expose live edit-buffer changes. SETF crosses the notifying callback boundary; callback conditions follow the existing Lisp condition protocol.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTextEntryDialog::GetValue / SetValue")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:dialog-value dialog) value)") (:p "Assign native stored value and return VALUE; no promise of OK-button validation/data transfer."))))
(:entry "api/disable-grid-cell-edit-control" :names ("disable-grid-cell-edit-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:disable-grid-cell-edit-control grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::DisableCellEditControl"))))
(:entry "api/display-count" :names ("display-count") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxDisplay GetCount on the GUI thread." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:display-count )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "Current nonnegative native display count.")) ("Description" (:p "Query wxDisplay GetCount on the GUI thread.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/display-geometry" :names ("display-geometry") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxDisplay GetGeometry, or GetClientArea with CLIENT-P; zero-based transient display index, possibly negative origins." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:display-geometry index &key client-p)")) ("Arguments" (:p "index &key client-p")) ("Returns" (:p "(x y width height) in native screen units.")) ("Description" (:p "Query wxDisplay GetGeometry, or GetClientArea with CLIENT-P; zero-based transient display index, possibly negative origins.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/display-ppi" :names ("display-ppi") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxDisplay GetPPI for a current display index." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:display-ppi index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "index")) ("Returns" (:p "(horizontal vertical) native PPI.")) ("Description" (:p "Query wxDisplay GetPPI for a current display index.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/display-scale-factor" :names ("display-scale-factor") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxDisplay GetScaleFactor." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:display-scale-factor index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "index")) ("Returns" (:p "Native double-float scale.")) ("Description" (:p "Query wxDisplay GetScaleFactor.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/drawing-canvas" :names ("drawing-canvas") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Retained drawing window for copied geometry, RGB colours, single-line text/font sizes and RGB bitmap values. Native paint/resize handlers render without calling Lisp; Lisp ancestry is WINDOW rather than PANEL." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:drawing-canvas")) ("Arguments" (:p "Required :parent WINDOW; :content defaults (:background (255 255 255) :items NIL), plus subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed DRAWING-CANVAS WINDOW subtype backed by a private wxPanel.")) ("Description" (:p "Retained drawing window for copied geometry, RGB colours, single-line text/font sizes and RGB bitmap values. Native paint/resize handlers render without calling Lisp; Lisp ancestry is WINDOW rather than PANEL.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session, live managed DRAWING-CANVAS, no DC/native object adoption or Lisp paint callback. Native scene staging, rendering/export and Input lifetime/reentry guards; writes/export reject event callbacks. Copied bounded data only; font/paint/DPI appearance is native. See docs/DRAWING-CANVAS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Private wxPanel subclass, wxAutoBufferedPaintDC, wxDC drawing/value adapters; wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:drawing-canvas :parent parent :content '(:background (255 255 255) :items nil))") (:p "Native-backed subclasses/default initargs and properties in AFTER hooks; validated one-concrete-kind ancestry and managed initialization/root rollback."))))
(:entry "api/drop-stc-selection" :names ("drop-stc-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native GetSelections, DropSelectionN. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:drop-stc-selection control index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; INDEX native selection.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native GetSelections, DropSelectionN. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/empty-stc-undo-buffer" :names ("empty-stc-undo-buffer") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native EmptyUndoBuffer. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:empty-stc-undo-buffer control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native EmptyUndoBuffer. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/enable-grid-cell-edit-control" :names ("enable-grid-cell-edit-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:enable-grid-cell-edit-control grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::EnableCellEditControl"))))
(:entry "api/enable-window" :names ("enable-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Enable or disable user input. Repeated requests are harmless; a disabled parent also disables its children effectively." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:enable-window window &optional (enable t))")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is live; optional ENABLE is a generalized boolean (default T).")) ("Returns" (:p "WINDOW, then a boolean indicating whether its native enabled state changed.")) ("Description" (:p "Enable or disable user input. Repeated requests are harmless; a disabled parent also disables its children effectively.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Enable(bool) / Disable() equivalent (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/enabled-p" :names ("enabled-p" "(setf enabled-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read effective enabled state, including disabled ancestors. A child's own disabled state survives parent disable/re-enable. Menu item access reads its native item flag, without an ancestor-window interpretation; separators reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:enabled-p item)")) ("Arguments" (:p "RECEIVER is a live window or MENU-ITEM.")) ("Returns" (:p "T or NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Read effective enabled state, including disabled ancestors. A child's own disabled state survives parent disable/re-enable. Menu item access reads its native item flag, without an ancestor-window interpretation; separators reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::IsEnabled (wxWidgets 3.2). wxMenuItem::IsEnabled / Enable.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:enabled-p window) new-value)") (:p "Assign the input-enabled state; return the supplied value and a second native changed-state flag. Writers are generic functions with VALUE first, followed by the receiver. Menu items support scalar callback-time changes and return VALUE plus whether their native flag changed; separators reject."))))
(:entry "api/end-modal" :names ("end-modal") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Call raw native EndModal with the selected result. This is not an OK-button click: it does not invoke button validation or native data transfer. Native IsModal can become false before SHOW-MODAL returns; the active modal lifetime guard remains until that call unwinds. Generic internal prompt cancellation unwinds internal-to-outer sequentially. Raw :OK does not enforce file must-exist/overwrite checks; actual native OK-button behavior handles configured validation. While an internal prompt is active, successful completion of the public outer dialog (:OK/:YES/:NO) rejects; only :CANCEL requests sequential unwind of the entire workflow." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:end-modal dialog result)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is the active managed public modal dialog; RESULT is :OK/:CANCEL or offered :YES/:NO for MESSAGE-DIALOG.")) ("Returns" (:p "DIALOG after a successful native completion request.")) ("Description" (:p "Call raw native EndModal with the selected result. This is not an OK-button click: it does not invoke button validation or native data transfer. Native IsModal can become false before SHOW-MODAL returns; the active modal lifetime guard remains until that call unwinds. Generic internal prompt cancellation unwinds internal-to-outer sequentially. Raw :OK does not enforce file must-exist/overwrite checks; actual native OK-button behavior handles configured validation. While an internal prompt is active, successful completion of the public outer dialog (:OK/:YES/:NO) rejects; only :CANCEL requests sequential unwind of the entire workflow.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice/generic-message/generic-file scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDialog::EndModal (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/end-stc-undo-action" :names ("end-stc-undo-action") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native EndUndoAction. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:end-stc-undo-action control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native EndUndoAction. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/ensure-stc-caret-visible" :names ("ensure-stc-caret-visible") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native EnsureCaretVisible. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:ensure-stc-caret-visible control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native EnsureCaretVisible. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/ensure-stc-line-visible" :names ("ensure-stc-line-visible") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native EnsureVisible. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:ensure-stc-line-visible control line)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; LINE native line.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native EnsureVisible. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event" :names ("event") :kind :type :kind-name "Type" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read-only event snapshot: kind, receiving source handler/control, native event ID and process-local native type, copied text, checked state and selection. Data survives later callbacks and source destruction. Close snapshots capture CanVeto and GetVeto before this callback; they never reflect later context mutation. Registered names and family/integer data remain available in saved snapshots after session cleanup. Notify snapshots capture pre-callback veto capability/state independently of later Veto/Allow. Timestamp and native IsCommandEvent are copied before each callback; saved reads need no active session. Snapshot EVENT-USER-DATA captures the per-binding EQ Lisp reference before callback, independently of later unbinding. Mutable referent contents are not copied/frozen." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:event")) ("Arguments" (:p "Snapshot type created by callbacks, without a public constructor.")) ("Returns" (:p "Lisp-owned event value.")) ("Description" (:p "Read-only event snapshot: kind, receiving source handler/control, native event ID and process-local native type, copied text, checked state and selection. Data survives later callbacks and source destruction. Close snapshots capture CanVeto and GetVeto before this callback; they never reflect later context mutation. Registered names and family/integer data remain available in saved snapshots after session cleanup. Notify snapshots capture pre-callback veto capability/state independently of later Veto/Allow. Timestamp and native IsCommandEvent are copied before each callback; saved reads need no active session. Snapshot EVENT-USER-DATA captures the per-binding EQ Lisp reference before callback, independently of later unbinding. Mutable referent contents are not copied/frozen.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Use only the exported predicate/accessors; native event objects do not escape callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent snapshot."))))
(:entry "api/event-alive-p" :names ("event-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query the independent owned-event registry. Failed/uninitialized wrappers have no native handle and signal NATIVE-ERROR. This is not context activity or native origin liveness. TRANSFER-EVENT consumes the source registry handle; queued copies from POST-EVENT/QUEUE-EVENT do not." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-alive-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an OWNED-EVENT wrapper.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for a live native owned resource; NIL for explicitly destroyed or transferred IDs during the active session.")) ("Description" (:p "Query the independent owned-event registry. Failed/uninitialized wrappers have no native handle and signal NATIVE-ERROR. This is not context activity or native origin liveness. TRANSFER-EVENT consumes the source registry handle; queued copies from POST-EVENT/QUEUE-EVENT do not.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required, including for dead-ID queries. After session cleanup native access signals NATIVE-ERROR. No GC finalization or cross-session reuse.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge-owned wxEvent registry predicate (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-aui-page-id" :names ("event-aui-page-id") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Captured numeric bridge target-page identity; CLOSED uses target captured during full native close span, never a shifted current index lookup. No wrapper adoption/resurrection." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-aui-page-id event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable snapshot or current innermost AUI event context.")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive ID or NIL if unavailable/unrelated snapshot.")) ("Description" (:p "Captured numeric bridge target-page identity; CLOSED uses target captured during full native close span, never a shifted current index lookup. No wrapper adoption/resurrection.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Snapshot reads survive native/session cleanup. Context reads require active main-thread session and exact innermost current AUI callback; unrelated/stale contexts reject. No writer. Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebookEvent/wxBookCtrlEvent, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-auto-repeat-p" :names ("event-auto-repeat-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native repeat boolean; availability varies by port." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-auto-repeat-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native repeat boolean; availability varies by port.")) ("Description" (:p "Native repeat boolean; availability varies by port.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-binding" :names ("event-binding") :kind :type :kind-name "Type" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Keep the returned object to query or remove exactly this registration. A binding records its receiving Lisp object and kind but not the callback function; active callback roots are held by the session registry. Native registration is session-scoped." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:event-binding")) ("Arguments" (:p "Opaque read-only structure returned by BIND-EVENT; no public constructor.")) ("Returns" (:p "An independent binding identity.")) ("Description" (:p "Keep the returned object to query or remove exactly this registration. A binding records its receiving Lisp object and kind but not the callback function; active callback roots are held by the session registry. Native registration is session-scoped.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR. Stale/deleting receivers reject registration/queuing. Invalid event kinds, IDs and payload options signal Lisp errors; wrong receiver types use CLOS dispatch errors. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Contexts support scoped Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto. Arbitrary native events, native control-specific notify subclasses, arbitrary native userData pointers, external handler adoption and worker-thread dispatch remain unbound.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge identity for wxEvtHandler::Bind/Unbind (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-binding-p" :names ("event-binding-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Type predicate only; does not query native registration and needs no active session." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-binding-p object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "OBJECT is any Lisp value.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for EVENT-BINDING structures, NIL otherwise.")) ("Description" (:p "Type predicate only; does not query native registration and needs no active session.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "No native session required. This predicate says nothing about whether a binding remains active.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Lisp-only binding identity predicate."))))
(:entry "api/event-can-veto-p" :names ("event-can-veto-p" "(setf event-can-veto-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Snapshots read copied capability without a session. Current close contexts use CanVeto; current notify contexts always support Veto/Allow. Plain command contexts return NIL. Scope validation remains required for native access. Context SETF maps native SetCanVeto directly, including false to true. GetVeto hides a stored veto when CanVeto is false and reveals it again if re-enabled. Forced close starts false but explicit metadata mutation can affect native closing results; OS veto acceptance is not guaranteed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-can-veto-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a saved snapshot or current event context. SETF requires a current close-family context; VALUE is a generalized boolean. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for veto-capable captured/current close or notify events; NIL otherwise.")) ("Description" (:p "Snapshots read copied capability without a session. Current close contexts use CanVeto; current notify contexts always support Veto/Allow. Plain command contexts return NIL. Scope validation remains required for native access. Context SETF maps native SetCanVeto directly, including false to true. GetVeto hides a stored veto when CanVeto is false and reveals it again if re-enabled. Forced close starts false but explicit metadata mutation can affect native closing results; OS veto acceptance is not guaranteed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required for native context or frame operations. Expired/suspended contexts and invalid/deleting frames signal NATIVE-ERROR. Saved snapshots need no session. Close and registered notify families permit checked veto. Other native control-specific notify subclasses, validated OS session delivery and arbitrary event classes remain open. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCloseEvent::CanVeto / SetCanVeto; intrinsic wxNotifyEvent capability is read-only (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-can-veto-p event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign current wxCloseEvent capability, returning VALUE. Snapshot, command and notify writers reject; stale/suspended contexts reject native access. Does not clear the native stored veto bit or guarantee OS policy. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-category" :names ("event-category") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read virtual GetEventCategory: current supported command/notify-derived classes report USER_INPUT and close/idle-family events report UI. Values are category flags, not event types/IDs/families; synthetic USER_INPUT is not proof of real user input. Snapshot values are captured before the callback." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-category context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot or current innermost event context. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "Captured/current native wxEventCategory integer flags.")) ("Description" (:p "Read virtual GetEventCategory: current supported command/notify-derived classes report USER_INPUT and close/idle-family events report UI. Values are category flags, not event types/IDs/families; synthetic USER_INPUT is not proof of real user input. Snapshot values are captured before the callback.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshots need no native session. Context reads require active main-thread session and innermost callback; stale/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. No category setter, native virtual override, selective YieldFor or socket/timer/thread event binding is supplied. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetEventCategory; native wxCommandEvent override includes notify-derived events (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-category-mask" :names ("event-category-mask") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Load the bridge and return its compiled wxEventCategory constant without initializing a GUI session. Combine with LOGIOR/test with LOGTEST. ALL can include implementation category bits and is not restricted to the public five-bit union." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-category-mask category)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CATEGORY is :UI, :USER-INPUT, :SOCKET, :TIMER, :THREAD or :ALL.")) ("Returns" (:p "Compiled native category bit/mask integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Load the bridge and return its compiled wxEventCategory constant without initializing a GUI session. Combine with LOGIOR/test with LOGTEST. ALL can include implementation category bits and is not restricted to the public five-bit union.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "No active GUI session required; normal native library/ABI load errors apply. Unknown names signal a Lisp error before FFI. No event pumping or event-family construction. Pinned interface ALL31 differs from local3.2.12 compiled ALL127; preserve actual compiled value.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEVT_CATEGORY_UI, USER_INPUT, SOCKET, TIMER, THREAD and ALL (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-checked-p" :names ("event-checked-p" "(setf event-checked-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the kind-limited checked interpretation of native command integer. Live SETF writes SetInt(0/1) only for :TOGGLE/:MENU without calling a control setter. Raw EVENT-INTEGER can supply other nonzero checked values; earlier snapshots stay unchanged. Later native/user handlers can react to changed metadata; the entire dispatch is not guaranteed to leave controls unchanged. Native normal-menu commands may carry integer -1 and thus read checked true; this raw view does not classify a check item. :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE exposes read-only semantic checked metadata; raw integer edits remain observational, not control state changes." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-checked-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT. Reads interpret :TOGGLE/:MENU/:TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE; SETF only :TOGGLE/:MENU.")) ("Returns" (:p "T/NIL for checkbox/toggle-button/menu checked metadata; NIL for other kinds. SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the kind-limited checked interpretation of native command integer. Live SETF writes SetInt(0/1) only for :TOGGLE/:MENU without calling a control setter. Raw EVENT-INTEGER can supply other nonzero checked values; earlier snapshots stay unchanged. Later native/user handlers can react to changed metadata; the entire dispatch is not guaranteed to leave controls unchanged. Native normal-menu commands may carry integer -1 and thus read checked true; this raw view does not classify a check item. :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE exposes read-only semantic checked metadata; raw integer edits remain observational, not control state changes.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshot reads need no session. Live operations require active main-thread session and valid owned/innermost-context lifetime. Wrong-kind live writes reject; no snapshot writer or direct checkbox-control setter.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::IsChecked for wxEVT_CHECKBOX/wxEVT_MENU/wxEVT_TOGGLEBUTTON; semantic SetInt writer only checkbox/menu kinds (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-checked-p event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign native :TOGGLE/:MENU command integer as 0/1, returning the supplied generalized boolean. No snapshot writer or menu-resource synchronization; no item-kind check is implied by raw event metadata. Toggle-button kinds reject; no owned/synthetic/cloned toggle-button events."))))
(:entry "api/event-cmd-down-p" :names ("event-cmd-down-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy wxKeyboardState::CmdDown from native key/mouse input. Distinguishes native Command semantics and physical Control on macOS." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-cmd-down-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Key/mouse EVENT snapshot or current innermost EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native boolean state.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy wxKeyboardState::CmdDown from native key/mouse input. Distinguishes native Command semantics and physical Control on macOS.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Read-only copied input payload. Wrong kinds and expired/outside-innermost contexts reject. No synthetic/owned/cloned input events; no platform flag inference. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyboardState::CmdDown, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-command-p" :names ("event-command-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read captured/current native IsCommandEvent classification. No mutable classification or event replacement. Saved values remain independent of source lifetime." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-command-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot or current event context. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for native command/notify-derived events; NIL for close/idle-family events.")) ("Description" (:p "Read captured/current native IsCommandEvent classification. No mutable classification or event replacement. Saved values remain independent of source lifetime.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshots need no session. Current-context access requires an active main-thread session and the innermost callback; stale/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. No SETF writer. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::IsCommandEvent copied or borrowed (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-context" :names ("event-context") :kind :type :kind-name "Type" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "The context token is immutable; operations mutate the live native event only during its exact innermost callback. Nested contextual callbacks suspend outer access; nested observer/control callbacks also deny outer access. The outer context becomes usable again after nesting returns. Unbinding or deferred receiver disposal does not prematurely expire the running callback context. :CLOSE contexts allow checked veto access; command contexts do not have close-veto state." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:event-context")) ("Arguments" (:p "Opaque read-only token value passed as the second argument by BIND-EVENT :WITH-CONTEXT T. No public constructor.")) ("Returns" (:p "A borrowed callback-scoped native wxEvent view.")) ("Description" (:p "The context token is immutable; operations mutate the live native event only during its exact innermost callback. Nested contextual callbacks suspend outer access; nested observer/control callbacks also deny outer access. The outer context becomes usable again after nesting returns. Unbinding or deferred receiver disposal does not prematurely expire the running callback context. :CLOSE contexts allow checked veto access; command contexts do not have close-veto state.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread session and the innermost currently executing contextual callback. Expired or outer contexts in nested callbacks signal NATIVE-ERROR for native access. Activity queries return NIL for those contexts during a session; outside a session they signal NATIVE-ERROR. No raw native event pointer escapes. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Veto applies only to actual wxCloseEvent/wxNotifyEvent contexts; arbitrary event types, general event construction/cloning and native control-specific subclasses and validated OS session delivery remains open.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Borrowed wxEvent base view, four wxCommandEvent tags (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-context-active-p" :names ("event-context-active-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Check scoped usability without dereferencing an expired pointer. Observer/control callbacks do not gain access to an enclosing context. The predicate does not assert receiver liveness and remains T during deferred receiver disposal until callback return." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-context-active-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTEXT is an EVENT-CONTEXT value.")) ("Returns" (:p "T only for the current innermost native callback context; NIL for expired/suspended contexts in an active session.")) ("Description" (:p "Check scoped usability without dereferencing an expired pointer. Observer/control callbacks do not gain access to an enclosing context. The predicate does not assert receiver liveness and remains T during deferred receiver disposal until callback return.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread session and the innermost currently executing contextual callback. Expired or outer contexts in nested callbacks signal NATIVE-ERROR for native access. Activity queries return NIL for those contexts during a session; outside a session they signal NATIVE-ERROR. No raw native event pointer escapes. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Veto applies only to actual wxCloseEvent/wxNotifyEvent contexts; arbitrary event types, general event construction/cloning and native control-specific subclasses and validated OS session delivery remains open.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge scope/depth validation of borrowed wxEvent access."))))
(:entry "api/event-context-p" :names ("event-context-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Type predicate only; a saved expired context still satisfies it. No native access or active session is needed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-context-p object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "OBJECT is any Lisp value.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for EVENT-CONTEXT values, NIL otherwise.")) ("Description" (:p "Type predicate only; a saved expired context still satisfies it. No native access or active session is needed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "No active native session required. Use EVENT-CONTEXT-ACTIVE-P for current callback usability.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Lisp-only context type predicate."))))
(:entry "api/event-date" :names ("event-date") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read captured or current native wxDateEvent date payload, independent of current picker value. Non-date contexts reject; snapshots survive callback/session. No writer, synthetic/owned events or detached clones." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-date event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh supported (year month day) date tuple, or NIL for non-date snapshots or invalid/out-of-scope native date payloads.")) ("Description" (:p "Read captured or current native wxDateEvent date payload, independent of current picker value. Non-date contexts reject; snapshots survive callback/session. No writer, synthetic/owned events or detached clones.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Native :date-change command family only. Context lifetime isolation applies; snapshot raw text/integer metadata is not a date encoding. Time-change uses separate EVENT-TIME metadata; calendar event families remain unbound. See docs/DATE-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDateEvent::GetDate and wxEVT_DATE_CHANGED, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-dragging-p" :names ("event-dragging-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native dragging boolean, not a mouse-capture guarantee." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-dragging-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native dragging boolean, not a mouse-capture guarantee.")) ("Description" (:p "Native dragging boolean, not a mouse-capture guarantee.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-extra-long" :names ("event-extra-long" "(setf event-extra-long)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read GetExtraLong or set native command/notify extra metadata. It is separate from signed32 EVENT-INTEGER and item indices. Raw EVENT-SELECTION-P reflects whether this field is nonzero. Snapshots preserve pre-callback values." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-extra-long event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT. SETF VALUE must fit signed native C LONG for command/notify events.")) ("Returns" (:p "Captured/current extra LONG integer; zero for close/idle-family reads. SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read GetExtraLong or set native command/notify extra metadata. It is separate from signed32 EVENT-INTEGER and item indices. Raw EVENT-SELECTION-P reflects whether this field is nonzero. Snapshots preserve pre-callback values.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved reads need no session; live access requires active main-thread session and valid owned/innermost-context lifetime. Close-family writes reject. Native LONG width/range are platform dependent; no snapshot writer or derived-control state update. Non-integer/out-of-range values signal TYPE-ERROR. WEB-VIEW :WEB-MESSAGE/:WEB-SCRIPT-RESULT/:WEB-LOADED/:WEB-ERROR payload contexts are read-only: text/integer/extra-LONG SETF reject. Script results carry JSON or error text, success1/error0 in EVENT-INTEGER and ticket in EVENT-EXTRA-LONG; messages carry JSON without sender authentication. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md. ABI57 raw key/mouse/focus/context-menu/size, STC and AUI native kinds have copied read-only payload metadata and reject owned/synthetic construction/cloning. Ordinary observers automatically Skip; scoped handlers explicitly Skip unhandled native input. STC styling has the exact innermost same-control STYLENEEDED StartStyling/SetStyling exception. AUI close/changing veto is native-scoped and CLOSED has former index/captured target ID. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md, docs/STYLED-TEXT.md and docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::GetExtraLong / SetExtraLong, including notify-derived events (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-extra-long event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign signed native LONG extra metadata and return VALUE. Changes raw IsSelection but not kind/index/control state. Close-family and snapshot writes reject."))))
(:entry "api/event-family" :names ("event-family") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read captured/current supported native classification :COMMAND/:NOTIFY/:CLOSE/:IDLE, including owned event values and saved snapshots after registry cleanup. It is bounded class metadata, not arbitrary native RTTI." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-family event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p "The portable family keyword :COMMAND, :CLOSE, :NOTIFY or :IDLE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read captured/current supported native classification :COMMAND/:NOTIFY/:CLOSE/:IDLE, including owned event values and saved snapshots after registry cleanup. It is bounded class metadata, not arbitrary native RTTI.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshots need no session. Owned/current reads require active main-thread session and valid native lifetime; contexts require the innermost callback. ABI58 :THREAD is a native base-family wxThreadEvent with copied immutable EVENT-TEXT, GUI-only callback dispatch and normal context lifetime. QUEUE-THREAD-EVENT alone permits worker posting after GUI binding; other GUI operations retain their thread rules. No owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Portable classification of supported wxCommandEvent/wxNotifyEvent/wxCloseEvent/wxIdleEvent classes (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-cell-value" :names ("event-grid-cell-value") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied current table string on CHANGING/CHANGED only, or NIL for invalid native cell. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-cell-value event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied copied current table string on CHANGING/CHANGED only, or NIL for invalid native cell.")) ("Description" (:p "Read copied current table string on CHANGING/CHANGED only, or NIL for invalid native cell. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-column" :names ("event-grid-column") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read column on non-range cell events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-column event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied column on non-range cell events.")) ("Description" (:p "Read column on non-range cell events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-modifiers" :names ("event-grid-modifiers") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native modifier bit mask. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-modifiers event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied native modifier bit mask.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native modifier bit mask. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-position" :names ("event-grid-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read fresh client (x y), or NIL for (-1 -1), on cell events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-position event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied fresh client (x y), or NIL for (-1 -1), on cell events.")) ("Description" (:p "Read fresh client (x y), or NIL for (-1 -1), on cell events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-range" :names ("event-grid-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read fresh (top left bottom right) on range events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-range event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied fresh (top left bottom right) on range events.")) ("Description" (:p "Read fresh (top left bottom right) on range events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-row" :names ("event-grid-row") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read row on non-range cell events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-row event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied row on non-range cell events.")) ("Description" (:p "Read row on non-range cell events. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-grid-selecting-p" :names ("event-grid-selecting-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native Selecting flag. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-grid-selecting-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied native Selecting flag.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native Selecting flag. Kind mismatch signals. Cell-value snapshot copied before user callback; contexts read during callback. EVENT-TEXT separately preserves proposed CHANGING/old CHANGED GetString.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridEvent / wxGridRangeSelectEvent metadata"))))
(:entry "api/event-handler" :names ("event-handler") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Concrete standalone wxEvtHandler wrapper and superclass of WINDOW. Standalone native objects are owned by the application session, explicitly destroyed or automatically freed at session cleanup, without a Lisp GC finalizer. Windows borrow their own native wxWindow base identity and retain window/parent lifetime. Neither case exposes an arbitrary GetEventHandler chain or permits user-supplied native handles. Standalone wrappers are now strongly canonicalized by session identity for EQ chain peer lookup; no new native ownership or finalizer is introduced. Managed window push leaves native ownership/session rooting unchanged; window destruction detaches handlers rather than deleting them." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:event-handler")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass STANDARD-OBJECT. No native initargs; subclasses may add slot initargs and defaults.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed owned standalone handler, or the base identity of an existing window subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Concrete standalone wxEvtHandler wrapper and superclass of WINDOW. Standalone native objects are owned by the application session, explicitly destroyed or automatically freed at session cleanup, without a Lisp GC finalizer. Windows borrow their own native wxWindow base identity and retain window/parent lifetime. Neither case exposes an arbitrary GetEventHandler chain or permits user-supplied native handles. Standalone wrappers are now strongly canonicalized by session identity for EQ chain peer lookup; no new native ownership or finalizer is introduced. Managed window push leaves native ownership/session rooting unchanged; window destruction detaches handlers rather than deleting them.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR, including after cleanup. Invalid/stale native handles signal NATIVE-ERROR except HANDLER-ALIVE-P, which returns NIL for destroyed/unknown IDs during an active session. Unsupported Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Generic observer/contextual bindings cover built-ins and registered command/notify names, including on the borrowed application view. Arbitrary native classes, validated OS session delivery, pushed handler chains and native virtual overrides remain unbound. Construction rollback releases created resources/roots but does not undo arbitrary external chain edits; native destruction splices survivors around the failed node.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler constructor/destructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline); window identity uses wxWindow inheritance.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:event-handler)") (:p "Subclass slot initargs and :DEFAULT-INITARGS are forwarded. Native state exists in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed managed initialization rolls back nested handlers/windows and callback roots through the shared construction context. WINDOW stays abstract; concrete windows allocate only their native widget."))))
(:entry "api/event-handler-client-data" :names ("event-handler-client-data" "(setf event-handler-client-data)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Store a session-root token in a bridge wxClientData adapter; the Lisp table retains the actual object. No Lisp pointer, serialization or native ownership of the Lisp object. Replacement/clear releases old association through cleanup; an ordinary returned Lisp reference remains valid. No constructor initarg: native-backed subclass AFTER hooks may SETF." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-handler-client-data handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live managed EVENT-HANDLER, window/control or APPLICATION-HANDLER. SETF VALUE is any Lisp object; NIL clears.")) ("Returns" (:p "The same retained Lisp object by EQ, or NIL for no bridge datum. SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Store a session-root token in a bridge wxClientData adapter; the Lisp table retains the actual object. No Lisp pointer, serialization or native ownership of the Lisp object. Replacement/clear releases old association through cleanup; an ordinary returned Lisp reference remains valid. No constructor initarg: native-backed subclass AFTER hooks may SETF.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and live managed receiver required. Foreign non-null typed objects and all native untyped/Void modes, including NULL-pointer Void slots, reject untouched before typed access. Fresh None/typed-NULL slots read NIL. Roots reap during access/generic cleanup/rollback or after native session finish; asynchronous destruction may retain them until a later boundary. No untyped, event/client/userData, per-item or arbitrary native container binding.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::GetClientObject / SetClientObject with bridge wxClientData token adapter; protected native mode inspection is a private C7 reconciliation dependency (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-handler-client-data handler) value)") (:p "Retain VALUE by EQ or clear for NIL, returning VALUE. Foreign storage rejects without replacement. Candidate Lisp roots roll back on failed native write; old roots release at cleanup. Does not pump events or change native handler ownership."))))
(:entry "api/event-id" :names ("event-id" "(setf event-id)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read a saved pre-callback ID or current native GetId. Context SETF changes event metadata and later native ID matching, not the source window ID or binding filters. Earlier snapshots stay unchanged. No dispatch restart or callback-order guarantee." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-id context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot or current innermost context. SETF VALUE is a signed 32-bit integer, including -1. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "Captured/current native integer ID; SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read a saved pre-callback ID or current native GetId. Context SETF changes event metadata and later native ID matching, not the source window ID or binding filters. Earlier snapshots stay unchanged. No dispatch restart or callback-order guarantee.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshots need no native session. Current reads/writes require an active main-thread session and innermost callback; stale/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. Invalid SETF values signal TYPE-ERROR. Context SetId permits -1; binding filters/synthetic initial IDs still reserve it. Native types/origin mutation remain unbound. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable. Native ABI57 raw input, STC and AUI context IDs/timestamps are read-only; their SETF writers reject.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetId / SetId, signed native int (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-id event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign current native ID and return VALUE. Later exact/range matching uses the changed ID; -1 remains literal event metadata and unfiltered bindings still match. No snapshot writer. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-integer" :names ("event-integer" "(setf event-integer)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read GetInt or change the native command payload with SETF. Built-in toggle/selection interpretations can reflect this underlying value. Earlier snapshots remain unchanged. Raw values can affect semantic checked/selection views; negative indices other than -1 remain visible through EVENT-SELECTION after raw writes. It does not alter EXTRA-LONG or raw IsSelection." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-integer event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT. SETF VALUE is signed32 and requires command/notify state.")) ("Returns" (:p "Captured/current native command integer; zero for close/idle-family reads. SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read GetInt or change the native command payload with SETF. Built-in toggle/selection interpretations can reflect this underlying value. Earlier snapshots remain unchanged. Raw values can affect semantic checked/selection views; negative indices other than -1 remain visible through EVENT-SELECTION after raw writes. It does not alter EXTRA-LONG or raw IsSelection.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved reads need no session. Live access requires active main-thread session and valid owned/innermost-context lifetime. Close-family writes reject; malformed/out-of-range values signal TYPE-ERROR. WEB-VIEW :WEB-MESSAGE/:WEB-SCRIPT-RESULT/:WEB-LOADED/:WEB-ERROR payload contexts are read-only: text/integer/extra-LONG SETF reject. Script results carry JSON or error text, success1/error0 in EVENT-INTEGER and ticket in EVENT-EXTRA-LONG; messages carry JSON without sender authentication. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md. ABI57 raw key/mouse/focus/context-menu/size, STC and AUI native kinds have copied read-only payload metadata and reject owned/synthetic construction/cloning. Ordinary observers automatically Skip; scoped handlers explicitly Skip unhandled native input. STC styling has the exact innermost same-control STYLENEEDED StartStyling/SetStyling exception. AUI close/changing veto is native-scoped and CLOSED has former index/captured target ID. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md, docs/STYLED-TEXT.md and docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::GetInt / SetInt, including wxNotifyEvent (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-integer event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign a signed32 native command/notify payload and return VALUE. No snapshot writer; stale contexts and destroyed resources reject."))))
(:entry "api/event-key-code" :names ("event-key-code") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native wx key code; special codes are not Unicode characters." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-key-code event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native wx key code; special codes are not Unicode characters.")) ("Description" (:p "Native wx key code; special codes are not Unicode characters.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-kind" :names ("event-kind") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the event kind. The captured kind reflects the actual supported native tag at callback entry, even if an earlier callback changed it; binding registration identity does not change." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-kind event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p ":CLICK, :TEXT-CHANGE, :TOGGLE, :SELECTION, :CLOSE, :QUERY-END-SESSION, :END-SESSION, :IDLE, :MENU or a registered command/notify keyword name.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the event kind. The captured kind reflects the actual supported native tag at callback entry, even if an earlier callback changed it; binding registration identity does not change.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshots need no session. Owned/current native reads require the active main-thread session; contexts must be innermost. Registered names expire with the session for native resources; saved copied keywords remain readable. ABI58 :THREAD is a native base-family wxThreadEvent with copied immutable EVENT-TEXT, GUI-only callback dispatch and normal context lifetime. QUEUE-THREAD-EVENT alone permits worker posting after GUI binding; other GUI operations retain their thread rules. No owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Lisp-owned wxCommandEvent snapshot."))))
(:entry "api/event-list-cache-range" :names ("event-list-cache-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh (first last) copied native cache-hint range; no guarantee of provider call order or fixed cache size." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-list-cache-range event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(event-or-context)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Fresh (first last) copied native cache-hint range; no guarantee of provider call order or fixed cache size.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListEvent::GetCacheFrom / GetCacheTo"))))
(:entry "api/event-list-column" :names ("event-list-column") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native column for list-column-click only, negative sentinel NIL. No inference for other list events." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-list-column event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(event-or-context)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Native column for list-column-click only, negative sentinel NIL. No inference for other list events.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListEvent::GetColumn"))))
(:entry "api/event-list-index" :names ("event-list-index") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native row for selected/deselected/activated/right-click only; negative sentinel returns NIL. Snapshot copied; context innermost only." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-list-index event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(event-or-context)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Native row for selected/deselected/activated/right-click only; negative sentinel returns NIL. Snapshot copied; context innermost only.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListEvent::GetIndex"))))
(:entry "api/event-list-position" :names ("event-list-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh (x y) copied native item-right-click point; native coordinate conventions apply." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-list-position event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(event-or-context)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Fresh (x y) copied native item-right-click point; native coordinate conventions apply.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListEvent::GetPoint"))))
(:entry "api/event-logging-off-p" :names ("event-logging-off-p" "(setf event-logging-off-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied or current wxCloseEvent logging-off metadata for :QUERY-END-SESSION/:END-SESSION. Context SETF changes native metadata only, not OS policy. Snapshots retain pre-callback state and have no SETF method." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-logging-off-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a saved session-event snapshot or current innermost session-event context. SETF VALUE is a generalized boolean. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for logging off, NIL for system shutdown; SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read copied or current wxCloseEvent logging-off metadata for :QUERY-END-SESSION/:END-SESSION. Context SETF changes native metadata only, not OS policy. Snapshots retain pre-callback state and have no SETF method.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved session snapshots require no session. Non-session snapshots signal Lisp errors; non-session, stale or suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. Native access requires an active main-thread session. OS session delivery is not validated by isolated synthetic tests. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCloseEvent::GetLoggingOff / SetLoggingOff (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-logging-off-p event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign the current native session flag, returning the generalized boolean. No snapshot writer; no OS logout/shutdown action is performed. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-modifiers" :names ("event-modifiers") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native wx modifier bits ALT1 CONTROL2 SHIFT4 META8, RAW_CONTROL16 on macOS (aliases CONTROL elsewhere); CONTROL means Command on macOS." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-modifiers event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native wx modifier bits ALT1 CONTROL2 SHIFT4 META8, RAW_CONTROL16 on macOS (aliases CONTROL elsewhere); CONTROL means Command on macOS.")) ("Description" (:p "Native wx modifier bits ALT1 CONTROL2 SHIFT4 META8, RAW_CONTROL16 on macOS (aliases CONTROL elsewhere); CONTROL means Command on macOS.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-more-requested-p" :names ("event-more-requested-p" "(setf event-more-requested-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read idle request-more metadata or call wxIdleEvent::RequestMore with SETF. Earlier snapshots stay unchanged. Bounded idle work may request another native idle pass; this is not a busy-loop, timer or immediate-delivery guarantee." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-more-requested-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT. SETF requires live idle state and accepts a generalized boolean.")) ("Returns" (:p "Captured/current/owned MoreRequested as T/NIL; NIL on non-idle families. SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read idle request-more metadata or call wxIdleEvent::RequestMore with SETF. Earlier snapshots stay unchanged. Bounded idle work may request another native idle pass; this is not a busy-loop, timer or immediate-delivery guarantee.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved reads need no session. Live access requires active main-thread session and valid owned/innermost-context lifetime. Non-idle writes and snapshot writers reject. Synthetic dispatch does not establish automatic native idle scheduling.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxIdleEvent::MoreRequested / RequestMore (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-more-requested-p event-or-context) value)") (:p "Set a live idle request-more flag and return the generalized boolean. Bound work and clear when finished; no non-idle/snapshot writer or inline pump."))))
(:entry "api/event-mouse-button" :names ("event-mouse-button") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Triggering :left/:middle/:right/:aux1/:aux2 or NIL." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-mouse-button event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Triggering :left/:middle/:right/:aux1/:aux2 or NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Triggering :left/:middle/:right/:aux1/:aux2 or NIL.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-mouse-buttons" :names ("event-mouse-buttons") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh list of currently held button keywords." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-mouse-buttons event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh list of currently held button keywords.")) ("Description" (:p "Fresh list of currently held button keywords.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-mouse-click-count" :names ("event-mouse-click-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native click count, potentially -1 where unsupported." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-mouse-click-count event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native click count, potentially -1 where unsupported.")) ("Description" (:p "Native click count, potentially -1 where unsupported.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-native-type" :names ("event-native-type" "(setf event-native-type)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied/current GetEventType. Saved values remain data after callback/source/session cleanup. Compare to EVENT-TYPE in the same active session; numeric tags are not stable serialized IDs or native cast authority. Context SETF accepts only registered same-family source/target tags and validates actual native command/notify class before SetEventType. Earlier snapshots and registration identities remain unchanged; later snapshots report the current native tag. No dispatch restart or local delivery-order guarantee." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-native-type context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot or current innermost event context. SETF VALUE is a signed32 native type returned by EVENT-TYPE for a registered name. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "Captured/current process-local native wxEventType integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read copied/current GetEventType. Saved values remain data after callback/source/session cleanup. Compare to EVENT-TYPE in the same active session; numeric tags are not stable serialized IDs or native cast authority. Context SETF accepts only registered same-family source/target tags and validates actual native command/notify class before SetEventType. Earlier snapshots and registration identities remain unchanged; later snapshots report the current native tag. No dispatch restart or local delivery-order guarantee.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshots need no session. Current reads/writes require active main-thread session and innermost callback; stale/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. SETF rejects built-in/session/unknown/cross-family types before mutation. Malformed integers signal TYPE-ERROR. Arbitrary tag mutation, class replacement and native ownership remain unbound. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetEventType / bounded SetEventType for registered same-family tags (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-native-type event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign a registered same-family native type after actual-class checks; return VALUE. Built-in/session sources or targets reject. No snapshot writer, rebind, dispatch restart or local callback-order guarantee. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-next-key-event-allowed-p" :names ("event-next-key-event-allowed-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copied/current CHAR_HOOK allow-next flag; old snapshots remain unchanged." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-next-key-event-allowed-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied/current CHAR_HOOK allow-next flag; old snapshots remain unchanged.")) ("Description" (:p "Copied/current CHAR_HOOK allow-next flag; old snapshots remain unchanged.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-numeric-value" :names ("event-numeric-value") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Numeric EVENT snapshot or current EVENT-CONTEXT." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-numeric-value event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Numeric EVENT snapshot or current EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Integer payload for :slider-change/:spin-change; NIL for unrelated snapshot, NATIVE-ERROR for unrelated context.")) ("Description" (:p "Numeric EVENT snapshot or current EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Immutable copied EVENT snapshots remain readable after source destruction and session cleanup. Borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT requires its innermost current callback and native lifetime checks. Payload metadata is not constrained by the control endpoint bounds. Read-only; spin veto/payload edits are observational and do not write or roll back control state. No owned/synthetic/detached-clone numeric events. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::GetInt / wxSpinEvent integer position payload (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/event-old-selection" :names ("event-old-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native old-selection metadata for AUI events; kind/event-stage meanings are native policy, not a universal prior-active-page contract. For CLOSE this field can be the private group-local tab index; it is not generally the old global active index." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-old-selection event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable snapshot or current innermost AUI event context.")) ("Returns" (:p "Nonnegative integer or NIL for absent/unrelated snapshot.")) ("Description" (:p "Native old-selection metadata for AUI events; kind/event-stage meanings are native policy, not a universal prior-active-page contract. For CLOSE this field can be the private group-local tab index; it is not generally the old global active index.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Snapshot reads survive native/session cleanup. Context reads require active main-thread session and exact innermost current AUI callback; unrelated/stale contexts reject. No writer. Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebookEvent/wxBookCtrlEvent, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-origin-id" :names ("event-origin-id" "(setf event-origin-id)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy/read GetEventObject identity only when it matches a registered application, owned handler, tracked window or managed menu resource. This differs from EVENT-SOURCE (binding receiver) and EVENT-ID (routing metadata). Pointer identity is compared without dereferencing the origin; no native pointer or wrapper reconstruction is exposed. Clear-only live SETF accepts NIL. Owned events are already detached; non-null current origins can clear only for registered command/notify tags matching actual native class. No origin object is retained or destroyed; EVENT-SOURCE and earlier snapshots stay unchanged." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-origin-id event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current innermost context or live OWNED-EVENT. SETF accepts only NIL on live state under the bounded detachment rules.")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive opaque bridge identity, or NIL for null/untracked native origin.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy/read GetEventObject identity only when it matches a registered application, owned handler, tracked window or managed menu resource. This differs from EVENT-SOURCE (binding receiver) and EVENT-ID (routing metadata). Pointer identity is compared without dereferencing the origin; no native pointer or wrapper reconstruction is exposed. Clear-only live SETF accepts NIL. Owned events are already detached; non-null current origins can clear only for registered command/notify tags matching actual native class. No origin object is retained or destroyed; EVENT-SOURCE and earlier snapshots stay unchanged.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved values need no native session and imply no current liveness. Context reads require active main-thread session and innermost callback; expired/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. Null and untracked origins both map to NIL. Registry lookup is at capture/read time, not a historical pointer-lifetime guarantee. No new-origin writer, generic wxObject wrapper, origin retention or native ownership transfer. Live owned-event reads validate the resource and return NIL because every owned event is detached; no new-origin setter/retention protocol is supplied. Non-NIL origin SETF signals TYPE-ERROR after session validation. Actual OS-generated origin identity is not guaranteed; origin can differ from the frame binding receiver.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetEventObject, bounded bridge-identity mapping (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-origin-id event-or-context) nil)") (:p "Drop only the native event-origin pointer. Non-NIL values reject. Actual-null live origins are no-op; non-null contexts require registered compatible command/notify native class. Built-in/nonregistered non-null origins reject. Reader NIL may also mean untracked and does not prove actual-null state."))))
(:entry "api/event-p" :names ("event-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Test whether an object is a Lisp-owned event snapshot." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-p object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "OBJECT is any Lisp value.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for an EVENT, otherwise NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Test whether an object is a Lisp-owned event snapshot.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "No GUI session required.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Lisp snapshot predicate."))))
(:entry "api/event-position" :names ("event-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh (x y) client coordinates for key/mouse, screen coordinates for context-menu, NIL for keyboard context-menu sentinel. Native coordinates, not automatic DIP conversion." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-position event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh (x y) client coordinates for key/mouse, screen coordinates for context-menu, NIL for keyboard context-menu sentinel. Native coordinates, not automatic DIP conversion.")) ("Description" (:p "Fresh (x y) client coordinates for key/mouse, screen coordinates for context-menu, NIL for keyboard context-menu sentinel. Native coordinates, not automatic DIP conversion.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-propagates-p" :names ("event-propagates-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Observe native ShouldPropagate, independently of Skip. A positive level alone does not forward a consumed event." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-propagates-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTEXT is the current event context. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "T when the native propagation level is positive, otherwise NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Observe native ShouldPropagate, independently of Skip. A positive level alone does not forward a consumed event.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread session and the innermost currently executing contextual callback. Expired or outer contexts in nested callbacks signal NATIVE-ERROR for native access. Activity queries return NIL for those contexts during a session; outside a session they signal NATIVE-ERROR. No raw native event pointer escapes. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Veto applies only to actual wxCloseEvent/wxNotifyEvent contexts; arbitrary event types, general event construction/cloning and native control-specific subclasses and validated OS session delivery remains open. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::ShouldPropagate (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-raw-control-down-p" :names ("event-raw-control-down-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy wxKeyboardState::RawControlDown from native key/mouse input. Distinguishes native Command semantics and physical Control on macOS." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-raw-control-down-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Key/mouse EVENT snapshot or current innermost EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native boolean state.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy wxKeyboardState::RawControlDown from native key/mouse input. Distinguishes native Command semantics and physical Control on macOS.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Read-only copied input payload. Wrong kinds and expired/outside-innermost contexts reject. No synthetic/owned/cloned input events; no platform flag inference. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyboardState::RawControlDown, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-raw-key-code" :names ("event-raw-key-code") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native platform raw key code or NIL when unsupported." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-raw-key-code event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native platform raw key code or NIL when unsupported.")) ("Description" (:p "Native platform raw key code or NIL when unsupported.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-raw-key-flags" :names ("event-raw-key-flags") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native platform raw key flags or NIL when unsupported." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-raw-key-flags event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native platform raw key flags or NIL when unsupported.")) ("Description" (:p "Native platform raw key flags or NIL when unsupported.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-related-window-id" :names ("event-related-window-id") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Numeric registered previous/next focus window identity or NIL; no raw pointer, ownership or retained liveness." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-related-window-id event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Numeric registered previous/next focus window identity or NIL; no raw pointer, ownership or retained liveness.")) ("Description" (:p "Numeric registered previous/next focus window identity or NIL; no raw pointer, ownership or retained liveness.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-sash-position" :names ("event-sash-position" "(setf event-sash-position)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "EVENT snapshot or context: sash pixels, NIL for unrelated snapshots. SETF only current CHANGING context: -1 cancels, or 0..536870911." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-sash-position event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT snapshot or context: sash pixels, NIL for unrelated snapshots. SETF only current CHANGING context: -1 cancels, or 0..536870911.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "EVENT snapshot or context: sash pixels, NIL for unrelated snapshots. SETF only current CHANGING context: -1 cancels, or 0..536870911.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-sash-position object) value)") (:p "EVENT snapshot or context: sash pixels, NIL for unrelated snapshots. SETF only current CHANGING context: -1 cancels, or 0..536870911."))))
(:entry "api/event-selection" :names ("event-selection" "(setf event-selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Reads choice/listbox wxCommandEvent selection metadata, or derived wxBookCtrlEvent selection for notebook changing/changed. This is event payload, not a fresh control-model query. Notebook CHANGING semantics are port-dependent (Windows may report the old page); old-selection metadata is not exposed. Snapshots survive later item edits unchanged. Radio-box wxCommandEvent selection is read-only semantic metadata; it does not query current control state. :COMBO-SELECTION command metadata is read-only semantic index data; it is not a fresh combo query. TEXT snapshots have NIL selection." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-selection event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "An immutable EVENT snapshot, live OWNED-EVENT, or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Zero-based choice/listbox/radio-box/combo-box or native notebook event index; NIL for none/non-selection kinds.")) ("Description" (:p "Reads choice/listbox wxCommandEvent selection metadata, or derived wxBookCtrlEvent selection for notebook changing/changed. This is event payload, not a fresh control-model query. Notebook CHANGING semantics are port-dependent (Windows may report the old page); old-selection metadata is not exposed. Snapshots survive later item edits unchanged. Radio-box wxCommandEvent selection is read-only semantic metadata; it does not query current control state. :COMBO-SELECTION command metadata is read-only semantic index data; it is not a fresh combo query. TEXT snapshots have NIL selection.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Snapshots need no session. Owned/context access requires the active main-thread session and a live resource/exact current context. Notebook selection is read-only; writable payload supports only choice/listbox selection/activation kinds, not arbitrary command tags. RADIO-BOX :radio-selection is a native-only command kind with copied/current index and native label metadata. Snapshot reads survive source/session cleanup; borrowed contexts require the exact innermost current callback. No owned/synthetic/cloned radio events. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md. ABI57 raw key/mouse/focus/context-menu/size, STC and AUI native kinds have copied read-only payload metadata and reject owned/synthetic construction/cloning. Ordinary observers automatically Skip; scoped handlers explicitly Skip unhandled native input. STC styling has the exact innermost same-control STYLENEEDED StartStyling/SetStyling exception. AUI close/changing veto is native-scoped and CLOSED has former index/captured target ID. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md, docs/STYLED-TEXT.md and docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::GetSelection/SetInt for wxEVT_CHOICE, wxEVT_LISTBOX and wxEVT_LISTBOX_DCLICK; wxBookCtrlEvent::GetSelection read-only (wxWidgets 3.2.12). wxEVT_RADIOBOX/wxCommandEvent::GetSelection (read-only). wxEVT_COMBOBOX/wxCommandEvent::GetSelection (read-only).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-selection event-or-context) value)") (:p "VALUE is NIL or a nonnegative signed-int index. Mutates live choice/listbox command payload only, without changing control selection or raw extra-LONG action metadata. Notebook kinds, other tags, snapshots and stale/suspended contexts reject. Radio-box kinds reject. Combo selection kinds reject; new kind has no owned/synthetic/clone resources."))))
(:entry "api/event-selection-p" :names ("event-selection-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read whether command extra LONG is nonzero. This is not a :SELECTION-kind predicate or index-validity test: normal choice metadata can have a valid index while this flag is NIL. Use EVENT-EXTRA-LONG to change the underlying field." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-selection-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Raw native IsSelection as T/NIL for command/notify events; NIL for close/idle-family reads.")) ("Description" (:p "Read whether command extra LONG is nonzero. This is not a :SELECTION-kind predicate or index-validity test: normal choice metadata can have a valid index while this flag is NIL. Use EVENT-EXTRA-LONG to change the underlying field.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved reads need no session. Live access requires active main-thread session and valid owned/innermost-context lifetime. No direct SETF, arbitrary derived event class or control-state operation is provided.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::IsSelection (m_extraLong !=0), including notify-derived events (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-size" :names ("event-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh native whole-window (width height), not client extent or a DIP guarantee." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-size event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native whole-window (width height), not client extent or a DIP guarantee.")) ("Description" (:p "Fresh native whole-window (width height), not client extent or a DIP guarantee.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-skipped-p" :names ("event-skipped-p" "(setf event-skipped-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Contextual bindings begin with Skip false. Assign true to continue to later native handlers and normal parent routing; false consumes the command at this handler. This is distinct from propagation level. Mutation is not rolled back on callback errors. Observer bindings without a context retain automatic Skip." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-skipped-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTEXT is the current event context. SETF VALUE is a generalized boolean. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native Skip flag as T/NIL; SETF returns the supplied value.")) ("Description" (:p "Contextual bindings begin with Skip false. Assign true to continue to later native handlers and normal parent routing; false consumes the command at this handler. This is distinct from propagation level. Mutation is not rolled back on callback errors. Observer bindings without a context retain automatic Skip.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread session and the innermost currently executing contextual callback. Expired or outer contexts in nested callbacks signal NATIVE-ERROR for native access. Activity queries return NIL for those contexts during a session; outside a session they signal NATIVE-ERROR. No raw native event pointer escapes. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Veto applies only to actual wxCloseEvent/wxNotifyEvent contexts; arbitrary event types, general event construction/cloning and native control-specific subclasses and validated OS session delivery remains open. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetSkipped / Skip (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-skipped-p event-or-context) value)") (:p "Set the native Skip flag only while CONTEXT is current. A true value continues dispatch; returning from a contextual callback does not automatically override the flag. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-source" :names ("event-source") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the binding receiver. For parent-propagated command events this can differ from the native originating child. EVENT-ORIGIN-ID separately reports a known native origin bridge identity without wrapping arbitrary wxObjects; EVENT-ID remains event routing metadata. Saved receiver wrappers may outlive their native object." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-source event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an event snapshot.")) ("Returns" (:p "The Lisp handler/control on which this callback was registered.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the binding receiver. For parent-propagated command events this can differ from the native originating child. EVENT-ORIGIN-ID separately reports a known native origin bridge identity without wrapping arbitrary wxObjects; EVENT-ID remains event routing metadata. Saved receiver wrappers may outlive their native object.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "No active GUI session required for saved snapshots. Wrong argument types signal Lisp type errors.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Lisp-owned wxCommandEvent snapshot."))))
(:entry "api/event-stc-fold-level-now" :names ("event-stc-fold-level-now") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "MODIFIED current native fold level." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-stc-fold-level-now event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Appropriate native STC immutable snapshot or current innermost event context.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied native integer metadata.")) ("Description" (:p "MODIFIED current native fold level.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Snapshots survive native/session cleanup. Wrong event kinds or unavailable fields signal; contexts additionally require exact innermost active native callback. No writer, raw origin retention, owned/synthetic/cloned STC event. Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextEvent, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-stc-fold-level-previous" :names ("event-stc-fold-level-previous") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "MODIFIED prior native fold level." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-stc-fold-level-previous event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Appropriate native STC immutable snapshot or current innermost event context.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied native integer metadata.")) ("Description" (:p "MODIFIED prior native fold level.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Snapshots survive native/session cleanup. Wrong event kinds or unavailable fields signal; contexts additionally require exact innermost active native callback. No writer, raw origin retention, owned/synthetic/cloned STC event. Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextEvent, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
