(:entry "api/event-text" :names ("event-text" "(setf event-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or copy native command string payload. Context/owned SETF uses explicit UTF-8 byte lengths, preserving embedded NULs. Saved snapshots stay immutable and retain their prior kind-specific payload interpretation. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-text event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a snapshot, current context or live OWNED-EVENT. SETF VALUE is a string and requires native command/notify state.")) ("Returns" (:p "Snapshot kind-specific copied string/NIL; live command/notify string (possibly empty), or NIL for close/idle-family reads. SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read or copy native command string payload. Context/owned SETF uses explicit UTF-8 byte lengths, preserving embedded NULs. Saved snapshots stay immutable and retain their prior kind-specific payload interpretation. ABI38 listbox selection/double-click command events carry cached string/index payloads; snapshots are independent of later item edits. Native list callback guards protect receiver/ancestors and defer modal/clipboard entry while allowing item edits.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved reads need no session. Live access requires active main-thread session and valid owned/innermost-context lifetime. Text writes to close/idle-family events reject; non-string values signal TYPE-ERROR. Native wxEVT_TEXT with a tracked text-entry or SEARCH-CONTROL origin rejects context string SETF; unknown origins reject too. The control is not changed. Detached context clones freeze effective GetString before clearing origin. RADIO-BOX :radio-selection is a native-only command kind with copied/current index and native label metadata. Snapshot reads survive source/session cleanup; borrowed contexts require the exact innermost current callback. No owned/synthetic/cloned radio events. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md. :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE copies native checked/text metadata (text normally empty, including explicit notify; no inferred label); no owned/synthetic/clone. Snapshots survive cleanup, contexts expire. See docs/TOGGLE-BUTTONS.md. COMBO-BOX uses new native-only :COMBO-SELECTION and existing :TEXT-CHANGE. Physical native selections may emit multiple command/text notifications; explicit setters emit only their requested kind. See docs/COMBO-BOXES.md. SEARCH-CONTROL :SEARCH/:SEARCH-CANCEL copy native command strings including empty, without inferring current query. Context metadata writes do not change the query. New kinds reject owned/synthetic/clones; generic TEXT scope remains unchanged. See docs/SEARCH-CONTROLS.md. WEB-VIEW :WEB-MESSAGE/:WEB-SCRIPT-RESULT/:WEB-LOADED/:WEB-ERROR payload contexts are read-only: text/integer/extra-LONG SETF reject. Script results carry JSON or error text, success1/error0 in EVENT-INTEGER and ticket in EVENT-EXTRA-LONG; messages carry JSON without sender authentication. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md. ABI57 raw key/mouse/focus/context-menu/size, STC and AUI native kinds have copied read-only payload metadata and reject owned/synthetic construction/cloning. Ordinary observers automatically Skip; scoped handlers explicitly Skip unhandled native input. STC styling has the exact innermost same-control STYLENEEDED StartStyling/SetStyling exception. AUI close/changing veto is native-scoped and CLOSED has former index/captured target ID. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md, docs/STYLED-TEXT.md and docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. ABI58 :THREAD is a native base-family wxThreadEvent with copied immutable EVENT-TEXT, GUI-only callback dispatch and normal context lifetime. QUEUE-THREAD-EVENT alone permits worker posting after GUI binding; other GUI operations retain their thread rules. No owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent::GetString / SetString, including wxNotifyEvent (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-text event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign a command/notify native string, returning VALUE. Owned values are persistent; context writes affect the current dispatch copy. No snapshot writer."))))
(:entry "api/event-time" :names ("event-time") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read captured/current native wxDateEvent time components independently of current control value; ignore date/milliseconds. Non-time or expired/outer contexts reject. Snapshot survives callback/session. No setter, owned/synthetic events or detached clones." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-time event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current innermost borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh (hour minute second), including (0 0 0) at midnight; NIL for non-time snapshots or invalid native time payload.")) ("Description" (:p "Read captured/current native wxDateEvent time components independently of current control value; ignore date/milliseconds. Non-time or expired/outer contexts reject. Snapshot survives callback/session. No setter, owned/synthetic events or detached clones.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Native :time-change command family only. Separate from EVENT-DATE, EVENT-TIMESTAMP and raw integer/text metadata. Context lifetime isolation applies; no date/timezone/instant interpretation. See docs/TIME-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDateEvent::GetDate components and wxEVT_TIME_CHANGED, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-timestamp" :names ("event-timestamp" "(setf event-timestamp)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied/current native timestamp, not necessarily Unix time. Negative values including -1 are valid. Synthetic events start at zero. Context SETF changes metadata only, not scheduling. Snapshots stay immutable and preserve pre-callback values." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-timestamp context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot or current event context. SETF VALUE must fit signed native C long. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native millisecond timestamp as a Lisp integer; SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read copied/current native timestamp, not necessarily Unix time. Negative values including -1 are valid. Synthetic events start at zero. Context SETF changes metadata only, not scheduling. Snapshots stay immutable and preserve pre-callback values.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved snapshot reads need no native session. Context access requires an active main-thread session and the innermost callback; expired/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. Malformed/out-of-range SETF values signal TYPE-ERROR. Native LONG width is platform-specific; mouse/key events are not yet bound. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable. Native ABI57 raw input, STC and AUI context IDs/timestamps are read-only; their SETF writers reject.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetTimestamp / SetTimestamp, native signed long widened to int64_t at the ABI (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-timestamp event-or-context) value)") (:p "Assign a signed native LONG timestamp to the current event. No snapshot writer or synthetic-constructor timestamp keyword. No Unix-epoch or scheduling meaning is implied. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-tree-item" :names ("event-tree-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Snapshot retains view identity, not live validity or frozen label. Non-tree snapshots return NIL; non-tree contexts reject. No owned-event method/setter; associated item can be invalidated later. Copy text while live if needed. New native activation/menu/expanding/expanded/collapsing/collapsed tree events retain checked borrowed same-tree item tokens." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-tree-item event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current tree EVENT-CONTEXT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Canonical TREE-ITEM view or NIL when no managed associated item.")) ("Description" (:p "Snapshot retains view identity, not live validity or frozen label. Non-tree snapshots return NIL; non-tree contexts reject. No owned-event method/setter; associated item can be invalidated later. Copy text while live if needed. New native activation/menu/expanding/expanded/collapsing/collapsed tree events retain checked borrowed same-tree item tokens.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Snapshot field access needs no session. Context access requires active main-thread exact borrowed context; dereferencing returned item requires live token/owner. Native derived selection events only, no synthetic/owned/cloning/old-item support. wxQt tree construction is explicitly unavailable pending generation-safe asynchronous event translation.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTreeEvent::GetItem (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/event-tree-position" :names ("event-tree-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fresh (x y) copied native tree-item-menu point, including native keyboard context requests." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-tree-position event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(event-or-context)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Fresh (x y) copied native tree-item-menu point, including native keyboard context requests.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTreeEvent::GetPoint"))))
(:entry "api/event-type" :names ("event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Look up a process-local native type ID. Twenty-two built-in kinds plus registered command/notify names are supported. Registry names are session-scoped; saved snapshot native IDs remain plain data after cleanup. Borrowed application handler access is supported; arbitrary native event-class binding and OS session delivery remains unverified." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-type kind)")) ("Arguments" (:p "KIND is a built-in event keyword or a name registered in this active session.")) ("Returns" (:p "The corresponding process-local native wxEventType integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Look up a process-local native type ID. Twenty-two built-in kinds plus registered command/notify names are supported. Registry names are session-scoped; saved snapshot native IDs remain plain data after cleanup. Borrowed application handler access is supported; arbitrary native event-class binding and OS session delivery remains unverified.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required; inactive calls signal NATIVE-ERROR before native-library lookup. Native IDs are process-local and may change between runs. RADIO-BOX :radio-selection is a native-only command kind with copied/current index and native label metadata. Snapshot reads survive source/session cleanup; borrowed contexts require the exact innermost current callback. No owned/synthetic/cloned radio events. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md. Scrolling panels add no new public scroll event kind.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEVT_BUTTON, wxEVT_TEXT, wxEVT_CHECKBOX, wxEVT_CHOICE, wxEVT_CLOSE_WINDOW, wxEVT_QUERY_END_SESSION, wxEVT_END_SESSION, wxEVT_IDLE, wxEVT_MENU, wxEVT_NOTEBOOK_PAGE_CHANGING, wxEVT_NOTEBOOK_PAGE_CHANGED, wxEVT_LISTBOX, wxEVT_LISTBOX_DCLICK; registered wxNewEventType values (wxWidgets 3.2.12). wxEVT_TREE_SEL_CHANGING and wxEVT_TREE_SEL_CHANGED in ABI39. Includes wxEVT_SPLITTER_SASH_POS_CHANGING/CHANGED, wxEVT_SLIDER, wxEVT_SPINCTRL and wxEVT_RADIOBOX (wxWidgets3.2.12). wxEVT_TOGGLEBUTTON. wxEVT_COMBOBOX."))))
(:entry "api/event-unicode-key" :names ("event-unicode-key") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Integer Unicode key value or NIL for WXK_NONE; not IME composition text." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-unicode-key event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Integer Unicode key value or NIL for WXK_NONE; not IME composition text.")) ("Description" (:p "Integer Unicode key value or NIL for WXK_NONE; not IME composition text.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-user-data" :names ("event-user-data") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the snapshot-captured or callback-frame-retained binding association. No deep copy: mutable referent contents remain ordinary Lisp state. Snapshot reads survive unbind/receiver/session cleanup. Current frames retain values across self/peer unbind and nested dispatch restores outer context identity." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-user-data event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is an immutable snapshot, current innermost context or live OWNED-EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p "The per-binding EQ Lisp value or NIL. Owned events return NIL after native validation; borrowed native pointers reject.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the snapshot-captured or callback-frame-retained binding association. No deep copy: mutable referent contents remain ordinary Lisp state. Snapshot reads survive unbind/receiver/session cleanup. Current frames retain values across self/peer unbind and nested dispatch restores outer context identity.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Saved reads need no native session. Context/owned reads require active main-thread session and valid native lifetime; stale/suspended contexts signal NATIVE-ERROR. No SETF, mutable association API, owned constructor/queue payload, pointer adoption or convenience ON-* userdata keyword. General native client/userData ownership remains unbound.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::GetEventUserData via entry-owned numeric wxObject binding adapter and captured context identity (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/event-vetoed-p" :names ("event-vetoed-p" "(setf event-vetoed-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Snapshots retain pre-callback state. Close contexts use GetVeto / checked Veto(bool); notify contexts use NOT IsAllowed, Veto() for true, and Allow() for NIL. A close initialized non-vetoable rejects writes unless its current CanVeto flag was explicitly enabled through SETF EVENT-CAN-VETO-P. Plain command contexts reject live veto-state access. Snapshots stay immutable. Native GetVeto is CanVeto AND the stored veto bit; disabling capability hides the bit without clearing it." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-vetoed-p context)")) ("Arguments" (:p "EVENT is a saved snapshot or current close/notify context. SETF requires a current veto-capable context. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied/current veto state as T/NIL; SETF returns the supplied generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Snapshots retain pre-callback state. Close contexts use GetVeto / checked Veto(bool); notify contexts use NOT IsAllowed, Veto() for true, and Allow() for NIL. A close initialized non-vetoable rejects writes unless its current CanVeto flag was explicitly enabled through SETF EVENT-CAN-VETO-P. Plain command contexts reject live veto-state access. Snapshots stay immutable. Native GetVeto is CanVeto AND the stored veto bit; disabling capability hides the bit without clearing it.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required for native context or frame operations. Expired/suspended contexts and invalid/deleting frames signal NATIVE-ERROR. Saved snapshots need no session. Close and registered notify families permit checked veto. Other native control-specific notify subclasses, validated OS session delivery and arbitrary event classes remain open. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCloseEvent::GetVeto / Veto(bool); wxNotifyEvent::IsAllowed / Veto / Allow. (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:event-vetoed-p event-or-context) value)") (:p "Close contexts require CanVeto true before either assignment. Notify true invokes Veto and NIL invokes Allow. Plain command contexts and stale/suspended contexts reject access; snapshots have no SETF method. Also accepts a live OWNED-EVENT under the same field/family restrictions; owned writes change the reusable resource, not copies already dispatched."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-axis" :names ("event-wheel-axis") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary ":vertical or :horizontal." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-axis event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p ":vertical or :horizontal.")) ("Description" (:p ":vertical or :horizontal.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-columns" :names ("event-wheel-columns") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native columns per horizontal wheel action." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-columns event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native columns per horizontal wheel action.")) ("Description" (:p "Native columns per horizontal wheel action.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-delta" :names ("event-wheel-delta") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native wheel delta threshold; do not assume one event equals one line." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-delta event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native wheel delta threshold; do not assume one event equals one line.")) ("Description" (:p "Native wheel delta threshold; do not assume one event equals one line.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-inverted-p" :names ("event-wheel-inverted-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native natural-scroll metadata; macOS already applies configured direction." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-inverted-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native natural-scroll metadata; macOS already applies configured direction.")) ("Description" (:p "Native natural-scroll metadata; macOS already applies configured direction.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-lines" :names ("event-wheel-lines") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native lines per wheel action." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-lines event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native lines per wheel action.")) ("Description" (:p "Native lines per wheel action.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-page-scroll-p" :names ("event-wheel-page-scroll-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native page-scroll boolean." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-page-scroll-p event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native page-scroll boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Native page-scroll boolean.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/event-wheel-rotation" :names ("event-wheel-rotation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Signed native wheel rotation, potentially finer than delta." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:event-wheel-rotation event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Immutable EVENT snapshot or current borrowed EVENT-CONTEXT of the appropriate kind.")) ("Returns" (:p "Signed native wheel rotation, potentially finer than delta.")) ("Description" (:p "Signed native wheel rotation, potentially finer than delta.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Raw input uses existing BIND-EVENT immutable snapshots/current-innermost contexts. Readers kind-check; payloads read-only; no native pointer adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned input events. Observers automatically Skip; contextual bindings must explicitly Skip unhandled input. Consuming KEY_DOWN/CHAR_HOOK can suppress normal CHAR/native editing/accelerators. Raw events do not imply portable IME composition support. GUI-thread/lifetime/source/ancestor/native-entry guards apply during callbacks. See docs/INPUT-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxKeyEvent/wxMouseEvent/wxFocusEvent/wxContextMenuEvent/wxSizeEvent bounded copied input adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/file-dialog" :names ("file-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a generic single-file selection dialog. Directory/path accept strings or pathnames converted through native namestring; supplied directory must exist, empty directory lets native code use cwd. Path must be nonempty; filename is a string. Filters require nonempty description/pattern pairs and valid zero-based filter index. No change-directory flag, multiselect or external controls. Dialog browser actions such as New Directory can change the filesystem; selection does not perform file-content IO. True MUST-EXIST is rejected for :SAVE, and true OVERWRITE-PROMPT for :OPEN. Supplied path directories must exist." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:file-dialog")) ("Arguments" (:p "Optional :PARENT, :TITLE(default \"Open file\"/\"Save file\" by mode), :DIRECTORY(default empty), :FILENAME(default empty), :WILDCARD(default \"All files|*\"), :MODE(:OPEN default or :SAVE), :MUST-EXIST(default true for open), :OVERWRITE-PROMPT(default true for save), :FILTER-INDEX(default0) and optional :PATH.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed dialog.")) ("Description" (:p "Construct a generic single-file selection dialog. Directory/path accept strings or pathnames converted through native namestring; supplied directory must exist, empty directory lets native code use cwd. Path must be nonempty; filename is a string. Filters require nonempty description/pattern pairs and valid zero-based filter index. No change-directory flag, multiselect or external controls. Dialog browser actions such as New Directory can change the filesystem; selection does not perform file-content IO. True MUST-EXIST is rejected for :SAVE, and true OVERWRITE-PROMPT for :OPEN. Supplied path directories must exist.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGenericFileDialog; bounded equivalent wxFileDialog public surface (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:file-dialog :mode :open :wildcard \"Lisp files|*.lisp|All files|*\")") (:p "Native-backed DIALOG/WINDOW subclass supporting direct construction, subclass slots/DEFAULT-INITARGS/AFTER and rollback. Optional parent is normalized to explicit requested window (including hidden) or truly parentless NIL. Construction is allowed in GUI-thread callbacks/RUN/pumps. Failed initialization cleans new resources/roots without reversing arbitrary external changes. Strings are Unicode without NUL."))))
(:entry "api/file-dialog-filter-index" :names ("file-dialog-filter-index" "(setf file-dialog-filter-index)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write one of the construction-time wildcard description/pattern pairs. Invalid index rejects. Filters do not prove current path acceptance." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:file-dialog-filter-index dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is live FILE-DIALOG. SETF VALUE is valid zero-based filter-pair index.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native filter index; SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write one of the construction-time wildcard description/pattern pairs. Invalid index rejects. Filters do not prove current path acceptance.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxFileDialogBase::GetFilterIndex / SetFilterIndex")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:file-dialog-filter-index dialog) value)") (:p "Select an existing filter pair and return VALUE; no wildcard mutation or acceptance claim. Uses the notifying boundary for native prompt/callback safety."))))
(:entry "api/file-dialog-mode" :names ("file-dialog-mode") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read fixed single-file selection mode. Configured native UI validation differs from raw END-MODAL result assignment. Reader reflects the actual restored generic file flags, including the macOS overlap repair, rather than merely echoing a Lisp requested-mode slot." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:file-dialog-mode dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is a live FILE-DIALOG.")) ("Returns" (:p ":OPEN or :SAVE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read fixed single-file selection mode. Configured native UI validation differs from raw END-MODAL result assignment. Reader reflects the actual restored generic file flags, including the macOS overlap repair, rather than merely echoing a Lisp requested-mode slot.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bounded wxFileDialog open/save style view"))))
(:entry "api/file-dialog-path" :names ("file-dialog-path" "(setf file-dialog-path)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write current single-file path. This is not acceptance, file existence, overwrite confirmation or successful content IO. A raw END-MODAL :OK bypasses button validation/transfer, must-exist and overwrite enforcement. Native property changes can open internal prompts and use the guarded prompt workflow." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:file-dialog-path dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is live FILE-DIALOG. SETF VALUE is nonempty string/pathname; pathnames convert to native namestring. A directory component, when present, must exist.")) ("Returns" (:p "Current native path string; SETF returns original supplied VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write current single-file path. This is not acceptance, file existence, overwrite confirmation or successful content IO. A raw END-MODAL :OK bypasses button validation/transfer, must-exist and overwrite enforcement. Native property changes can open internal prompts and use the guarded prompt workflow.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxFileDialogBase::GetPath / wxGenericFileDialog::SetPath")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:file-dialog-path dialog) value)") (:p "Set converted nonempty native path; return original string/pathname, not the normalized getter string. No file content IO or acceptance guarantee."))))
(:entry "api/fill-stc-indicator-range" :names ("fill-stc-indicator-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native GetLength, IndicatorFillRange. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:fill-stc-indicator-range control start length)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; START native position.; LENGTH native nonnegative.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native GetLength, IndicatorFillRange. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/fit-scroll-content" :names ("fit-scroll-content") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Layout/FitInside/Layout refreshes virtual extent from max(client,sizer minimum), without resizing frame. Requires own sizer and supported content extent; no callback mutation." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:fit-scroll-content panel)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL with own attached sizer.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied panel.")) ("Description" (:p "Layout/FitInside/Layout refreshes virtual extent from max(client,sizer minimum), without resizing frame. Requires own sizer and supported content extent; no callback mutation.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. No callback-time fit/rate/position changes: defer via owner-bound UI action. Supported extent<=1000000 pixels/axis checked before explicit mutation, not globally enforced on inherited/native layout. Private native scroll helper stays owned; managed handler-stack APIs reject for this class. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Layout/FitInside (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/flush-clipboard" :names ("flush-clipboard") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Best-effort persistence after exit, on the standard clipboard. Does not set clipboard contents. A false native Flush result is normal; open/session failures signal NATIVE-ERROR." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:flush-clipboard )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "T when native Flush succeeds, NIL for unsupported/unsuccessful persistence.")) ("Description" (:p "Best-effort persistence after exit, on the standard clipboard. Does not set clipboard contents. A false native Flush result is normal; open/session failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; brief scoped open/close and restored PRIMARY preference. Port-specific support; live exit persistence remains unverified. ABI37 rejects entry during notebook navigation/page callbacks; defer to later application work. ABI38 also rejects entry while a list-origin selection/activation callback is active. ABI39 also defers entry during tree operations/selection callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxClipboard::Flush (wxWidgets 3.2.12; pinned documentation identifies MSW/GTK support)."))))
(:entry "api/focus-window" :names ("focus-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request native SetFocus, or SetFocusFromKbd for a keyboard-origin request. Containers can delegate focus to children; keyboard focus can select text according to the native control." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:focus-window window &key from-keyboard)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW; keyword FROM-KEYBOARD defaults NIL (generalized boolean).")) ("Returns" (:p "WINDOW after requesting focus.")) ("Description" (:p "Request native SetFocus, or SetFocusFromKbd for a keyboard-origin request. Containers can delegate focus to children; keyboard focus can select text according to the native control.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Shown-on-screen, enabled live window on GUI thread; callbacks reject: use an owner-bound deferred UI action. OS activation/focus receipt is not guaranteed. Synchronous operation protects all session windows from bridge destruction/close and blocks nested navigation, GUI/modal/clipboard entry. No focus event binding or global focused-window pointer is exposed.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::SetFocus / SetFocusFromKbd, wxPanel::SetFocus; wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/frame" :names ("frame") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxFrame, including frame-specific title methods." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:frame")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass: WXLAMBDA:WINDOW. Optional :accelerators defaults NIL; list entries (KEY ID &rest MODIFIERS), see FRAME-ACCELERATORS.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance of this class or a subclass (WINDOW itself is abstract).")) ("Description" (:p "CLOS wrapper for wxFrame, including frame-specific title methods.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Construction requires an active main-thread application session. Concrete classes create their native widgets in inherited INITIALIZE-INSTANCE methods; subclass AFTER hooks can use them. Native handles cannot be supplied as initargs. Lisp subclassing does not imply native C++ virtual callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxFrame (wxWidgets 3.2); this is a Lisp wrapper, not a native subclass.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:frame)") (:p "TITLE string, WIDTH 480 and HEIGHT 240; default title is wxlambda. Class :DEFAULT-INITARGS and custom slot initargs are honored; native creation precedes subclass AFTER hooks. :ACCELERATORS installs a copied frame table before subclass AFTER hooks; see FRAME-ACCELERATORS."))))
(:entry "api/frame-accelerators" :names ("frame-accelerators" "(setf frame-accelerators)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/replace a copied native frame accelerator table for shared :MENU action IDs. Native menu enable/check and origin/metadata behavior vary by port; use a Lisp action model." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:frame-accelerators frame)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME. Entries are (KEY ID &rest MODIFIERS): ASCII letters/digits or :F1..:F12, ID1..32767, :CTRL/:SHIFT/:ALT/:RAW-CTRL. Maximum256; modified letters/digits only.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh normalized nested lists. Generic SETF returns original supplied list; NIL clears the explicit table.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/replace a copied native frame accelerator table for shared :MENU action IDs. Native menu enable/check and origin/metadata behavior vary by port; use a Lisp action model.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active live frame. Quiescent whole-table replacement, duplicate effective chords and invalid/cyclic input reject without replacing the prior table. While tables are nonempty all managed :MENU callbacks conservatively protect installed-frame subtrees and reject modal/clipboard/nested dispatch entry. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp validation errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/KEYBOARD-ACCELERATORS.md. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAcceleratorEntry, wxAcceleratorTable, wxWindow::SetAcceleratorTable (wxWidgets3.2.12); wxUSE_ACCEL required.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:frame-accelerators frame) entries)") (:p "Replace/clear only outside RUN, pumps, callbacks and modal loops. Copies entries, canonicalizes keys/modifiers, bounds count/ID and rejects duplicate native chords. ABI43 also permits this operation inside a safe deferred UI action under RUN/poll; nested event callback guards remain."))))
(:entry "api/frame-title" :names ("frame-title" "(setf frame-title)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the frame title, including the title initially supplied to MAKE-FRAME. Returned strings survive later metadata queries and destruction." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:frame-title frame)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME is a live frame.")) ("Returns" (:p "An independent Lisp string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the frame title, including the title initially supplied to MAKE-FRAME. Returned strings survive later metadata queries and destruction.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Only wxFrame receivers are currently exposed; panels and other controls signal NATIVE-ERROR. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTopLevelWindow::GetTitle (wxWidgets 3.2).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:frame-title frame) new-value)") (:p "Update the frame title. Other top-level receiver types remain future work. Writers are generic functions with VALUE first, followed by the receiver."))))
(:entry "api/from-dip" :names ("from-dip") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native FromDIP(wxPoint); input±1000000 DIP." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:from-dip object x y)")) ("Arguments" (:p "window x y")) ("Returns" (:p "Two-element converted coordinate list.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native FromDIP(wxPoint); input±1000000 DIP.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/gauge" :names ("gauge") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Parent-owned progress indicator; supports inherited window operations. Positive range, value from zero through range, horizontal or vertical orientation. IDs, position, size, validator and native name use wxWidgets defaults; custom styles, taskbar progress and two-step creation remain unbound." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:gauge")) ("Arguments" (:p "Native-backed WINDOW subclass. Required :PARENT; :RANGE defaults to 100, :VALUE to 0, :ORIENTATION to :HORIZONTAL.")) ("Returns" (:p "A gauge wrapper or Lisp subclass instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Parent-owned progress indicator; supports inherited window operations. Positive range, value from zero through range, horizontal or vertical orientation. IDs, position, size, validator and native name use wxWidgets defaults; custom styles, taskbar progress and two-step creation remain unbound.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires a live gauge in an active main-thread GUI session. Stale/destroyed handles, native type errors and values above the range signal NATIVE-ERROR; wrong Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Numeric arguments must fit signed 32-bit integers; invalid Lisp types/ranges signal TYPE-ERROR. No command events or native virtual overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGauge constructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:gauge :parent parent :range 100 :value 0 :orientation :horizontal)") (:p "Subclass slot initargs and :DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported. Native properties are ready in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed managed initialization rolls back native allocation. Orientation is :HORIZONTAL or :VERTICAL and cannot be changed after construction."))))
(:entry "api/gauge-range" :names ("gauge-range" "(setf gauge-range)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or assign the maximum progress. Assignment clamps the current native value to the new range and restores determinate mode by calling SetRange followed by SetValue. After a pulse the preserved value is platform-dependent; explicitly set GAUGE-VALUE when resuming measured work." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:gauge-range gauge)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GAUGE is a live gauge; SETF VALUE is an integer in [1, 2147483647].")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive integer maximum; SETF returns the supplied integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read or assign the maximum progress. Assignment clamps the current native value to the new range and restores determinate mode by calling SetRange followed by SetValue. After a pulse the preserved value is platform-dependent; explicitly set GAUGE-VALUE when resuming measured work.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires a live gauge in an active main-thread GUI session. Stale/destroyed handles, native type errors and values above the range signal NATIVE-ERROR; wrong Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Numeric arguments must fit signed 32-bit integers; invalid Lisp types/ranges signal TYPE-ERROR. No command events or native virtual overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGauge::GetRange / SetRange / SetValue (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:gauge-range gauge) value)") (:p "A positive signed 32-bit integer. Progress becomes MIN(old native value, new range); no events. Zero ranges are intentionally unsupported."))))
(:entry "api/gauge-value" :names ("gauge-value" "(setf gauge-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read determinate progress. After PULSE-GAUGE the reading is platform-dependent; do not interpret it as completed work. Assigning a value restores determinate mode without events." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:gauge-value gauge)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GAUGE is a live gauge; SETF VALUE is an integer from 0 through GAUGE-RANGE.")) ("Returns" (:p "Integer progress; SETF returns the supplied integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read determinate progress. After PULSE-GAUGE the reading is platform-dependent; do not interpret it as completed work. Assigning a value restores determinate mode without events.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires a live gauge in an active main-thread GUI session. Stale/destroyed handles, native type errors and values above the range signal NATIVE-ERROR; wrong Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Numeric arguments must fit signed 32-bit integers; invalid Lisp types/ranges signal TYPE-ERROR. No command events or native virtual overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGauge::GetValue / SetValue (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:gauge-value gauge) value)") (:p "VALUE must be an integer in [0, range]. Invalid updates preserve existing progress. No notification option."))))
(:entry "api/gauge-vertical-p" :names ("gauge-vertical-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query construction orientation; this property has no writer." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:gauge-vertical-p gauge)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GAUGE is a live gauge.")) ("Returns" (:p "T for vertical, NIL for horizontal.")) ("Description" (:p "Query construction orientation; this property has no writer.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires a live gauge in an active main-thread GUI session. Stale/destroyed handles, native type errors and values above the range signal NATIVE-ERROR; wrong Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Numeric arguments must fit signed 32-bit integers; invalid Lisp types/ranges signal TYPE-ERROR. No command events or native virtual overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGauge::IsVertical (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/grid" :names ("grid") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fixed-shape native-owned default string table with native keyboard/mouse editing. CLOS subclasses/defaults/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure/root rollback. Requires wxUSE_GRID/core." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:grid")) ("Arguments" (:p "Required live :parent WINDOW; :rows default10, :columns default5, :editable-p defaultT. Dimensions1..256, total<=16384 cells; subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed GRID WINDOW subtype.")) ("Description" (:p "Fixed-shape native-owned default string table with native keyboard/mouse editing. CLOS subclasses/defaults/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure/root rollback. Requires wxUSE_GRID/core.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::Create/CreateGrid, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:grid :parent parent :rows 10 :columns 5 :editable-p t)") (:p "Direct subclass construction forwards slot/default initargs; mixed concrete native kinds reject before native allocation."))))
(:entry "api/grid-can-enable-cell-control-p" :names ("grid-can-enable-cell-control-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query native current-cell editor availability." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-can-enable-cell-control-p grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Query native current-cell editor availability.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::CanEnableCellControl"))))
(:entry "api/grid-cell-background" :names ("grid-cell-background" "(setf grid-cell-background)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write a copied per-cell native attribute." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-cell-background grid row column)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, zero-based ROW and COLUMN. SETF accepts 0xRRGGBB integer.")) ("Returns" (:p "0xRRGGBB integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write a copied per-cell native attribute.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::SetCellBackgroundColour / GetCellBackgroundColour")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-cell-background grid row column) value)") (:p "Set the checked native property and return the supplied value. Callback and active editor writes reject."))))
(:entry "api/grid-cell-editor-shown-p" :names ("grid-cell-editor-shown-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query native editor visibility, independently of enabled editing." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-cell-editor-shown-p grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Query native editor visibility, independently of enabled editing.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::IsCellEditControlShown"))))
(:entry "api/grid-cell-foreground" :names ("grid-cell-foreground" "(setf grid-cell-foreground)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write a copied per-cell native attribute." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-cell-foreground grid row column)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, zero-based ROW and COLUMN. SETF accepts 0xRRGGBB integer.")) ("Returns" (:p "0xRRGGBB integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write a copied per-cell native attribute.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::SetCellTextColour / GetCellTextColour")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-cell-foreground grid row column) value)") (:p "Set the checked native property and return the supplied value. Callback and active editor writes reject."))))
(:entry "api/grid-cell-read-only-p" :names ("grid-cell-read-only-p" "(setf grid-cell-read-only-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write a copied per-cell native attribute." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-cell-read-only-p grid row column)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, zero-based ROW and COLUMN. SETF accepts Generalized boolean.")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write a copied per-cell native attribute.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::SetReadOnly / IsReadOnly")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-cell-read-only-p grid row column) value)") (:p "Set the checked native property and return the supplied value. Callback and active editor writes reject."))))
(:entry "api/grid-cell-text" :names ("grid-cell-text" "(setf grid-cell-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write copied native string-table cell text. An active editor buffer can differ; read-only user policy does not prohibit programmatic writes." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-cell-text grid row column)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID and zero-based ROW/COLUMN within actual shape. SETF accepts a NUL-free string <=65536 UTF-8 bytes, including multiline text.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh committed-value string; writer returns supplied string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write copied native string-table cell text. An active editor buffer can differ; read-only user policy does not prohibit programmatic writes.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::GetCellValue/SetCellValue, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-cell-text grid row column) value)") (:p "Writer returns the supplied value. Callback use and active native editors reject; native string mutations are silent."))))
(:entry "api/grid-column-label" :names ("grid-column-label" "(setf grid-column-label)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write a copied column label, initially native defaults. Empty labels accepted." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-column-label grid column)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID and zero-based COLUMN within shape. SETF NUL-free string <=65536 UTF-8 bytes.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native label string; writer returns supplied string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write a copied column label, initially native defaults. Empty labels accepted.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::GetColLabelValue/SetColLabelValue, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-column-label grid column) value)") (:p "Writer returns the supplied value. Callback use and active native editors reject; native string mutations are silent."))))
(:entry "api/grid-columns" :names ("grid-columns") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the fixed native column count; no dimension writer." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-columns grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the fixed native column count; no dimension writer.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::GetNumberCols, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/grid-cursor" :names ("grid-cursor" "(setf grid-cursor)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native cursor or request SetGridCursor. SELECT_CELL veto can prevent movement; read back resulting state." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-cursor grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID. SETF accepts (ROW COLUMN).")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh pair or NIL; SETF returns supplied pair.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native cursor or request SetGridCursor. SELECT_CELL veto can prevent movement; read back resulting state.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::GetGridCursorRow / GetGridCursorCol / SetGridCursor")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-cursor grid) value)") (:p "Set the checked native property and return the supplied value. Callback and active editor writes reject."))))
(:entry "api/grid-editable-p" :names ("grid-editable-p" "(setf grid-editable-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Enable/disable native user edits for the whole grid. Programmatic text writes still work while user editing is disabled. Active editor refusal avoids implicit commit." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-editable-p grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID; SETF accepts generalized boolean.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native T/NIL user-editing policy; writer returns supplied value.")) ("Description" (:p "Enable/disable native user edits for the whole grid. Programmatic text writes still work while user editing is disabled. Active editor refusal avoids implicit commit.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::IsEditable/EnableEditing, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-editable-p grid) value)") (:p "Writer returns the supplied value. Callback use and active native editors reject; native string mutations are silent."))))
(:entry "api/grid-editing-p" :names ("grid-editing-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read whether the native cell editor is enabled, including when hidden. This is not focus or dirty state; no explicit commit/cancel writer." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-editing-p grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native T/NIL editor enablement.")) ("Description" (:p "Read whether the native cell editor is enabled, including when hidden. This is not focus or dirty state; no explicit commit/cancel writer.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::IsCellEditControlEnabled, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/grid-row-label" :names ("grid-row-label" "(setf grid-row-label)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write a copied row label, initially native defaults. Empty labels accepted." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-row-label grid row)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID and zero-based ROW within shape. SETF NUL-free string <=65536 UTF-8 bytes.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native label string; writer returns supplied string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write a copied row label, initially native defaults. Empty labels accepted.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::GetRowLabelValue/SetRowLabelValue, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:grid-row-label grid row) value)") (:p "Writer returns the supplied value. Callback use and active native editors reject; native string mutations are silent."))))
(:entry "api/grid-rows" :names ("grid-rows") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the fixed native row count; no dimension writer." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:grid-rows grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the fixed native row count; no dimension writer.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::GetNumberRows, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/handler-alive-p" :names ("handler-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Observe native lifetime without dereferencing dead windows. Native weak tracking makes window destruction safe even with event processing disabled. A failed/uninitialized Lisp wrapper has no handle and signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup invalidates every identity; outside a session this query signals NATIVE-ERROR." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:handler-alive-p handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is an EVENT-HANDLER or a WINDOW subclass.")) ("Returns" (:p "T if native identity exists and is not being deleted; NIL for stale/destroyed identity during an active session.")) ("Description" (:p "Observe native lifetime without dereferencing dead windows. Native weak tracking makes window destruction safe even with event processing disabled. A failed/uninitialized Lisp wrapper has no handle and signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup invalidates every identity; outside a session this query signals NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR, including after cleanup. Invalid/stale native handles signal NATIVE-ERROR except HANDLER-ALIVE-P, which returns NIL for destroyed/unknown IDs during an active session. Unsupported Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Generic observer/contextual bindings cover built-ins and registered command/notify names, including on the borrowed application view. Arbitrary native classes, validated OS session delivery, pushed handler chains and native virtual overrides remain unbound. Pending/scheduled native deletion of a window receiver/owning frame or any native ancestor makes that resource unavailable; IsBeingDeleted alone is not the liveness test.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge lifetime predicate using native registries and wxWeakRef<wxWindow>/IsBeingDeleted; no standalone public wxWeakRef wrapper."))))
(:entry "api/handler-enabled-p" :names ("handler-enabled-p" "(setf handler-enabled-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or write the native wxEvtHandler event-processing flag. Separate from window ENABLED-P/input state: disabled handlers can skip callbacks without greying the control. Native propagation rules still apply. Scoped contexts support Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto; arbitrary pushed handlers remain unbound. In standalone chains this affects only the node itself, not processing by following nodes." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:handler-enabled-p handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is an EVENT-HANDLER or WINDOW subclass; SETF VALUE is a generalized boolean.")) ("Returns" (:p "T/NIL for the own native handler flag; SETF returns the supplied value.")) ("Description" (:p "Read or write the native wxEvtHandler event-processing flag. Separate from window ENABLED-P/input state: disabled handlers can skip callbacks without greying the control. Native propagation rules still apply. Scoped contexts support Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto; arbitrary pushed handlers remain unbound. In standalone chains this affects only the node itself, not processing by following nodes.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR, including after cleanup. Invalid/stale native handles signal NATIVE-ERROR except HANDLER-ALIVE-P, which returns NIL for destroyed/unknown IDs during an active session. Unsupported Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Generic observer/contextual bindings cover built-ins and registered command/notify names, including on the borrowed application view. Arbitrary native classes, validated OS session delivery, pushed handler chains and native virtual overrides remain unbound. On APPLICATION-HANDLER this is the real wxApp flag; disabling can delay app-queued work and deferred disposal until restoration or cleanup.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::GetEvtHandlerEnabled / SetEvtHandlerEnabled (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:handler-enabled-p handler) value)") (:p "Normalize a generalized boolean to the native flag and return the original supplied value. No command event is synthesized."))))
(:entry "api/handler-unlinked-p" :names ("handler-unlinked-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native IsUnlinked without changing native ownership or queue membership. An unlinked wrapper remains strongly registered and its native object remains session-owned until explicit destruction or cleanup." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:handler-unlinked-p handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live owned standalone EVENT-HANDLER/subclass.")) ("Returns" (:p "T when both native next/previous links are NIL; otherwise NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native IsUnlinked without changing native ownership or queue membership. An unlinked wrapper remains strongly registered and its native object remains session-owned until explicit destruction or cleanup.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and valid owned standalone handle; reads may run inside callbacks. Borrowed window/application and stale/pending handles reject. No borrowed native stack or pointer access. Attached owned pushed handlers are supported by this query and return NIL; generic peer operations remain excluded.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::IsUnlinked (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/hide-grid-cell-edit-control" :names ("hide-grid-cell-edit-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:hide-grid-cell-edit-control grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::HideCellEditControl"))))
(:entry "api/hide-stc-lines" :names ("hide-stc-lines") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native HideLines. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:hide-stc-lines control first last)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; FIRST native line.; LAST native line.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native HideLines. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/idle-mode" :names ("idle-mode" "(setf idle-mode)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/change process-wide wxIdleEvent GetMode/SetMode in the managed GUI session. Save/restore pre-session native policy at finish, including error cleanup. This is not a synthetic event field or effective per-window eligibility query." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:idle-mode )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No reader arguments. SETF VALUE is :ALL or :SPECIFIED.")) ("Returns" (:p "Current native automatic-window idle policy; SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/change process-wide wxIdleEvent GetMode/SetMode in the managed GUI session. Save/restore pre-session native policy at finish, including error cleanup. This is not a synthetic event field or effective per-window eligibility query.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required. Unknown mode rejects. Automatic delivery also depends on window opt-in/visibility/native rules; explicit synthetic idle bypasses this policy. No worker policy access or arbitrary native event loop is supplied.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxIdleEvent::GetMode / SetMode and wxIdleMode :ALL/:SPECIFIED mapping (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:idle-mode) :specified)") (:p "Change global automatic idle policy, returning VALUE. Restore temporary within-session changes with UNWIND-PROTECT; native finish restores the pre-session mode."))))
(:entry "api/image" :names ("image") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Session-owned wxImage. Construct with WIDTH/HEIGHT and copied RGB/optional ALPHA, local PNG PATH, or SOURCE image/bitmap. Native-backed subclass initargs/AFTER hooks and rollback." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:image")) ("Arguments" (:p "Session-owned wxImage. Construct with WIDTH/HEIGHT and copied RGB/optional ALPHA, local PNG PATH, or SOURCE image/bitmap. Native-backed subclass initargs/AFTER hooks and rollback.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Session-owned wxImage. Construct with WIDTH/HEIGHT and copied RGB/optional ALPHA, local PNG PATH, or SOURCE image/bitmap. Native-backed subclass initargs/AFTER hooks and rollback.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:image :width 32 :height 32 :rgb rgb :alpha alpha)") (:p "Concrete native-backed resource/control; subclass initargs/defaults/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/image-alive-p" :names ("image-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query active-session image validity; NIL after explicit disposal." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:image-alive-p object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Query active-session image validity; NIL after explicit disposal.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/image-alpha" :names ("image-alpha" "(setf image-alpha)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy width*height opacity bytes,255 if no channel. SETF copies a vector or NIL to clear the channel." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:image-alpha object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image")) ("Returns" (:p "A fresh simple unsigned-byte8 vector.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy width*height opacity bytes,255 if no channel. SETF copies a vector or NIL to clear the channel.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:image-alpha object) value)") (:p "Invoke the native mutation with copied/checked data; return supplied value. See supported scope."))))
(:entry "api/image-alpha-p" :names ("image-alpha-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query native HasAlpha; absence differs from an explicit all-opaque channel." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:image-alpha-p object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized boolean.")) ("Description" (:p "Query native HasAlpha; absence differs from an explicit all-opaque channel.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/image-pixel" :names ("image-pixel" "(setf image-pixel)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write one zero-based pixel; SETF accepts four bytes, allocating alpha for nonopaque values if absent." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:image-pixel object x y)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image x y")) ("Returns" (:p "Four-element (R G B A) byte list.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write one zero-based pixel; SETF accepts four bytes, allocating alpha for nonopaque values if absent.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:image-pixel image x y) value)") (:p "Invoke the native mutation with copied/checked data; return supplied value. See supported scope."))))
(:entry "api/image-rgb" :names ("image-rgb" "(setf image-rgb)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy interleaved RGB bytes; SETF copies an exact width*height*3 vector into native image data." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:image-rgb object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image")) ("Returns" (:p "A fresh simple unsigned-byte8 vector.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy interleaved RGB bytes; SETF copies an exact width*height*3 vector into native image data.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:image-rgb object) value)") (:p "Invoke the native mutation with copied/checked data; return supplied value. See supported scope."))))
(:entry "api/image-size" :names ("image-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native wxImage dimensions." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:image-size object)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image")) ("Returns" (:p "(width height) in pixels.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native wxImage dimensions.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/initialize-splitter" :names ("initialize-splitter") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Initialize one visible attached pane." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:initialize-splitter splitter pane)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Empty SPLITTER-WINDOW and unattached PANEL child.")) ("Returns" (:p "PANE.")) ("Description" (:p "Initialize one visible attached pane.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and quiescent structural boundary or safe owner-bound deferred action; callback use rejects. Native-backed SPLITTER-WINDOW and fully initialized direct unsizered PANEL children. Canonical roots precede native sizing/focus work; old/new/attached pane and ancestor lifetime guards apply. Retained hidden panels remain native children and die with parent. No raw adoption, dynamic event/virtual hooks or editor layout abstraction. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md and docs/SPLITTER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow::Initialize, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/insert-grid-columns" :names ("insert-grid-columns") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:insert-grid-columns grid position &optional count)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, POSITION, optional COUNT (default1), each count1..256.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::InsertCols"))))
(:entry "api/insert-grid-rows" :names ("insert-grid-rows") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:insert-grid-rows grid position &optional count)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, POSITION, optional COUNT (default1), each count1..256.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Change owned native string-table dimensions. Result axes0..256, product at most16384; constructor remains nonempty. Safe structural phase required; active editor rejects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::InsertRows"))))
(:entry "api/insert-list-column" :names ("insert-list-column") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Insert left-aligned heading at zero-based index while item count0. NUL-free heading<=4096UTF8 bytes, width1..10000 pixels, max64 columns. Return CONTROL." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:insert-list-column control index label &key (width 120))")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control index label &key (width120))")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Insert left-aligned heading at zero-based index while item count0. NUL-free heading<=4096UTF8 bytes, width1..10000 pixels, max64 columns. Return CONTROL.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::InsertColumn"))))
(:entry "api/insert-notebook-page" :names ("insert-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Insert and publish canonical page. Native selection may notify/veto under port rules; first page becomes selected. No automatic reparenting." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:insert-notebook-page book page index &key (label \"\") select)")) ("Arguments" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK, fully initialized unattached unsizered direct PANEL child, insertion INDEX0..count, NUL-free caption<=4096UTF8 bytes, generalized SELECT.")) ("Returns" (:p "Supplied PAGE.")) ("Description" (:p "Insert and publish canonical page. Native selection may notify/veto under port rules; first page becomes selected. No automatic reparenting.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::InsertPage, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/item-count" :names ("item-count" "(setf item-count)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native item count. RADIO-BOX and COMBO-BOX retain their fixed constructor choices. LIST-CONTROL returns native report row count; SETF supports only virtual lists with columns and0..10000000 rows, no per-row allocation; returns value." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:item-count control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL is a live LIST-BOX, RADIO-BOX or COMBO-BOX.")) ("Returns" (:p "Nonnegative native item count.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native item count. RADIO-BOX and COMBO-BOX retain their fixed constructor choices. LIST-CONTROL returns native report row count; SETF supports only virtual lists with columns and0..10000000 rows, no per-row allocation; returns value.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and native lifetime checks. LIST-BOX supports mutable text items; RADIO-BOX has fixed2..64 choices; COMBO-BOX has fixed0..256 unsorted nonempty choices. No generic receiver fallback or arbitrary native item-container access. Invalid indices/types/handles signal. See docs/LIST-BOX.md, docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md and docs/COMBO-BOXES.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxItemContainerImmutable/wxListBox::GetCount (wxWidgets 3.2.12). wxRadioBox::GetCount. wxComboBox::GetCount.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:item-count control) value)") (:p "Use generic SETF with validated arguments; report/tree mutations reject active providers/callbacks and native lifetime violations. ITEM-COUNT SETF is virtual LIST-CONTROL only."))))
(:entry "api/item-text" :names ("item-text" "(setf item-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy native item text into an independent Lisp string. LIST-BOX and COMBO-BOX use explicit UTF-8 length; RADIO-BOX uses NUL-terminated UTF-8 with NUL-free constructor strings and native mnemonic normalization. Index is not durable identity." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:item-text control index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL is a live LIST-BOX, RADIO-BOX or COMBO-BOX; INDEX is an existing zero-based signed-int index.")) ("Returns" (:p "Independent Lisp string of native item text.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy native item text into an independent Lisp string. LIST-BOX and COMBO-BOX use explicit UTF-8 length; RADIO-BOX uses NUL-terminated UTF-8 with NUL-free constructor strings and native mnemonic normalization. Index is not durable identity.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and native lifetime checks. LIST-BOX supports mutable text items; RADIO-BOX has fixed2..64 choices; COMBO-BOX has fixed0..256 unsorted nonempty choices. No generic receiver fallback or arbitrary native item-container access. Invalid indices/types/handles signal. See docs/LIST-BOX.md, docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md and docs/COMBO-BOXES.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxItemContainerImmutable/wxListBox::GetString/SetString (wxWidgets 3.2.12). wxRadioBox::GetString (no SetString binding). wxComboBox::GetString (no writer).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:item-text control index) value)") (:p "LIST-BOX only. VALUE is a string without NUL, empty allowed. Silent rename preserves selection index and returns the supplied string. No sorting or item-data adoption. RADIO-BOX has no writer method. COMBO-BOX also has no writer."))))
(:entry "api/label" :names ("label") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxStaticText; label operations specialize on this class." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:label")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass: WXLAMBDA:WINDOW.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance of this class or a subclass (WINDOW itself is abstract).")) ("Description" (:p "CLOS wrapper for wxStaticText; label operations specialize on this class.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Construction requires an active main-thread application session. Concrete classes create their native widgets in inherited INITIALIZE-INSTANCE methods; subclass AFTER hooks can use them. Native handles cannot be supplied as initargs. Lisp subclassing does not imply native C++ virtual callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStaticText (wxWidgets 3.2); this is a Lisp wrapper, not a native subclass.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:label :parent parent :label \"\")") (:p "PARENT is required; LABEL defaults to an empty string. Class :DEFAULT-INITARGS and custom slot initargs are honored; native creation precedes subclass AFTER hooks."))))
(:entry "api/label-text" :names ("label-text" "(setf label-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read raw label text including mnemonic/accelerator syntax. Menu item reads preserve the raw label, not stripped display text." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:label-text control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "RECEIVER is live static text, TOGGLE-BUTTON or MENU-ITEM; separator reads are empty, separator writes reject.")) ("Returns" (:p "An independent Lisp string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read raw label text including mnemonic/accelerator syntax. Menu item reads preserve the raw label, not stripped display text.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxControl::GetLabel/SetLabel (wxStaticText and wxToggleButton); wxMenuItem::GetItemLabel/SetItemLabel (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:label-text label) new-value)") (:p "Assign static text and relayout its parent if necessary. Writers are generic functions with VALUE first, followed by the receiver. Menu item labels must be nonempty Unicode strings without NUL; separators reject. Scalar changes are allowed in callbacks and do not synthesize menu commands. TOGGLE-BUTTON requires a NUL-free string, silently preserves checked state, rejects same-button callback writes and may need explicit relayout for native best-size changes. See docs/TOGGLE-BUTTONS.md."))))
(:entry "api/layout-window" :names ("layout-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Recompute the window sizer layout, including after batching label changes. Native success boolean is not exposed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:layout-window window)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is a live window.")) ("Returns" (:p "WINDOW.")) ("Description" (:p "Recompute the window sizer layout, including after batching label changes. Native success boolean is not exposed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Layout"))))
(:entry "api/list-box" :names ("list-box") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Single-selection unsorted list with mutable UTF-8 text items and selection/activation events." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:list-box")) ("Arguments" (:p "Subclass of WINDOW; native wxListBox with wxLB_SINGLE.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed list widget.")) ("Description" (:p "Single-selection unsorted list with mutable UTF-8 text items and selection/activation events.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session, LIST-BOX receivers only. Unsorted single selection, native-owned text values; no item client data, multi-selection, sorting, arbitrary styles, virtual list/data-view/tree support. Invalid indices/types/handles signal.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListBox / wxItemContainer (wxWidgets 3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:list-box :parent parent :items nil :selection nil)") (:p "PARENT required; ITEMS finite proper string list defaults empty, SELECTION existing index or NIL defaults none. Empty/duplicate items valid; NUL rejects. Subclass slots/default initargs/AFTER hooks and managed failure cleanup apply."))))
(:entry "api/list-column-count" :names ("list-column-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Return current native column count0..64." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:list-column-count control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Return current native column count0..64.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::GetColumnCount"))))
(:entry "api/list-column-label" :names ("list-column-label" "(setf list-column-label)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied heading or silently set NUL-free heading<=4096UTF8 bytes; SETF returns value." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:list-column-label control index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control index); SETF(value control index)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Read copied heading or silently set NUL-free heading<=4096UTF8 bytes; SETF returns value.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::GetColumn / SetColumn")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:list-column-label control index) value)") (:p "Use generic SETF with validated arguments; report/tree mutations reject active providers/callbacks and native lifetime violations. ITEM-COUNT SETF is virtual LIST-CONTROL only."))))
(:entry "api/list-column-width" :names ("list-column-width" "(setf list-column-width)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native pixel width or set1..10000 pixels; SETF returns value." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:list-column-width control index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control index); SETF(value control index)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native pixel width or set1..10000 pixels; SETF returns value.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::GetColumnWidth / SetColumnWidth")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:list-column-width control index) value)") (:p "Use generic SETF with validated arguments; report/tree mutations reject active providers/callbacks and native lifetime violations. ITEM-COUNT SETF is virtual LIST-CONTROL only."))))
(:entry "api/list-control" :names ("list-control") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "A managed wxListCtrl report, fixed single selection; direct subclasses retain native-backed construction. Virtual lists support only registered frame/panel/scroll/drawing/web/notebook/AUI/splitter ancestor chains." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:list-control :parent parent :virtual-p nil :item-text-function nil)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Native-backed WINDOW with :parent, :virtual-p NIL, :item-text-function NIL.")) ("Returns" (:p "Instance.")) ("Description" (:p "A managed wxListCtrl report, fixed single selection; direct subclasses retain native-backed construction. Virtual lists support only registered frame/panel/scroll/drawing/web/notebook/AUI/splitter ancestor chains.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:list-control :parent parent :virtual-p nil :item-text-function nil)") (:p "Direct CLOS subclasses and native-ready AFTER hooks supported; managed initialization failure destroys native identity and reaps provider roots."))))
(:entry "api/list-item-text" :names ("list-item-text" "(setf list-item-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read copied native cell text. In virtual lists actual OnGetItemText calls this generic for subclasses or constructor function; provider must return NUL-free text<=65536UTF8 bytes, may read data and must not mutate source/ancestors or enter native loops. Errors/nonlocal exits contained at callback boundary. SETF silently writes stored lists only." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:list-item-text control row column)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control row column); SETF(value control row column)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Read copied native cell text. In virtual lists actual OnGetItemText calls this generic for subclasses or constructor function; provider must return NUL-free text<=65536UTF8 bytes, may read data and must not mutate source/ancestors or enter native loops. Errors/nonlocal exits contained at callback boundary. SETF silently writes stored lists only.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::GetItemText / SetItem / OnGetItemText")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:list-item-text control row column) value)") (:p "Use generic SETF with validated arguments; report/tree mutations reject active providers/callbacks and native lifetime violations. ITEM-COUNT SETF is virtual LIST-CONTROL only."))))
(:entry "api/list-virtual-p" :names ("list-virtual-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Return whether fixed native wxLC_VIRTUAL mode is enabled." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:list-virtual-p control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Return whether fixed native wxLC_VIRTUAL mode is enabled.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::IsVirtual"))))
(:entry "api/load-native-library" :names ("load-native-library") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Load the native bridge once. An explicit path supports packaged applications without consulting ASDF." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:load-native-library &optional path)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Optional PATH names the bridge; default searches build/ and then the system loader.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after successful load and ABI verification.")) ("Description" (:p "Load the native bridge once. An explicit path supports packaged applications without consulting ASDF.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "May be used before a GUI session. Loader and ABI failures signal Lisp errors.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge-specific ABI loader."))))
(:entry "api/main-loop-running-p" :names ("main-loop-running-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxAppConsole::IsMainLoopRunning. False during standalone pending dispatch, standalone GUI polling and the cooperative application REPL; those modes can still deliver callbacks. This is a main-loop query, not a callback-safety predicate." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:main-loop-running-p )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "T while the native main loop runs, otherwise NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Query wxAppConsole::IsMainLoopRunning. False during standalone pending dispatch, standalone GUI polling and the cooperative application REPL; those modes can still deliver callbacks. This is a main-loop query, not a callback-safety predicate.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session; use before startup or after cleanup signals NATIVE-ERROR. This API is scoped to the bridge application, not arbitrary wxApp instances.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAppConsole::IsMainLoopRunning (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/make-activity-indicator" :names ("make-activity-indicator") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. Initially stopped unless RUNNING-P is non-NIL. Animation is feedback, not background work." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-activity-indicator parent &rest initargs &key (class 'activity-indicator) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT and forwarded :running-p/:class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New ACTIVITY-INDICATOR or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. Initially stopped unless RUNNING-P is non-NIL. Animation is feedback, not background work.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread live parent and active GUI session; native default style/geometry. See docs/ACTIVITY-INDICATORS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxActivityIndicator::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-aui-notebook" :names ("make-aui-notebook") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-aui-notebook parent &rest initargs &key (class 'aui-notebook) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Live parent WINDOW; validated AUI-NOTEBOOK :class and forwarded subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New AUI-NOTEBOOK or subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-bitmap" :names ("make-bitmap") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a native display bitmap from IMAGE, with validated CLASS and forwarded subclass initargs. SOURCE copies an existing bitmap value or native static display GetBitmap through managed CLOS construction." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-bitmap &rest initargs &key (class 'bitmap) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Exactly one IMAGE or SOURCE; SOURCE is BITMAP or STATIC-BITMAP. CLASS and subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new BITMAP.")) ("Description" (:p "Construct a native display bitmap from IMAGE, with validated CLASS and forwarded subclass initargs. SOURCE copies an existing bitmap value or native static display GetBitmap through managed CLOS construction.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-button" :names ("make-button") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a text button with replaceable click handler support." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-button parent &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:button) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT; optional LABEL string (default Button). :CLASS selects the corresponding concrete wrapper class or a subclass (symbol or class object). Additional initargs are forwarded to MAKE-INSTANCE.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a text button with replaceable click handler support.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxButton constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-checkbox" :names ("make-checkbox") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a two-state checkbox with initial boolean state." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-checkbox parent &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:checkbox) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT; LABEL string and CHECKED generalized boolean. :CLASS selects the corresponding concrete wrapper class or a subclass (symbol or class object). Additional initargs are forwarded to MAKE-INSTANCE.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a two-state checkbox with initial boolean state.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCheckBox constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-choice" :names ("make-choice") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a dropdown with copied item strings; NIL means no selection." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-choice parent &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:choice) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT; ITEMS list of strings; SELECTION zero-based index or NIL. :CLASS selects the corresponding concrete wrapper class or a subclass (symbol or class object). Additional initargs are forwarded to MAKE-INSTANCE.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a dropdown with copied item strings; NIL means no selection.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxChoice constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-column" :names ("make-column") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Attach a parent-owned vertical box sizer. Standalone nested sizer objects are not exposed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-column parent)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT is a live window without a sizer.")) ("Returns" (:p "PARENT.")) ("Description" (:p "Attach a parent-owned vertical box sizer. Standalone nested sizer objects are not exposed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBoxSizer / wxWindow::SetSizer"))))
(:entry "api/make-combo-box" :names ("make-combo-box") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Editable single-line fixed unsorted choices with generic TEXT/SETF, SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT. Native CmpNoCase duplicate/case-only choices reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-combo-box parent &rest initargs &key (class 'combo-box) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT (or :parent for MAKE-INSTANCE); :items finite proper list0..256 nonempty single-line strings, :value default empty, :selection NIL/index. A non-NIL index and nonempty initial value conflict. Factory accepts :class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New COMBO-BOX or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Editable single-line fixed unsorted choices with generic TEXT/SETF, SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT. Native CmpNoCase duplicate/case-only choices reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and native lifetime guards. Strings reject NUL/CR/LF. No readonly/sort/item-mutation/text-position API, native adoption or full class parity. See docs/COMBO-BOXES.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxComboBox::Create/GetSelection/SetSelection/GetCount/GetString; wxTextEntry::GetValue/ChangeValue (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-date-picker" :names ("make-date-picker") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. DATE defaults to (2000 1 1), not today." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-date-picker parent &rest initargs &key (class 'date-picker) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT and forwarded :date/:class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New DATE-PICKER or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. DATE defaults to (2000 1 1), not today.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session, live native lifetime, Gregorian dates1900..2100 and representable native local calendar dates only. Fixed inclusive1900-01-01..2100-12-31 range; native range/value readback required. Default native date editor style; no NIL/time/timezone/range/style APIs. Input callback/composite-child/propagation guards and early generic Destroy suppression. Requires core/base/adv, wxUSE_DATEPICKCTRL and wxUSE_DATETIME. See docs/DATE-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDatePickerCtrl::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-drawing-canvas" :names ("make-drawing-canvas") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory for the retained canvas. Use existing row/column layout, typically proportion1 and expandT." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-drawing-canvas parent &rest initargs &key (class 'drawing-canvas) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT and forwarded :content/:class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New DRAWING-CANVAS or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory for the retained canvas. Use existing row/column layout, typically proportion1 and expandT.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session, live managed WINDOW parent, no DC/native object adoption or Lisp paint callback. Native scene staging, rendering/export and Input lifetime/reentry guards; writes/export reject event callbacks. Copied bounded data only; font/paint/DPI appearance is native. See docs/DRAWING-CANVAS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxPanel::Create with private retained paint/size handlers, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-event" :names ("make-event") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin class-validating CLOS factory with forwarded subclass initargs. Initial ID -1 remains reserved. Clone construction detaches origin and preserves native source state; factories reject explicit payload overrides while inherited defaults do not replace cloned values." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-event &rest initargs &key (class 'owned-event) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Keyword initargs: CLASS defaults OWNED-EVENT; KIND defaults :CLICK. ID/TEXT/INTEGER/CHECKED-P/SELECTION/CAN-VETO-P/VETOED-P/LOGGING-OFF-P match synthetic payload rules. Optional CLONE-FROM accepts a live owned event/current context. Optional EXTRA-LONG accepts signed native LONG only for command/notify construction; explicit clone overrides reject. Optional MORE-REQUESTED-P applies only to idle construction; explicitly supplied non-idle values (including NIL) reject/rollback. Keyword synthetic queue/process do not add this option.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new OWNED-EVENT or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin class-validating CLOS factory with forwarded subclass initargs. Initial ID -1 remains reserved. Clone construction detaches origin and preserves native source state; factories reject explicit payload overrides while inherited defaults do not replace cloned values.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required. Unknown/wrong-family options and invalid class construction reject. No arbitrary native class or raw handle. Explicit DESTROY-EVENT or session cleanup owns native lifetime. Notebook native page events cannot be synthesized, queued, processed as owned events or contextually cloned in ABI37. ABI38 simple listbox command kinds support owned/synthetic dispatch and text/selection payloads; no automatic list-model mutation. Derived tree selection kinds cannot be synthesized/owned/cloned in ABI39.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bounded native event constructors / wxEvent::Clone (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/make-event-handler" :names ("make-event-handler") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory. Rejects WINDOW subclasses and non-handler classes before construction; no parent or native-enabled initarg is provided." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-event-handler &rest initargs &key (class 'event-handler) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Keyword :CLASS is an EVENT-HANDLER subclass symbol or class object, default EVENT-HANDLER. Additional initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new owned standalone handler instance of CLASS.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory. Rejects WINDOW subclasses and non-handler classes before construction; no parent or native-enabled initarg is provided.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR, including after cleanup. Invalid/stale native handles signal NATIVE-ERROR except HANDLER-ALIVE-P, which returns NIL for destroyed/unknown IDs during an active session. Unsupported Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Generic observer/contextual bindings cover built-ins and registered command/notify names, including on the borrowed application view. Arbitrary native classes, validated OS session delivery, pushed handler chains and native virtual overrides remain unbound.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::wxEvtHandler (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/make-file-dialog" :names ("make-file-dialog") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with same backend, defaults, validation, lifetime and rollback as FILE-DIALOG." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-file-dialog &rest initargs &key (class 'file-dialog) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Keyword-only constructor initargs and validated :CLASS(default FILE-DIALOG); subclass initargs forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New selected concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with same backend, defaults, validation, lifetime and rollback as FILE-DIALOG.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGenericFileDialog; bounded equivalent wxFileDialog public surface constructor."))))
(:entry "api/make-frame" :names ("make-frame") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a top-level frame; native ID and style options use defaults." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-frame &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:frame) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "TITLE string; positive WIDTH and HEIGHT (defaults 480 and 240). :CLASS selects the corresponding concrete wrapper class or a subclass (symbol or class object). Additional initargs are forwarded to MAKE-INSTANCE.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a top-level frame; native ID and style options use defaults.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxFrame constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-gauge" :names ("make-gauge") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated GAUGE subclass support. Same construction defaults and restrictions as GAUGE." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-gauge parent &rest initargs &key (class 'gauge) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT is a WINDOW; :CLASS defaults to GAUGE. :RANGE, :VALUE, :ORIENTATION and subclass initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new GAUGE instance of CLASS.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated GAUGE subclass support. Same construction defaults and restrictions as GAUGE.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires a live gauge in an active main-thread GUI session. Stale/destroyed handles, native type errors and values above the range signal NATIVE-ERROR; wrong Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Numeric arguments must fit signed 32-bit integers; invalid Lisp types/ranges signal TYPE-ERROR. No command events or native virtual overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGauge constructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/make-grid" :names ("make-grid") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory; defaults10x5 editable, fixed shape and default native styles/selection." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-grid parent &rest initargs &key (class 'grid) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Live PARENT WINDOW, validated :class GRID subclass and forwarded constructor/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New GRID or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory; defaults10x5 editable, fixed shape and default native styles/selection.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active GUI session and checked native WINDOW lifetime. All writers reject Lisp callbacks and any enabled native cell editor; defer callback work and finish/cancel native edits first. Readers report committed table state. Input operation/composite child TEXT/BUTTON guards preserve owner/ancestor lifetime and native-entry isolation; early Destroy suppresses child input teardown. Selected native grid events, bounded row/column dimension changes, cursor/selection requests and editor operations are documented in docs/GRID-EDITING.md. No table/editor/renderer adoption or spreadsheet evaluation. See docs/GRID.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::Create/CreateGrid, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-image" :names ("make-image") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a native image or subclass; RGB defaults black, alpha absent,1..4096 pixel axes. PATH is bounded PNG only. SOURCE image requires destination size and native nearest/high scaling; SOURCE bitmap retains backing pixel size." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-image &rest initargs &key (class 'image) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "&rest initargs &key class width height rgb alpha path source quality")) ("Returns" (:p "A new IMAGE.")) ("Description" (:p "Construct a native image or subclass; RGB defaults black, alpha absent,1..4096 pixel axes. PATH is bounded PNG only. SOURCE image requires destination size and native nearest/high scaling; SOURCE bitmap retains backing pixel size.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-label" :names ("make-label") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create static text; wxWidgets label/mnemonic syntax is retained." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-label parent &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:label) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT; optional LABEL string. :CLASS selects the corresponding concrete wrapper class or a subclass (symbol or class object). Additional initargs are forwarded to MAKE-INSTANCE.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create static text; wxWidgets label/mnemonic syntax is retained.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStaticText constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-list-box" :names ("make-list-box") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin validated CLOS factory; unsorted single selection only." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-list-box parent &rest initargs &key (class 'list-box) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT window; :ITEMS string list, :SELECTION index/NIL, :CLASS LIST-BOX/subclass, forwarded initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed LIST-BOX/subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin validated CLOS factory; unsorted single selection only.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session, LIST-BOX receivers only. Unsorted single selection, native-owned text values; no item client data, multi-selection, sorting, arbitrary styles, virtual list/data-view/tree support. Invalid indices/types/handles signal.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListBox constructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-list-control" :names ("make-list-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin checked CLOS factory; ITEM-TEXT-FUNCTION requires virtual mode and receives (control row column)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-list-control parent &rest initargs &key (class 'list-control) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(parent &key class virtual-p item-text-function &allow-other-keys)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin checked CLOS factory; ITEM-TEXT-FUNCTION requires virtual mode and receives (control row column).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::wxListCtrl"))))
(:entry "api/make-menu" :names ("make-menu") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated subclass support; same ownership, defaults and validation as MENU." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-menu bar &rest initargs &key (class 'menu) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU-BAR is live; :CLASS defaults to MENU. Remaining constructor and subclass initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New instance of the selected concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated subclass support; same ownership, defaults and validation as MENU.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenu and wxMenuBar::Append"))))
(:entry "api/make-menu-bar" :names ("make-menu-bar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated subclass support; same ownership, defaults and validation as MENU-BAR." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-menu-bar frame &rest initargs &key (class 'menu-bar) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME is live; :CLASS defaults to MENU-BAR. Remaining constructor and subclass initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New instance of the selected concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated subclass support; same ownership, defaults and validation as MENU-BAR.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuBar and wxFrame::SetMenuBar"))))
(:entry "api/make-menu-item" :names ("make-menu-item") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated subclass support; same ownership, defaults and validation as MENU-ITEM." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-menu-item menu &rest initargs &key (class 'menu-item) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU is live; :CLASS defaults to MENU-ITEM. Remaining constructor and subclass initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New instance of the selected concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with validated subclass support; same ownership, defaults and validation as MENU-ITEM.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuItem and wxMenu::Append"))))
(:entry "api/make-message-dialog" :names ("make-message-dialog") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with same backend, defaults, validation, lifetime and rollback as MESSAGE-DIALOG." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-message-dialog &rest initargs &key (class 'message-dialog) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Keyword-only constructor initargs and validated :CLASS(default MESSAGE-DIALOG); subclass initargs forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New selected concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with same backend, defaults, validation, lifetime and rollback as MESSAGE-DIALOG.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGenericMessageDialog; bounded equivalent wxMessageDialog public surface constructor."))))
(:entry "api/make-notebook" :names ("make-notebook") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin validated CLOS factory with required parent and native defaults." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-notebook parent &rest initargs &key (class 'notebook) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT window; :CLASS defaults NOTEBOOK, remaining initargs forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed NOTEBOOK/subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin validated CLOS factory with required parent and native defaults.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; NOTEBOOK receivers and fixed setup-time PANEL pages only. Invalid handles/indices/ownership signal. No removal, reordering, reparenting, icons, arbitrary styles or other book controls.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxNotebook constructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-panel" :names ("make-panel") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a child panel." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-panel parent &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:panel) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT is a live window. :CLASS selects the corresponding concrete wrapper class or a subclass (symbol or class object). Additional initargs are forwarded to MAKE-INSTANCE.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin factory over MAKE-INSTANCE; validates :CLASS against the factory's widget kind and forwards initargs. Create a child panel.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxPanel constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-radio-box" :names ("make-radio-box") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-radio-box parent &rest initargs &key (class 'radio-box) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT (or :parent for MAKE-INSTANCE), :items proper list2..64 NUL-free strings, :label string default empty, :selection index default0, :orientation :vertical/:horizontal, subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed RADIO-BOX or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed2..64 choices, mandatory valid zero-based selection, one row/column orientation. Active GUI session/native lifetime checks for widget operations; no standalone radio buttons, item mutation or full native parity. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxRadioBox::Create, wxRA_SPECIFY_COLS/ROWS (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-row" :names ("make-row") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Attach a parent-owned horizontal box sizer. Standalone nested sizer objects are not exposed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-row parent)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT is a live window without a sizer.")) ("Returns" (:p "PARENT.")) ("Description" (:p "Attach a parent-owned horizontal box sizer. Standalone nested sizer objects are not exposed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBoxSizer / wxWindow::SetSizer"))))
(:entry "api/make-scrolled-panel" :names ("make-scrolled-panel") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "PARENT plus :class/:scroll-rate and subclass initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-scrolled-panel parent &rest initargs &key (class 'scrolled-panel) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT plus :class/:scroll-rate and subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New SCROLLED-PANEL or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "PARENT plus :class/:scroll-rate and subclass initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. No callback-time fit/rate/position changes: defer via owner-bound UI action. Supported extent<=1000000 pixels/axis checked before explicit mutation, not globally enforced on inherited/native layout. Private native scroll helper stays owned; managed handler-stack APIs reject for this class. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxScrolled::Create (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-search-control" :names ("make-search-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. Query defaults empty; hint defaults literal Search. Native icon display and Enter/empty-query/cancel behavior are not normalized." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-search-control parent &rest initargs &key (class 'search-control) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT and forwarded :value/:hint/:class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New SEARCH-CONTROL or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. Query defaults empty; hint defaults literal Search. Native icon display and Enter/empty-query/cancel behavior are not normalized.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and live WINDOW lifetime. Editable single-line copied UTF-8 query/hint, NUL/CR/LF rejected, empty accepted. Fixed native style/icon requests; actual native search/cancel/Enter/default-clear/text event behavior varies by port. Shared Input actual/propagated/composite callbacks and early Destroy guards. No style/menu/button visibility/editing/raw-resource APIs. See docs/SEARCH-CONTROLS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSearchCtrl::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-single-choice-dialog" :names ("make-single-choice-dialog") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with the same defaults, validation, ownership and rollback as SINGLE-CHOICE-DIALOG." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-single-choice-dialog &rest initargs &key (class 'single-choice-dialog) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Keyword-only constructor initargs; :CLASS defaults to SINGLE-CHOICE-DIALOG. Remaining subclass initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New instance of the validated concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with the same defaults, validation, ownership and rollback as SINGLE-CHOICE-DIALOG.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSingleChoiceDialog constructor."))))
(:entry "api/make-slider" :names ("make-slider") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "PARENT plus :class/:minimum/:maximum/:value/:orientation and subclass initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-slider parent &rest initargs &key (class 'slider) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT plus :class/:minimum/:maximum/:value/:orientation and subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New SLIDER/subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "PARENT plus :class/:minimum/:maximum/:value/:orientation and subclass initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSlider::Create (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-spin-control" :names ("make-spin-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "PARENT plus :class/:minimum/:maximum/:value and subclass initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-spin-control parent &rest initargs &key (class 'spin-control) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT plus :class/:minimum/:maximum/:value and subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New SPIN-CONTROL/subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "PARENT plus :class/:minimum/:maximum/:value and subclass initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSpinCtrl::Create (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-splitter-window" :names ("make-splitter-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "PARENT and forwarded initargs, including validated :class subclass." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-splitter-window parent &rest initargs &key (class 'splitter-window) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT and forwarded initargs, including validated :class subclass.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "PARENT and forwarded initargs, including validated :class subclass.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-static-bitmap" :names ("make-static-bitmap") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed wxStaticBitmap constructor with validated CLASS and forwarded initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-static-bitmap parent bitmap &rest initargs &key (class 'static-bitmap) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "parent bitmap &rest initargs &key class")) ("Returns" (:p "A new STATIC-BITMAP.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed wxStaticBitmap constructor with validated CLASS and forwarded initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-status-bar" :names ("make-status-bar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "FRAME and forwarded :fields/:class initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-status-bar frame &rest initargs &key (class 'status-bar) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME and forwarded :fields/:class initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed status bar.")) ("Description" (:p "FRAME and forwarded :fields/:class initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Quiescent construction; one status bar per frame. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStatusBar / wxFrame::SetStatusBar (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-styled-text-control" :names ("make-styled-text-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-styled-text-control parent &rest initargs &key (class 'styled-text-control) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Live WINDOW parent; validated :class and forwarded :value/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL or subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-text" :names ("make-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. Construct single-line or multiline text with user editability policy. Text uses explicit UTF-8 lengths and rejects NUL." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-text parent &rest initargs &key (class 'wxlambda:text-control) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT; VALUE defaults to empty string, MULTILINE to NIL, EDITABLE-P to T. :CLASS selects TEXT-CONTROL or a subclass; remaining initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "A new Lisp object wrapping the native window handle.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory. Construct single-line or multiline text with user editability policy. Text uses explicit UTF-8 lengths and rejects NUL.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTextCtrl constructor (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/make-text-entry-dialog" :names ("make-text-entry-dialog") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with the same defaults, validation, ownership and rollback as TEXT-ENTRY-DIALOG." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-text-entry-dialog &rest initargs &key (class 'text-entry-dialog) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Keyword-only constructor initargs; :CLASS defaults to TEXT-ENTRY-DIALOG. Remaining subclass initargs are forwarded.")) ("Returns" (:p "New instance of the validated concrete subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin MAKE-INSTANCE factory with the same defaults, validation, ownership and rollback as TEXT-ENTRY-DIALOG.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTextEntryDialog constructor."))))
(:entry "api/make-time-picker" :names ("make-time-picker") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory; TIME defaults to (0 0 0)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-time-picker parent &rest initargs &key (class 'time-picker) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT and forwarded :time/:class/subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New TIME-PICKER or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory; TIME defaults to (0 0 0).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and live WINDOW lifetime. Required (hour minute second), hour0..23 and minute/second0..59, whole seconds only. Fixed local2012-01-01 native construction with component roundtrip/readback, no date/timezone/Unix/universal-time/scheduling API. Default native editor style/locale display. Input origin/composite/propagation and early Destroy guards; core/base/adv plus wxUSE_TIMEPICKCTRL/wxUSE_DATETIME required. See docs/TIME-PICKER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTimePickerCtrl::Create, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-toggle-button" :names ("make-toggle-button") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Persistent independent two-state push button. Generic CHECKED-P/SETF and LABEL-TEXT/SETF properties; BIND-EVENT :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-toggle-button parent &rest initargs &key (class 'toggle-button) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT (or :parent for MAKE-INSTANCE), :label NUL-free string default empty, :checked generalized boolean default NIL; :class and subclass initargs for factory.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed TOGGLE-BUTTON or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Persistent independent two-state push button. Generic CHECKED-P/SETF and LABEL-TEXT/SETF properties; BIND-EVENT :TOGGLE-BUTTON-CHANGE.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session, native handle/type/lifetime guards. No bitmap toggle, grouping, arbitrary styles or full class parity. Same-source value/label callback writes reject; silent other-source updates allowed. See docs/TOGGLE-BUTTONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxToggleButton::Create/GetValue/SetValue, inherited wxControl::GetLabel/SetLabel; wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/make-toolbar" :names ("make-toolbar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "FRAME and forwarded initargs, including validated :class subclass." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-toolbar frame &rest initargs &key (class 'toolbar) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME and forwarded initargs, including validated :class subclass.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed toolbar.")) ("Description" (:p "FRAME and forwarded initargs, including validated :class subclass.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Quiescent construction; one toolbar per frame. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxToolBar / wxFrame::SetToolBar (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-tree-control" :names ("make-tree-control") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin validated native-backed CLOS factory." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-tree-control parent &rest initargs &key (class 'tree-control) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT; :CLASS defaults TREE-CONTROL, forwarded initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New TREE-CONTROL/subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin validated native-backed CLOS factory.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; managed tree-control/items only. Native tokens validate owner/lifetime; no raw IDs/adoption, multiselect, item data, icons, label editing, sorting, drag/drop, virtual models or arbitrary styles. Same-tree writes and nested native loops defer during tree callbacks. wxQt tree construction is explicitly unavailable pending generation-safe asynchronous event translation.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTreeCtrl constructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/make-web-view" :names ("make-web-view") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Thin native-backed CLOS factory; initially about:blank." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:make-web-view parent &rest initargs &key (class 'web-view) &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT WINDOW; validated :class and forwarded subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New WEB-VIEW or subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Thin native-backed CLOS factory; initially about:blank.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Verified macOS wxWidgets3.2.12 WKWebView backend only. Active GUI thread/session and live WEB-VIEW WINDOW container; private browser child has no public handle. JavaScript enabled for trusted development content, not a security sandbox. Known wx native dialogs/upload/popups/printing suppressed, known permission requests denied; no complete OS WebKit security/permission policy claim. Mutations/scripts reject callbacks and protect receiver/ancestors/native reentry; use deferred actions. No managed handler stacks, native backend adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned web events. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md. Explicit URL navigation/base-URL inputs support about:blank or absolute http/https/file URLs only; native links, redirects and subresource loads are not a complete navigation sandbox. JSON script messages can originate from all frames and origins; receipt does not authenticate the sender or authorize an action. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWebView/WKWebView bounded adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12; system WebKit runtime."))))
(:entry "api/menu" :names ("menu") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Create a menu and append its raw tab label to the managed bar. Concrete subclass initargs and DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported; native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed initialization cleans newly allocated resources and descendants; it does not undo arbitrary external mutations." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "menu")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU-BAR via :PARENT and nonempty :LABEL.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Create a menu and append its raw tab label to the managed bar. Concrete subclass initargs and DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported; native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed initialization cleans newly allocated resources and descendants; it does not undo arbitrary external mutations.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenu and wxMenuBar::Append")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:menu :parent bar :label \"&File\")") (:p "Native-backed CLOS construction; ownership transfers only into the managed parent hierarchy. Labels/help are Unicode strings without NUL. Nonseparator labels must be nonempty."))))
(:entry "api/menu-bar" :names ("menu-bar") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Create and attach a frame-owned menu bar; existing native bars cannot be adopted. Concrete subclass initargs and DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported; native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed initialization cleans newly allocated resources and descendants; it does not undo arbitrary external mutations." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "menu-bar")) ("Arguments" (:p "FRAME via :PARENT; one managed bar per frame.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Create and attach a frame-owned menu bar; existing native bars cannot be adopted. Concrete subclass initargs and DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported; native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed initialization cleans newly allocated resources and descendants; it does not undo arbitrary external mutations.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuBar and wxFrame::SetMenuBar")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:menu-bar :parent frame)") (:p "Native-backed CLOS construction; ownership transfers only into the managed parent hierarchy. Labels/help are Unicode strings without NUL. Nonseparator labels must be nonempty."))))
(:entry "api/menu-count" :names ("menu-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Count menus attached to this bar." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:menu-count bar)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU-BAR is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "Nonnegative integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Count menus attached to this bar.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuBar::GetMenuCount"))))
(:entry "api/menu-item" :names ("menu-item") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Create and append a normal/check/separator item. Normal/check IDs are positive signed32 and unique across the bar. Separators require NIL ID and empty label/help. Check state is only valid for :CHECK. Help is construction-only. Concrete subclass initargs and DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported; native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed initialization cleans newly allocated resources and descendants; it does not undo arbitrary external mutations. Explicit :ENABLED-P or :CHECKED-P on a separator rejects even NIL. A normal item permits NIL checked state but rejects a non-NIL initial check." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "menu-item")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU via :PARENT; :ID, :LABEL, :HELP, :KIND, :CHECKED-P and :ENABLED-P.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Create and append a normal/check/separator item. Normal/check IDs are positive signed32 and unique across the bar. Separators require NIL ID and empty label/help. Check state is only valid for :CHECK. Help is construction-only. Concrete subclass initargs and DEFAULT-INITARGS are supported; native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Failed initialization cleans newly allocated resources and descendants; it does not undo arbitrary external mutations. Explicit :ENABLED-P or :CHECKED-P on a separator rejects even NIL. A normal item permits NIL checked state but rejects a non-NIL initial check.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuItem and wxMenu::Append")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:menu-item :parent menu :id 1001 :label \"&Open\")") (:p "Native-backed CLOS construction; ownership transfers only into the managed parent hierarchy. Labels/help are Unicode strings without NUL. Nonseparator labels must be nonempty."))))
(:entry "api/menu-item-count" :names ("menu-item-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Count all items including separators in this menu." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:menu-item-count menu)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "Nonnegative integer.")) ("Description" (:p "Count all items including separators in this menu.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenu::GetMenuItemCount"))))
(:entry "api/menu-item-id" :names ("menu-item-id") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read immutable routing identity. IDs are unique across the managed bar." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:menu-item-id item)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU-ITEM is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive command ID or NIL for a separator.")) ("Description" (:p "Read immutable routing identity. IDs are unique across the managed bar.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuItem::GetId"))))
(:entry "api/menu-item-kind" :names ("menu-item-kind") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read immutable item kind; radio and submenu kinds are outside this slice." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:menu-item-kind item)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU-ITEM is live.")) ("Returns" (:p ":NORMAL, :CHECK or :SEPARATOR.")) ("Description" (:p "Read immutable item kind; radio and submenu kinds are outside this slice.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuItem::GetKind"))))
(:entry "api/menu-label" :names ("menu-label" "(setf menu-label)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write bar tab label including native mnemonic syntax. This differs from a menu item label. Scalar writes are permitted in callbacks." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:menu-label menu)")) ("Arguments" (:p "MENU is live; SETF VALUE is a nonempty Unicode string without NUL.")) ("Returns" (:p "Raw top-level tab label; SETF returns VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write bar tab label including native mnemonic syntax. This differs from a menu item label. Scalar writes are permitted in callbacks.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxMenuBar::GetMenuLabel / SetMenuLabel")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:menu-label menu) value)") (:p "Assign the raw tab label; no command callback is synthesized."))))
(:entry "api/menu-resource" :names ("menu-resource") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-owned menu resource identity with explicit liveness and destruction. Resources are not windows or event handlers; mixed managed ancestry rejects before allocation." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:menu-resource")) ("Arguments" (:p "Abstract base of MENU-BAR, MENU and MENU-ITEM.")) ("Returns" (:p "No direct abstract construction.")) ("Description" (:p "Native-owned menu resource identity with explicit liveness and destruction. Resources are not windows or event handlers; mixed managed ancestry rejects before allocation.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed resource. Native resource/type/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types and CLOS receivers signal Lisp conditions. Structural operations reject during callbacks, pumps and RUN. Ownership stays in the frame/bar/menu native hierarchy; no raw pointer adoption or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bounded wxMenuBar/wxMenu/wxMenuItem lifetime protocol.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:menu-resource) ; signals an error") (:p "Abstract base: no direct instantiation or native allocation. A subclass must inherit exactly one concrete MENU-BAR, MENU or MENU-ITEM class. Mixed event-handler/window/owned-event ancestry and multiple concrete menu ancestry reject before native allocation. Use the concrete constructor with :PARENT frame/bar/menu."))))
(:entry "api/menu-resource-alive-p" :names ("menu-resource-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query managed native liveness. Parent destruction invalidates all descendants. Requires an active session; no pointer adoption." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:menu-resource-alive-p resource)")) ("Arguments" (:p "RESOURCE is a menu resource.")) ("Returns" (:p "T/NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Query managed native liveness. Parent destruction invalidates all descendants. Requires an active session; no pointer adoption.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a completed managed wrapper. Expired/destroyed native resources return NIL rather than requiring native liveness. Invalid Lisp receivers signal CLOS conditions; no raw native adoption or GC finalizer. Pending/scheduled native deletion of a window receiver/owning frame or any native ancestor makes that resource unavailable; IsBeingDeleted alone is not the liveness test.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge registry identity and native ownership"))))
(:entry "api/message-dialog" :names ("message-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a generic GUI message dialog. Message body, button set and icon are fixed at construction. SHOW-MODAL/END-MODAL support offered :YES/:NO results as well as safe :CANCEL; there is no native OS alert backend." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:message-dialog")) ("Arguments" (:p "Optional :PARENT, :MESSAGE(default empty string), :TITLE(default \"Message\"), :BUTTONS(default :OK) and :ICON(default :INFORMATION). Buttons :OK/:OK-CANCEL/:YES-NO/:YES-NO-CANCEL; icons :NONE/:INFORMATION/:WARNING/:ERROR/:QUESTION.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed dialog.")) ("Description" (:p "Construct a generic GUI message dialog. Message body, button set and icon are fixed at construction. SHOW-MODAL/END-MODAL support offered :YES/:NO results as well as safe :CANCEL; there is no native OS alert backend.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGenericMessageDialog; bounded equivalent wxMessageDialog public surface (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:message-dialog :message \"Save changes?\" :buttons :yes-no-cancel)") (:p "Native-backed DIALOG/WINDOW subclass supporting direct construction, subclass slots/DEFAULT-INITARGS/AFTER and rollback. Optional parent is normalized to explicit requested window (including hidden) or truly parentless NIL. Construction is allowed in GUI-thread callbacks/RUN/pumps. Failed initialization cleans new resources/roots without reversing arbitrary external changes. Strings are Unicode without NUL."))))
(:entry "api/message-dialog-buttons" :names ("message-dialog-buttons") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read fixed offered button set. :YES/:NO modal completion is valid only when offered; :CANCEL remains a safe unwind result." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:message-dialog-buttons dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is a live MESSAGE-DIALOG.")) ("Returns" (:p ":OK, :OK-CANCEL, :YES-NO or :YES-NO-CANCEL.")) ("Description" (:p "Read fixed offered button set. :YES/:NO modal completion is valid only when offered; :CANCEL remains a safe unwind result.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires active main-thread GUI session and live managed modal dialog, including receiver/ancestor pending/scheduled-deletion checks. Uses explicit generic wxWidgets GUI backend; native OS NSAlert/NSPanel implementations remain unbound. No backend selector, native pointer adoption, modeless interface or GC finalizer.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bounded wxMessageDialog button-style view"))))
(:entry "api/move-notebook-page" :names ("move-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Silent native remove/insert move preserving selected page by identity; no native MovePage parity claim. Allocation failure is not transactional and can leave a live detached page. Native InsertPage places the moved page in the active group; removing an empty source group can merge the workspace back to one group." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:move-notebook-page book from to)")) ("Arguments" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK and existing zero-based FROM/TO indices.")) ("Returns" (:p "BOOK.")) ("Description" (:p "Silent native remove/insert move preserving selected page by identity; no native MovePage parity claim. Allocation failure is not transactional and can leave a live detached page. Native InsertPage places the moved page in the active group; removing an empty source group can merge the workspace back to one group.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::RemovePage/InsertPage/ChangeSelection, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/native-error" :names ("native-error") :kind :condition :kind-name "Condition" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Signals native bridge failures instead of exposing C++ exceptions or native pointers." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(handler-case form (wxlambda:native-error (condition) ...))")) ("Arguments" (:p "Condition class; native diagnostic text is available through its printed report.")) ("Returns" (:p "A Lisp ERROR condition.")) ("Description" (:p "Signals native bridge failures instead of exposing C++ exceptions or native pointers.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Catch with HANDLER-CASE or HANDLER-BIND. Lisp argument and callback conditions retain their own condition types.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Bridge exception translation."))))
(:entry "api/navigate-focus" :names ("navigate-focus") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Perform native keyboard navigation starting from WINDOW via its parent traversal container. Only forward/backward traversal is exposed; no tab-order mutation, window-change flags or NavigateIn binding." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:navigate-focus window &key (forward t))")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW; keyword FORWARD defaults T (generalized boolean); NIL requests backward.")) ("Returns" (:p "Generalized native navigation result as T/NIL; not a portable focused-window identity.")) ("Description" (:p "Perform native keyboard navigation starting from WINDOW via its parent traversal container. Only forward/backward traversal is exposed; no tab-order mutation, window-change flags or NavigateIn binding.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Same shown/enabled/live/main-thread and callback deferral/operation guards as FOCUS-WINDOW. Native traversal order, wrapping, eligible controls and focus effects depend on port/container; successful return does not promise a particular widget.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Navigate with IsForward/IsBackward, wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/next-handler" :names ("next-handler" "(setf next-handler)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native next link through the session canonical wrapper map. SETF joins reciprocal vacant source-next/peer-previous endpoints, including existing segments, or detaches one reciprocal edge for NIL. Repeating an existing pair is idempotent; self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:next-handler handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live owned standalone EVENT-HANDLER/subclass. SETF PEER is another owned standalone handler or NIL.")) ("Returns" (:p "The EQ canonical managed next wrapper or NIL; SETF returns PEER.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the native next link through the session canonical wrapper map. SETF joins reciprocal vacant source-next/peer-previous endpoints, including existing segments, or detaches one reciprocal edge for NIL. Repeating an existing pair is idempotent; self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and valid standalone handles required. Reads are permitted in callbacks; SETF rejects RUN/pump/callback use. Window/application sources and peers reject. Wrappers are strongly rooted until destruction/rollback/session end; no ownership transfer, raw pointer or GC finalizer. Attached pushed nodes reject both peer reads and writes; use WINDOW-EVENT-HANDLER/POP/REMOVE so the standalone protocol cannot expose the borrowed window tail. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::GetNextHandler / SetNextHandler with managed reciprocal SetPreviousHandler (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:next-handler handler) peer-or-nil)") (:p "Join vacant reciprocal endpoints after cycle/ownership validation, or split one edge for NIL. Return supplied peer/NIL. Does not destroy handlers, reparent native ownership or permit in-dispatch structural edits. ABI43 also permits this operation inside a safe deferred UI action under RUN/poll; nested event callback guards remain."))))
(:entry "api/notebook" :names ("notebook") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Fixed setup-time panel pages, native selection and tab captions. Lisp page wrappers retain canonical identity; native notebook/ancestor owns page lifetime." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:notebook")) ("Arguments" (:p "Subclass of WINDOW; native wxNotebook.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed window wrapper.")) ("Description" (:p "Fixed setup-time panel pages, native selection and tab captions. Lisp page wrappers retain canonical identity; native notebook/ancestor owns page lifetime.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; NOTEBOOK receivers and fixed setup-time PANEL pages only. Invalid handles/indices/ownership signal. No removal, reordering, reparenting, icons, arbitrary styles or other book controls.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxNotebook / wxBookCtrlBase (wxWidgets 3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:notebook :parent parent)") (:p "PARENT required, other native arguments default. Subclass slot initargs/defaults/AFTER hooks and managed rollback apply. Add fully initialized page panels after their construction; no page self-attachment during its initializer."))))
(:entry "api/notebook-page" :names ("notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native page identity then resolve its strongly rooted Lisp wrapper. Access during successful native publication is supported. No new wrapper/native adoption is performed." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:notebook-page book index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BOOK notebook, INDEX existing zero-based signed-int page index.")) ("Returns" (:p "The canonical EQ panel wrapper supplied to ADD-NOTEBOOK-PAGE.")) ("Description" (:p "Read native page identity then resolve its strongly rooted Lisp wrapper. Access during successful native publication is supported. No new wrapper/native adoption is performed.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; NOTEBOOK receivers and fixed setup-time PANEL pages only. Invalid handles/indices/ownership signal. No removal, reordering, reparenting, icons, arbitrary styles or other book controls. Also specializes on AUI-NOTEBOOK and returns canonical current PANEL identity; indices can change after native drag or structural edits.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBookCtrlBase::GetPage (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/notebook-page-count" :names ("notebook-page-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the fixed managed page collection count." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:notebook-page-count book)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BOOK notebook.")) ("Returns" (:p "Current nonnegative native page count.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the fixed managed page collection count.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; NOTEBOOK receivers and fixed setup-time PANEL pages only. Invalid handles/indices/ownership signal. No removal, reordering, reparenting, icons, arbitrary styles or other book controls. Also specializes on AUI-NOTEBOOK with checked native lifetime and fixed256-page capacity.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBookCtrlBase::GetPageCount (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/notebook-page-index" :names ("notebook-page-index") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Resolve stable page wrapper to current position after dynamic edits/native same-book reorder. Destroyed wrappers reject; index is not durable identity." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:notebook-page-index book page)")) ("Arguments" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK and live PANEL.")) ("Returns" (:p "Current zero-based index, or NIL when not attached to BOOK.")) ("Description" (:p "Resolve stable page wrapper to current position after dynamic edits/native same-book reorder. Destroyed wrappers reject; index is not durable identity.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::GetPageIndex, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/notebook-page-label" :names ("notebook-page-label" "(setf notebook-page-label)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Reads GetPageText. Native mnemonic processing/length limits differ by port; no exact arbitrary caption round-trip guarantee." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:notebook-page-label book index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BOOK notebook, INDEX existing zero-based page index.")) ("Returns" (:p "Independent string of current native caption.")) ("Description" (:p "Reads GetPageText. Native mnemonic processing/length limits differ by port; no exact arbitrary caption round-trip guarantee.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; NOTEBOOK receivers and fixed setup-time PANEL pages only. Invalid handles/indices/ownership signal. No removal, reordering, reparenting, icons, arbitrary styles or other book controls. Also specializes on AUI-NOTEBOOK with copied caption<=4096UTF8 bytes; AUI SETF rejects callbacks and holds native operation/lifetime guards.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxBookCtrlBase/wxNotebook::GetPageText/SetPageText (wxWidgets 3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:notebook-page-label book index) value)") (:p "VALUE is a string without NUL, empty allowed. Native SetPageText; returns original VALUE string. No property alias or raw style exposure."))))
(:entry "api/numeric-range" :names ("numeric-range" "(setf numeric-range)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SLIDER or SPIN-CONTROL. SETF accepts exact two-element integer list (minimum maximum)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:numeric-range control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SLIDER or SPIN-CONTROL. SETF accepts exact two-element integer list (minimum maximum).")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh list of two bounds. SETF returns supplied list and silently clamps current value.")) ("Description" (:p "SLIDER or SPIN-CONTROL. SETF accepts exact two-element integer list (minimum maximum).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSlider / wxSpinCtrl::GetMin/GetMax/SetRange (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:numeric-range control) (list minimum maximum))") (:p "Validate strict bounded endpoints, read old numeric value, update silently and clamp to new range. Invalid intermediate spin edit may reject before mutation; supplied/result lists are not retained."))))
(:entry "api/numeric-value" :names ("numeric-value" "(setf numeric-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SLIDER or SPIN-CONTROL; :notify keyword for SETF (default NIL)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:numeric-value control &key notify)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SLIDER or SPIN-CONTROL; :notify keyword for SETF (default NIL).")) ("Returns" (:p "Bounded integer. SETF returns supplied integer.")) ("Description" (:p "SLIDER or SPIN-CONTROL; :notify keyword for SETF (default NIL).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSlider::GetValue/SetValue / wxSpinCtrl::GetTextValue/GetValue/SetValue (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:numeric-value control :notify t) value)") (:p "Default silent. Explicit notification commits then sends one native-class event even unchanged; no rollback on callback error. Invalid spin edit getter rejects, but integer write can recover it. Out-of-range values reject."))))
(:entry "api/off-click" :names ("off-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:off-click button)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BUTTON is a live source control.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Unbind before destruction; unbinding a destroyed handle is an error. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets event bridge unbinding"))))
(:entry "api/off-selection" :names ("off-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:off-selection control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL is a live CHOICE or LIST-BOX.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Unbind before destruction; unbinding a destroyed handle is an error. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets event bridge unbinding"))))
(:entry "api/off-text-change" :names ("off-text-change") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:off-text-change control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL (wxTextCtrl) is a live source control.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Unbind before destruction; unbinding a destroyed handle is an error. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets event bridge unbinding"))))
(:entry "api/off-toggle" :names ("off-toggle") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:off-toggle checkbox)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CHECKBOX is a live source control.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Remove the handler and release its closure. Repeated removal is harmless for a live control, including inside its callback.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Unbind before destruction; unbinding a destroyed handle is an error. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets event bridge unbinding"))))
(:entry "api/on-click" :names ("on-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :CLICK snapshots with no payload. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:on-click button function &key with-event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BUTTON and FUNCTION; WITH-EVENT true makes FUNCTION accept one EVENT; otherwise no arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :CLICK snapshots with no payload. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Handler closures stay rooted until explicit unbinding or session cleanup. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets command event binding"))))
(:entry "api/on-selection" :names ("on-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :SELECTION snapshots with selected index or NIL. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:on-selection control function)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL is a live CHOICE or LIST-BOX; FUNCTION accepts one immutable EVENT snapshot.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :SELECTION snapshots with selected index or NIL. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Handler closures stay rooted until explicit unbinding or session cleanup. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets command event binding"))))
(:entry "api/on-text-change" :names ("on-text-change") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TEXT-CHANGE snapshots with copied text. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:on-text-change control function)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL (wxTextCtrl) and FUNCTION; FUNCTION receives one EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TEXT-CHANGE snapshots with copied text. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Handler closures stay rooted until explicit unbinding or session cleanup. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets command event binding"))))
(:entry "api/on-toggle" :names ("on-toggle") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TOGGLE snapshots with boolean state. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:on-toggle checkbox function)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CHECKBOX and FUNCTION; FUNCTION receives one EVENT.")) ("Returns" (:p "The source control.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TOGGLE snapshots with boolean state. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Handler closures stay rooted until explicit unbinding or session cleanup. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWidgets command event binding"))))
(:entry "api/owned-event" :names ("owned-event") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed CLOS construction supports subclasses, slot initargs, defaults and AFTER hooks. Native origin is NIL. Mixed ancestry with EVENT-HANDLER/window is invalid. Explicit destruction or session cleanup owns deletion; there is no GC finalizer." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:owned-event")) ("Arguments" (:p "Construct with MAKE-INSTANCE or MAKE-EVENT; KIND/payload options match supported synthetic events. CLONE-FROM accepts an owned event/current context.")) ("Returns" (:p "A detached session-owned native event resource, not a snapshot or borrowed context.")) ("Description" (:p "Native-backed CLOS construction supports subclasses, slot initargs, defaults and AFTER hooks. Native origin is NIL. Mixed ancestry with EVENT-HANDLER/window is invalid. Explicit destruction or session cleanup owns deletion; there is no GC finalizer.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Exact supported command/notify/close/idle native classes only; one active main-thread session. No native handle initarg, arbitrary derived event class, origin retention or userdata/client ownership. TRANSFER-EVENT supports bounded native ownership handoff of this resource; copy APIs preserve it.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxCommandEvent / wxNotifyEvent / wxCloseEvent / wxIdleEvent construction and wxEvent::Clone (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:owned-event :kind :click)
(wxlambda:make-event :kind registered-name :text \"payload\" :integer 1)") (:p "Inherited native initialization runs before subclass AFTER hooks; managed failures roll back mixed native resources. Direct MAKE-INSTANCE :CLONE-FROM preserves source native state and ignores payload initargs/defaults. Factories reject explicit clone payload overrides. EXTRA-LONG initargs follow command/notify-only native LONG validation; inherited clone defaults never replace source values. Idle construction supports MORE-REQUESTED-P; clones preserve source state over inherited defaults and factory explicit payload overrides reject."))))
(:entry "api/panel" :names ("panel") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for a child wxPanel." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:panel")) ("Arguments" (:p "Superclass: WXLAMBDA:WINDOW.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance of this class or a subclass (WINDOW itself is abstract).")) ("Description" (:p "CLOS wrapper for a child wxPanel.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Construction requires an active main-thread application session. Concrete classes create their native widgets in inherited INITIALIZE-INSTANCE methods; subclass AFTER hooks can use them. Native handles cannot be supplied as initargs. Lisp subclassing does not imply native C++ virtual callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxPanel (wxWidgets 3.2); this is a Lisp wrapper, not a native subclass.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:panel :parent parent)") (:p "PARENT is a live window and is required. Class :DEFAULT-INITARGS and custom slot initargs are honored; native creation precedes subclass AFTER hooks."))))
(:entry "api/pending-events-p" :names ("pending-events-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents across the current application. Does not report OS input, idle work or timers that have not queued an event. It is an observation, not a guarantee about the next dispatch. Safe to query during callbacks." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:pending-events-p )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "T if wxWidgets has queued pending events, otherwise NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Query wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents across the current application. Does not report OS input, idle work or timers that have not queued an event. It is an observation, not a guarantee about the next dispatch. Safe to query during callbacks.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session; use before startup or after cleanup signals NATIVE-ERROR. This API is scoped to the bridge application, not arbitrary wxApp instances.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/pop-event-handler" :names ("pop-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach the top entry. Default preserves native owned registry/root; DELETE true releases bridge ownership before native PopEventHandler deletion and clears canonical roots/bindings. Empty stacks reject instead of invoking native assertions." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:pop-event-handler window &key delete)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is bridge-managed with a nonempty managed stack. DELETE defaults NIL; true requests native deletion.")) ("Returns" (:p "Popped canonical handler, alive/unlinked, or NIL when DELETE is true.")) ("Description" (:p "Detach the top entry. Default preserves native owned registry/root; DELETE true releases bridge ownership before native PopEventHandler deletion and clears canonical roots/bindings. Empty stacks reject instead of invoking native assertions.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread non-dispatch boundary; RUN/pump/callback use rejects. Consumed/deleted wrappers reject later native access. No deletion of the base window or arbitrary native stack entry. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md. SCROLLED-PANEL rejects because wxWidgets owns a private scroll-helper handler; no helper adoption/removal. Ordinary bindings still work. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md. GRID and WEB-VIEW also reject this managed stack-aware protocol because their native composite scroll/browser handlers remain private. Ordinary event bindings and generic receiver processing retain their documented scope. See docs/GRID.md and docs/WEB-VIEW.md. AUI-NOTEBOOK also rejects this managed stack-aware protocol because native AUI manager/tab handlers remain private.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::PopEventHandler(bool) (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/post-event" :names ("post-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post an independent detached copy with wxPostEvent/AddPendingEvent; attach the receiver as copy origin. Input stays live/unchanged and may be destroyed or changed immediately. Delivery is asynchronous in the managed GUI session." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:post-event handler event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live EVENT-HANDLER/window, EVENT is a live OWNED-EVENT. No synthetic payload overrides.")) ("Returns" (:p "HANDLER after successful GUI posting.")) ("Description" (:p "Post an independent detached copy with wxPostEvent/AddPendingEvent; attach the receiver as copy origin. Input stays live/unchanged and may be destroyed or changed immediately. Delivery is asynchronous in the managed GUI session.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required. Existing session-isolated receiver and lazy text-entry-origin restrictions apply before emission. No non-GUI immediate dispatch, worker posting or ownership transfer. Managed standalone chains participate in native traversal; linking does not change pending queue ownership or introduce window/app pushed chains. Window receivers retain wxEvtHandler semantics and bypass pushed stacks; explicit PROCESS-WINDOW-EVENT/LOCALLY provide stack-aware synchronous routing. Synthetic session delivery to attached pushed handlers rejects before emission/transfer. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxPostEvent / wxEvtHandler::AddPendingEvent, bounded GUI copy mapping (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/previous-handler" :names ("previous-handler" "(setf previous-handler)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native previous link. SETF mirrors NEXT-HANDLER, joining vacant source-previous/peer-next endpoints reciprocally or detaching one edge for NIL. Self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation; an existing reciprocal pair is idempotent." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:previous-handler handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live owned standalone EVENT-HANDLER/subclass. SETF PEER is another owned standalone handler or NIL.")) ("Returns" (:p "The EQ canonical managed previous wrapper or NIL; SETF returns PEER.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the native previous link. SETF mirrors NEXT-HANDLER, joining vacant source-previous/peer-next endpoints reciprocally or detaching one edge for NIL. Self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation; an existing reciprocal pair is idempotent.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and valid owned standalone handles. Reads are permitted during callbacks; SETF rejects RUN/pump/callback use. Borrowed window/application sources and peers reject. Strong canonical roots preserve wrapper/subclass identity, not new native ownership. Attached pushed nodes reject both peer reads and writes; use WINDOW-EVENT-HANDLER/POP/REMOVE so the standalone protocol cannot expose the borrowed window tail. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::GetPreviousHandler / SetPreviousHandler with managed reciprocal SetNextHandler (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:previous-handler handler) peer-or-nil)") (:p "Join or split a reciprocal previous edge at a non-dispatch boundary; return PEER/NIL. Same lifetime, cycle and endpoint validation as NEXT-HANDLER. ABI43 also permits this operation inside a safe deferred UI action under RUN/poll; nested event callback guards remain."))))
(:entry "api/process-event" :names ("process-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously dispatch a fresh owned synthetic event through ProcessEvent, copy final veto state and then delete the event. Observer callbacks may run while handled-p is NIL because they Skip; native consumption/default handling determines the first result. Final veto is independent of handled-p and may be true from initial VETOED-P even without a matching handler. Close dispatch can run frame defaults. Callback errors re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary; handled nested errors do not stop RUN. No final values are returned when a condition escapes, and earlier callback mutations are not rolled back. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:process-event handler event &rest options &key &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live EVENT-HANDLER/window. KIND and keyword payloads match QUEUE-EVENT. LOGGING-OFF-P defaults NIL and is accepted only for :QUERY-END-SESSION/:END-SESSION; CAN-VETO-P applies to all close-family kinds. The second positional argument may instead be a live OWNED-EVENT, with no payload keyword overrides.")) ("Returns" (:p "Two values: native handled-p and final vetoed-p.")) ("Description" (:p "Synchronously dispatch a fresh owned synthetic event through ProcessEvent, copy final veto state and then delete the event. Observer callbacks may run while handled-p is NIL because they Skip; native consumption/default handling determines the first result. Final veto is independent of handled-p and may be true from initial VETOED-P even without a matching handler. Close dispatch can run frame defaults. Callback errors re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary; handled nested errors do not stop RUN. No final values are returned when a condition escapes, and earlier callback mutations are not rolled back. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required for registration/dispatch and scoped native access; inactive calls signal NATIVE-ERROR before FFI. Wrong receiver types use CLOS dispatch errors. Registry metadata lasts until session cleanup; snapshot data is immutable. Borrowed application dispatch is supported; no worker dispatch, validated OS session delivery or arbitrary native class construction is provided. Synthetic session kinds require isolated owned standalone handlers; application/window receivers reject before emission. Standalone session fallback to wxApp is suppressed even for skipped, disabled or unmatched delivery. Native application session bindings are distinct from synthetic probes. Owned session event copies retain isolated standalone-receiver guards. Copies carrying borrowed userdata/client pointers or unsupported exact native classes reject. Copied owned :TEXT-CHANGE delivery to text-entry receivers rejects before emission, preventing lazy GetString from shadowing the owned payload. Keyword synthetic behavior is unchanged. Managed standalone chains participate in native traversal; linking does not change pending queue ownership or introduce window/app pushed chains. Window receivers retain wxEvtHandler semantics and bypass pushed stacks; explicit PROCESS-WINDOW-EVENT/LOCALLY provide stack-aware synchronous routing. Synthetic session delivery to attached pushed handlers rejects before emission/transfer. Notebook native page events cannot be synthesized, queued, processed as owned events or contextually cloned in ABI37. ABI38 simple listbox command kinds support owned/synthetic dispatch and text/selection payloads; no automatic list-model mutation. Derived tree selection kinds cannot be synthesized/owned/cloned in ABI39. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::ProcessEvent; wxCloseEvent::GetVeto or NOT wxNotifyEvent::IsAllowed after dispatch. (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/process-event-locally" :names ("process-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously process an independent detached copy with ProcessEventLocally, including local pre-processing and native chained handlers, without normal outer global-filter/parent/application fallback. Source remains live/unchanged. Observer delivery can return handled NIL; final veto is independent. Native local static/default handlers may still execute, including frame-close behavior; local processing is not observer-only or a no-default-action mode." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:process-event-locally handler event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is a live EVENT-HANDLER/window; EVENT is a live OWNED-EVENT. No payload overrides.")) ("Returns" (:p "Two values: native handled-p and final-vetoed-p of the processing copy.")) ("Description" (:p "Synchronously process an independent detached copy with ProcessEventLocally, including local pre-processing and native chained handlers, without normal outer global-filter/parent/application fallback. Source remains live/unchanged. Observer delivery can return handled NIL; final veto is independent. Native local static/default handlers may still execute, including frame-close behavior; local processing is not observer-only or a no-default-action mode.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required. Existing supported-class, session-isolation, text-entry receiver and callback/context protections apply. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary. No pending queue pump, pushed-handler API or native virtual override is added. Managed standalone chains participate in native traversal; linking does not change pending queue ownership or introduce window/app pushed chains. Window receivers retain wxEvtHandler semantics and bypass pushed stacks; explicit PROCESS-WINDOW-EVENT/LOCALLY provide stack-aware synchronous routing. Synthetic session delivery to attached pushed handlers rejects before emission/transfer. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::ProcessEventLocally on a supported detached copy (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/process-events" :names ("process-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Yield to GUI events and process idle work without waiting for new input; re-signal callback errors after returning from native polling." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:process-events )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Yield to GUI events and process idle work without waiting for new input; re-signal callback errors after returning from native polling.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session. Forbidden inside RUN, either event pump or any native-to-Lisp callback (NATIVE-ERROR), and inside the application REPL debugger (Lisp error). Existing synchronous notifying setters remain supported. Explicit manual dispatch/pumping is rejected while a managed modal call is active; the native modal loop owns dispatch.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAppConsole::Yield(true) and ProcessIdle"))))
(:entry "api/process-pending-events" :names ("process-pending-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Dispatch queued wx events for all pending handlers of the bridge application via ProcessPendingEvents. Does not yield to OS input or run ProcessIdle. Does not wait for new events; callback duration and continuously requeued work may delay return. Callback conditions are contained at the native boundary and re-signaled afterwards." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:process-pending-events )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "NIL after successful dispatch.")) ("Description" (:p "Dispatch queued wx events for all pending handlers of the bridge application via ProcessPendingEvents. Does not yield to OS input or run ProcessIdle. Does not wait for new events; callback duration and continuously requeued work may delay return. Callback conditions are contained at the native boundary and re-signaled afterwards.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session; use before startup or after cleanup signals NATIVE-ERROR. This API is scoped to the bridge application, not arbitrary wxApp instances. Forbidden inside RUN, either pump or any native-to-Lisp callback (NATIVE-ERROR), and inside the application REPL debugger (Lisp error). Dispatch guards recover on callback failure. Synchronous notifying setters remain supported. Explicit manual dispatch/pumping is rejected while a managed modal call is active; the native modal loop owns dispatch.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAppConsole::ProcessPendingEvents (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/process-window-event" :names ("process-window-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Process a detached copy through native GetEventHandler stack routing, window and normal parent/application fallback. Source remains alive/unchanged; copy origin is WINDOW and callback source can be a pushed handler. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:process-window-event window event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is bridge-managed; EVENT is a live supported OWNED-EVENT. No payload overrides.")) ("Returns" (:p "Two values: native handled-p and final-vetoed-p of an independent copy.")) ("Description" (:p "Process a detached copy through native GetEventHandler stack routing, window and normal parent/application fallback. Source remains alive/unchanged; copy origin is WINDOW and callback source can be a pushed handler. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session with copied-event exact-class/session/lazy-text guards. Synthetic session delivery rejects; no origin retention or native class replacement. Generic PROCESS-EVENT and queued window operations still bypass pushed handlers. SCROLLED-PANEL rejects because wxWidgets owns a private scroll-helper handler; no helper adoption/removal. Ordinary bindings still work. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md. GRID and WEB-VIEW also reject this managed stack-aware protocol because their native composite scroll/browser handlers remain private. Ordinary event bindings and generic receiver processing retain their documented scope. See docs/GRID.md and docs/WEB-VIEW.md. AUI-NOTEBOOK also rejects this managed stack-aware protocol because native AUI manager/tab handlers remain private.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::ProcessWindowEvent on an independent owned-event copy (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/process-window-event-locally" :names ("process-window-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Search the window and its pushed handlers with local pre-processing/validators, without normal upward window propagation. Process an independent detached copy with receiver-window origin and unchanged source. Observer delivery may still return handled NIL. Native local static/default handlers can still run, including frame-close behavior; local routing is not observer-only." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:process-window-event-locally window event)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is bridge-managed; EVENT is a live supported OWNED-EVENT. No payload overrides.")) ("Returns" (:p "Two values: native handled-p and final-vetoed-p of the local copy.")) ("Description" (:p "Search the window and its pushed handlers with local pre-processing/validators, without normal upward window propagation. Process an independent detached copy with receiver-window origin and unchanged source. Observer delivery may still return handled NIL. Native local static/default handlers can still run, including frame-close behavior; local routing is not observer-only.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session and existing copied-event/session/lazy-text guards. Current contexts stay innermost-scoped; callback errors re-signal at the nearer boundary. No pending pump, external native chain adoption or native virtual Lisp hooks. SCROLLED-PANEL rejects because wxWidgets owns a private scroll-helper handler; no helper adoption/removal. Ordinary bindings still work. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md. GRID and WEB-VIEW also reject this managed stack-aware protocol because their native composite scroll/browser handlers remain private. Ordinary event bindings and generic receiver processing retain their documented scope. See docs/GRID.md and docs/WEB-VIEW.md. AUI-NOTEBOOK also rejects this managed stack-aware protocol because native AUI manager/tab handlers remain private.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::ProcessWindowEventLocally on an independent copy (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/pulse-gauge" :names ("pulse-gauge") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request platform-native indeterminate progress. Call periodically while keeping the GUI event loop responsive. Visual animation and value readings vary by platform; no timer, worker dispatch or completion event is provided. SETF GAUGE-VALUE restores determinate mode." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:pulse-gauge gauge)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GAUGE is a live gauge.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied gauge.")) ("Description" (:p "Request platform-native indeterminate progress. Call periodically while keeping the GUI event loop responsive. Visual animation and value readings vary by platform; no timer, worker dispatch or completion event is provided. SETF GAUGE-VALUE restores determinate mode.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires a live gauge in an active main-thread GUI session. Stale/destroyed handles, native type errors and values above the range signal NATIVE-ERROR; wrong Lisp receivers use CLOS dispatch errors. Numeric arguments must fit signed 32-bit integers; invalid Lisp types/ranges signal TYPE-ERROR. No command events or native virtual overrides.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGauge::Pulse (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/push-event-handler" :names ("push-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Push above the existing stack top while keeping native ownership in the bridge registry. Reject linked/attached or borrowed window/app peers, active session bindings and queued session events before mutation." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:push-event-handler window handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is bridge-managed; HANDLER is a live unlinked standalone owned EVENT-HANDLER/subclass, not already attached.")) ("Returns" (:p "HANDLER after managed push.")) ("Description" (:p "Push above the existing stack top while keeping native ownership in the bridge registry. Reject linked/attached or borrowed window/app peers, active session bindings and queued session events before mutation.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread non-dispatch boundary; RUN/pump/callback use rejects. Canonical wrapper rooting continues. No raw native adoption or window ownership transfer. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md. SCROLLED-PANEL rejects because wxWidgets owns a private scroll-helper handler; no helper adoption/removal. Ordinary bindings still work. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md. GRID and WEB-VIEW also reject this managed stack-aware protocol because their native composite scroll/browser handlers remain private. Ordinary event bindings and generic receiver processing retain their documented scope. See docs/GRID.md and docs/WEB-VIEW.md. AUI-NOTEBOOK also rejects this managed stack-aware protocol because native AUI manager/tab handlers remain private.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::PushEventHandler with managed ownership/session guards (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/queue-click" :names ("queue-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post a button click for later dispatch. It uses the handler registered at dispatch time, including any replacement." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:queue-click button)")) ("Arguments" (:p "BUTTON is a live button.")) ("Returns" (:p "T.")) ("Description" (:p "Post a button click for later dispatch. It uses the handler registered at dispatch time, including any replacement.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxPostEvent / wxEVT_BUTTON"))))
(:entry "api/queue-event" :names ("queue-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Queue a copied synthetic event: wxCommandEvent for seven command kinds, wxCloseEvent for close/session kinds and wxIdleEvent for :IDLE. Ordinary control properties are not changed directly. A queued close on a frame may run its native default closing action; use CLOSE-WINDOW for a synchronous acceptance result. Explicit UTF-8 lengths preserve text. Close events take no command payload, may be vetoable or non-vetoable, and do not normally propagate to parents. Registry types create wxCommandEvent or wxNotifyEvent according to their declared family. Initial veto applies only to custom notify types. Queuing offers no final veto/handled result; use PROCESS-EVENT when a synchronous decision is required. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:queue-event handler event &rest options &key &allow-other-keys)")) ("Arguments" (:p "HANDLER is live; KIND is a built-in keyword or registered name. ID defaults 0; TEXT defaults empty. CHECKED-P is toggle/menu-only; SELECTION is NIL/nonnegative index for selection. CAN-VETO-P is close-family-only (default T). Registered types accept signed INTEGER (default 0) and copied TEXT; registered notify types accept initial VETOED-P (default NIL). LOGGING-OFF-P defaults NIL and is accepted only for :QUERY-END-SESSION/:END-SESSION; CAN-VETO-P applies to all close-family kinds. The second positional argument may instead be a live OWNED-EVENT, with no payload keyword overrides.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied handler.")) ("Description" (:p "Queue a copied synthetic event: wxCommandEvent for seven command kinds, wxCloseEvent for close/session kinds and wxIdleEvent for :IDLE. Ordinary control properties are not changed directly. A queued close on a frame may run its native default closing action; use CLOSE-WINDOW for a synchronous acceptance result. Explicit UTF-8 lengths preserve text. Close events take no command payload, may be vetoable or non-vetoable, and do not normally propagate to parents. Registry types create wxCommandEvent or wxNotifyEvent according to their declared family. Initial veto applies only to custom notify types. Queuing offers no final veto/handled result; use PROCESS-EVENT when a synchronous decision is required. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session required; otherwise NATIVE-ERROR. Stale/deleting receivers reject registration/queuing. Invalid event kinds, IDs and payload options signal Lisp errors; wrong receiver types use CLOS dispatch errors. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Contexts support scoped Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto. Arbitrary native events, native control-specific notify subclasses, arbitrary native userData pointers, external handler adoption and worker-thread dispatch remain unbound. Synthetic session kinds require isolated owned standalone handlers; application/window receivers reject before emission. Standalone session fallback to wxApp is suppressed even for skipped, disabled or unmatched delivery. Native application session bindings are distinct from synthetic probes. Owned session event copies retain isolated standalone-receiver guards. Copies carrying borrowed userdata/client pointers or unsupported exact native classes reject. Copied owned :TEXT-CHANGE delivery to text-entry receivers rejects before emission, preventing lazy GetString from shadowing the owned payload. Keyword synthetic behavior is unchanged. Managed standalone chains participate in native traversal; linking does not change pending queue ownership or introduce window/app pushed chains. Window receivers retain wxEvtHandler semantics and bypass pushed stacks; explicit PROCESS-WINDOW-EVENT/LOCALLY provide stack-aware synchronous routing. Synthetic session delivery to attached pushed handlers rejects before emission/transfer. Notebook native page events cannot be synthesized, queued, processed as owned events or contextually cloned in ABI37. ABI38 simple listbox command kinds support owned/synthetic dispatch and text/selection payloads; no automatic list-model mutation. Derived tree selection kinds cannot be synthesized/owned/cloned in ABI39. ABI58 :THREAD is a native base-family wxThreadEvent with copied immutable EVENT-TEXT, GUI-only callback dispatch and normal context lifetime. QUEUE-THREAD-EVENT alone permits worker posting after GUI binding; other GUI operations retain their thread rules. No owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvtHandler::QueueEvent; wxCommandEvent, wxCloseEvent or wxIdleEvent construction, SetCanVeto at close-event creation only."))))
(:entry "api/queue-thread-event" :names ("queue-thread-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Worker-safe wxThreadEvent delivery. Copies bytes before return and never invokes Lisp GUI callbacks on the posting thread. GUI BIND-EVENT :THREAD receives copied EVENT-TEXT in a base-family snapshot/current context. Queue acceptance does not guarantee callback delivery. The packet stores an independently owned native wxThreadEvent string through SetString; all worker temporary aliases die before publication. GetString and inherited native Clone retain native string semantics; public owned-event cloning remains unsupported." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:queue-thread-event receiver payload)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Existing EVENT-HANDLER receiver with a GUI-established :THREAD binding endpoint; PAYLOAD string of at most1MiB UTF-8, including NUL.")) ("Returns" (:p "RECEIVER after copied native queue acceptance.")) ("Description" (:p "Worker-safe wxThreadEvent delivery. Copies bytes before return and never invokes Lisp GUI callbacks on the posting thread. GUI BIND-EVENT :THREAD receives copied EVENT-TEXT in a base-family snapshot/current context. Queue acceptance does not guarantee callback delivery. The packet stores an independently owned native wxThreadEvent string through SetString; all worker temporary aliases die before publication. GetString and inherited native Clone retain native string semantics; public owned-event cloning remains unsupported.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Only this operation is worker-safe. Endpoint registry and target teardown synchronize independently of GUI registries; posts never call ready or touch wxWeakRef. Endpoints survive unbinding until native receiver destruction; unbound packets may be ignored. At most256 queued/delivering packets per receiver and4096 per session; full/stale/unregistered/shutdown posts signal NATIVE-ERROR. GUI shutdown closes ingress before native cleanup; late posts reject without entering wx. No public endpoint/thread/job/editor abstraction, arbitrary Lisp object/pointer payload, or owned/synthetic/cloned :THREAD events. See docs/THREAD-EVENTS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxThreadEvent, wxEvtHandler::QueueEvent, wxWidgets3.2.12 pinned pending-event lock behavior."))))
(:entry "api/radio-box" :names ("radio-box") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:radio-box")) ("Arguments" (:p "PARENT (or :parent for MAKE-INSTANCE), :items proper list2..64 NUL-free strings, :label string default empty, :selection index default0, :orientation :vertical/:horizontal, subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed RADIO-BOX or validated subclass.")) ("Description" (:p "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed2..64 choices, mandatory valid zero-based selection, one row/column orientation. Active GUI session/native lifetime checks for widget operations; no standalone radio buttons, item mutation or full native parity. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxRadioBox::Create, wxRA_SPECIFY_COLS/ROWS (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:radio-box :parent panel :items '(\"First\" \"Second\"))") (:p "Supports slots/default initargs, native-ready AFTER hooks and managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/realize-toolbar" :names ("realize-toolbar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:realize-toolbar toolbar)")) ("Arguments" (:p "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator.")) ("Returns" (:p "T after native successful realization.")) ("Description" (:p "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Quiescent; exactly one successful call. Fixes tool collection. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxToolBar::Realize (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/refresh-list-items" :names ("refresh-list-items") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invalidate inclusive native row range; provider data remains application-owned. Return CONTROL." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:refresh-list-items control first last)")) ("Arguments" (:p "(control first last)")) ("Returns" (:p "Native property/copied value or documented receiver/value.")) ("Description" (:p "Invalidate inclusive native row range; provider data remains application-owned. Return CONTROL.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Main-thread active session; checked live native receivers. Invalid state signals NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain conditions. See REPORT-TREE-VIEWS guide for bounds and callback rules.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxListCtrl::RefreshItems"))))
(:entry "api/register-event-type" :names ("register-event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Allocate a process-local native event type and map NAME in the active session. Duplicate names, built-ins and unsupported families are rejected before registration. Names cannot be unregistered or replaced during this session. Registrations are session-wide metadata, not rolled back when an unrelated resource initializer fails. Native type IDs are not stable across processes." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:register-event-type name &key (family :notify))")) ("Arguments" (:p "NAME is a unique keyword not reserved by a built-in kind. FAMILY is :NOTIFY (default) or :COMMAND.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied NAME keyword.")) ("Description" (:p "Allocate a process-local native event type and map NAME in the active session. Duplicate names, built-ins and unsupported families are rejected before registration. Names cannot be unregistered or replaced during this session. Registrations are session-wide metadata, not rolled back when an unrelated resource initializer fails. Native type IDs are not stable across processes.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session required for registration/dispatch and scoped native access; inactive calls signal NATIVE-ERROR before FFI. Wrong receiver types use CLOS dispatch errors. Registry metadata lasts until session cleanup; snapshot data is immutable. Borrowed application dispatch is supported; no worker dispatch, validated OS session delivery or arbitrary native class construction is provided.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxNewEventType; synthetic wxCommandEvent/wxNotifyEvent family registration (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/remove-event-handler" :names ("remove-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Preflight membership and detach without deletion. A live detached handler or handler belonging to another window returns NIL unchanged; only present entries reach native RemoveEventHandler, avoiding its absent-entry assertion." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:remove-event-handler window handler)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is bridge-managed; HANDLER is a live owned standalone handler.")) ("Returns" (:p "T if removed from this window; NIL for a valid nonmember.")) ("Description" (:p "Preflight membership and detach without deletion. A live detached handler or handler belonging to another window returns NIL unchanged; only present entries reach native RemoveEventHandler, avoiding its absent-entry assertion.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread non-dispatch boundary; RUN/pump/callback use, stale peers and borrowed window/application peers reject. Own pending queue and native ownership survive; other stack entries remain intact. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md. SCROLLED-PANEL rejects because wxWidgets owns a private scroll-helper handler; no helper adoption/removal. Ordinary bindings still work. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md. GRID and WEB-VIEW also reject this managed stack-aware protocol because their native composite scroll/browser handlers remain private. Ordinary event bindings and generic receiver processing retain their documented scope. See docs/GRID.md and docs/WEB-VIEW.md. AUI-NOTEBOOK also rejects this managed stack-aware protocol because native AUI manager/tab handlers remain private.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::RemoveEventHandler with safe managed membership probe (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/remove-notebook-page" :names ("remove-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach/hide without deletion or reparenting. Returned panel can be reinserted or explicitly destroyed, but remains a native child and dies with book." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:remove-notebook-page book index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK and current zero-based INDEX.")) ("Returns" (:p "Removed live PANEL.")) ("Description" (:p "Detach/hide without deletion or reparenting. Returned panel can be reinserted or explicitly destroyed, but remains a native child and dies with book.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::RemovePage, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/replace-splitter-pane" :names ("replace-splitter-pane") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace an attached pane, explicitly hide the old pane and show the new one." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:replace-splitter-pane splitter index pane)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Existing pane INDEX0/1 and distinct unattached PANEL child.")) ("Returns" (:p "Replaced hidden live PANEL.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace an attached pane, explicitly hide the old pane and show the new one.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and quiescent structural boundary or safe owner-bound deferred action; callback use rejects. Native-backed SPLITTER-WINDOW and fully initialized direct unsizered PANEL children. Canonical roots precede native sizing/focus work; old/new/attached pane and ancestor lifetime guards apply. Retained hidden panels remain native children and die with parent. No raw adoption, dynamic event/virtual hooks or editor layout abstraction. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md and docs/SPLITTER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow::ReplaceWindow, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/replace-stc-range" :names ("replace-stc-range") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace a native byte range; read-only rejects. Native modifications notify under existing guards; no general rollback after native callback errors." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:replace-stc-range control start end value)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Ordered existing byte START/END boundaries; valid UTF-8 replacement, new document<=64MiB.")) ("Returns" (:p "Supplied VALUE.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace a native byte range; read-only rejects. Native modifications notify under existing guards; no general rollback after native callback errors.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::SetTargetRange/ReplaceTargetRaw, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/replace-text" :names ("replace-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace half-open native [FROM,TO) with VALUE using native Replace and text-change notification. Equal endpoints insert, empty VALUE removes. Mutation may precede a callback condition rethrow; handled conditions permit recovery. Exact no-op event counts, caret/selection and undo effects are port-specific." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:replace-text control from to value)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL, FROM, TO, VALUE string without NUL. Positions are ordered nonnegative signed-64-bit integers bounded by native end.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied replacement VALUE string.")) ("Description" (:p "Replace half-open native [FROM,TO) with VALUE using native Replace and text-change notification. Equal endpoints insert, empty VALUE removes. Mutation may precede a callback condition rethrow; handled conditions permit recovery. Exact no-op event counts, caret/selection and undo effects are port-specific.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread application; TEXT-CONTROL receivers only, including Lisp subclasses. Wrong receiver dispatch, stale/wrong native handles and invalid ranges/types signal. Native offsets are not portable Lisp string indices; no -1 sentinels, GetRange, undo/redo, rich text or native file IO.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTextEntry::Replace (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/reset-grid-cell-editor" :names ("reset-grid-cell-editor") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:reset-grid-cell-editor grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGridCellEditor::Reset"))))
(:entry "api/resplit-window" :names ("resplit-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Attach second pane using current orientation/requested sash geometry. Native geometry can clamp." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:resplit-window splitter pane)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Exactly one initialized pane plus distinct unattached PANEL child.")) ("Returns" (:p "PANE.")) ("Description" (:p "Attach second pane using current orientation/requested sash geometry. Native geometry can clamp.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and quiescent structural boundary or safe owner-bound deferred action; callback use rejects. Native-backed SPLITTER-WINDOW and fully initialized direct unsizered PANEL children. Canonical roots precede native sizing/focus work; old/new/attached pane and ancestor lifetime guards apply. Retained hidden panels remain native children and die with parent. No raw adoption, dynamic event/virtual hooks or editor layout abstraction. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md and docs/SPLITTER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow::SplitVertically/SplitHorizontally, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/resume-event-propagation" :names ("resume-event-propagation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Restore the native propagation level without changing Skip. Zero is allowed and keeps propagation stopped. Invalid LEVEL signals TYPE-ERROR; expired contexts reject native access." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:resume-event-propagation event level)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTEXT is current; LEVEL is an integer from 0 through 2147483647, commonly returned by STOP-EVENT-PROPAGATION. A live OWNED-EVENT is also accepted for applicable operations.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied context.")) ("Description" (:p "Restore the native propagation level without changing Skip. Zero is allowed and keeps propagation stopped. Invalid LEVEL signals TYPE-ERROR; expired contexts reject native access.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread session and the innermost currently executing contextual callback. Expired or outer contexts in nested callbacks signal NATIVE-ERROR for native access. Activity queries return NIL for those contexts during a session; outside a session they signal NATIVE-ERROR. No raw native event pointer escapes. Built-ins and registered command/notify types. Veto applies only to actual wxCloseEvent/wxNotifyEvent contexts; arbitrary event types, general event construction/cloning and native control-specific subclasses and validated OS session delivery remains open. Live OWNED-EVENT receivers are also supported under the same native field/family validation. They require an active main-thread session and remain mutable until destroyed; snapshots stay immutable.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxEvent::ResumePropagation (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline)."))))
(:entry "api/return-to-application-repl" :names ("return-to-application-repl") :kind :restart :kind-name "Restart" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Abandon the failing REPL evaluation or callback operation using the active debugger restart." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(invoke-restart 'wxlambda:return-to-application-repl)")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments; invoke this restart from the application REPL debugger.")) ("Returns" (:p "Control returns to the application REPL.")) ("Description" (:p "Abandon the failing REPL evaluation or callback operation using the active debugger restart.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "This is an exported restart name, not a callable function. Available only while the application REPL debugger establishes it.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Lisp-only debugger recovery."))))
(:entry "api/run" :names ("run") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Block until STOP or the last top-level frame closes. Callback errors are re-signaled after returning from native code." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:run )")) ("Arguments" (:p "No arguments.")) ("Returns" (:p "NIL after the event loop returns.")) ("Description" (:p "Block until STOP or the last top-level frame closes. Callback errors are re-signaled after returning from native code.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and at least one frame. Forbidden inside RUN, either pump, any native-to-Lisp callback, and the application REPL. Native failures and callback conditions propagate. Explicit manual dispatch/pumping is rejected while a managed modal call is active; the native modal loop owns dispatch.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAppConsole::OnRun"))))
(:entry "api/run-web-script" :names ("run-web-script") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Asynchronously evaluates JavaScript. JSON-fragment success (undefined maps to null), native error or non-serializable result failure arrives through :web-script-result. Results over1MiB become an error. Ticket retires before event callbacks. Messages posted to window.webkit.messageHandlers.wxlambda.postMessage(value) arrive as JSON via :web-message; at most256 queued messages, each up to1MiB, excess dropped. Owner teardown drops late completions. Queued immutable command snapshots: :web-message text is JSON (including quoted strings); :web-script-result text is JSON on success or an error description on failure, EVENT-INTEGER is1/0 and EVENT-EXTRA-LONG is the request ticket; :web-loaded text is native URL and :web-error text is native error description. BIND-EVENT supports scoped contexts/Skip/propagation but payload SETF rejects. Async delivery occurs through normal GUI polling/RUN, never directly from an Objective-C completion. Native loaded/error events can reflect prior/subframe navigation; no exact per-navigation correlation or veto API." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:run-web-script view script)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WEB-VIEW and NUL-free JavaScript string up to1MiB UTF-8; at most64 outstanding requests.")) ("Returns" (:p "Positive numeric request ticket.")) ("Description" (:p "Asynchronously evaluates JavaScript. JSON-fragment success (undefined maps to null), native error or non-serializable result failure arrives through :web-script-result. Results over1MiB become an error. Ticket retires before event callbacks. Messages posted to window.webkit.messageHandlers.wxlambda.postMessage(value) arrive as JSON via :web-message; at most256 queued messages, each up to1MiB, excess dropped. Owner teardown drops late completions. Queued immutable command snapshots: :web-message text is JSON (including quoted strings); :web-script-result text is JSON on success or an error description on failure, EVENT-INTEGER is1/0 and EVENT-EXTRA-LONG is the request ticket; :web-loaded text is native URL and :web-error text is native error description. BIND-EVENT supports scoped contexts/Skip/propagation but payload SETF rejects. Async delivery occurs through normal GUI polling/RUN, never directly from an Objective-C completion. Native loaded/error events can reflect prior/subframe navigation; no exact per-navigation correlation or veto API.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Verified macOS wxWidgets3.2.12 WKWebView backend only. Active GUI thread/session and live WEB-VIEW WINDOW container; private browser child has no public handle. JavaScript enabled for trusted development content, not a security sandbox. Known wx native dialogs/upload/popups/printing suppressed, known permission requests denied; no complete OS WebKit security/permission policy claim. Mutations/scripts reject callbacks and protect receiver/ancestors/native reentry; use deferred actions. No managed handler stacks, native backend adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned web events. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md. Explicit URL navigation/base-URL inputs support about:blank or absolute http/https/file URLs only; native links, redirects and subresource loads are not a complete navigation sandbox. JSON script messages can originate from all frames and origins; receipt does not authenticate the sender or authorize an action. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Internal WKWebView evaluateJavaScript completion adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12-owned WKWebView; wxWebView::RunScriptAsync/clientData ownership is not exposed."))))
(:entry "api/save-canvas-image" :names ("save-canvas-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Render same retained scene into private RGB24 bitmap and PNG. Export coordinates are pixels, one scene unit per pixel with clipping, not model scaling; fonts keep native point-size metrics. Internal PNG handler does not alter global registry. Existing target is overwritten; encoding is staged before open, but write/flush/close failure can leave partial output and is not atomic replacement." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:save-canvas-image canvas path &key (width 640) (height 480))")) ("Arguments" (:p "DRAWING-CANVAS, string/pathname PATH; WIDTH/HEIGHT default640/480, each1..2048 pixels.")) ("Returns" (:p "(pathname PATH) after successful PNG encoding/write/flush/close.")) ("Description" (:p "Render same retained scene into private RGB24 bitmap and PNG. Export coordinates are pixels, one scene unit per pixel with clipping, not model scaling; fonts keep native point-size metrics. Internal PNG handler does not alter global registry. Existing target is overwritten; encoding is staged before open, but write/flush/close failure can leave partial output and is not atomic replacement.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session, live managed DRAWING-CANVAS, no DC/native object adoption or Lisp paint callback. Native scene staging, rendering/export and Input lifetime/reentry guards; writes/export reject event callbacks. Copied bounded data only; font/paint/DPI appearance is native. See docs/DRAWING-CANVAS.md. Explicit UTF-8 native path conversion with NUL/empty-path rejection. Invalid arguments/native IO/render failures signal Lisp/native conditions; no general image/file-loader/printing or arbitrary filesystem fault recovery API.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "Private wxMemoryDC/wxBitmap/wxPNGHandler and checked wxFFileOutputStream output, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/save-grid-edit-control-value" :names ("save-grid-edit-control-value") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:save-grid-edit-control-value grid)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke the distinct native editor operation. Save leaves enabled; Hide is not cancel; Disable attempts save; Reset restores current editor baseline, which can change during prior Save/veto. All callback-time calls reject.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::SaveEditControlValue"))))
(:entry "api/save-image" :names ("save-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Encode via native PNG handler and write/flush/close the local native pathname. Existing output may be overwritten; failure may leave a partial file." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:save-image object path)")) ("Arguments" (:p "image path")) ("Returns" (:p "PATH.")) ("Description" (:p "Encode via native PNG handler and write/flush/close the local native pathname. Existing output may be overwritten; failure may leave a partial file.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/scale-image" :names ("scale-image") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Call native Scale using :NEAREST or default :HIGH, with1..4096 destination pixel axes and validated subclass construction." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:scale-image object width height &key (quality :high) (class 'image))")) ("Arguments" (:p "image width height &key quality class")) ("Returns" (:p "A new independently owned IMAGE.")) ("Description" (:p "Call native Scale using :NEAREST or default :HIGH, with1..4096 destination pixel axes and validated subclass construction.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/screen-to-client" :names ("screen-to-client") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native ScreenToClient; input±1000000 native screen units." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:screen-to-client object x y)")) ("Arguments" (:p "window x y")) ("Returns" (:p "Two-element converted coordinate list.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native ScreenToClient; input±1000000 native screen units.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxImage/wxBitmap/wxStaticBitmap/wxDisplay/wxWindow, selected native methods in wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/scroll-extent" :names ("scroll-extent") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SCROLLED-PANEL. Read-only." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:scroll-extent panel)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL. Read-only.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh current virtual (width height) pixel pair.")) ("Description" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL. Read-only.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. No callback-time fit/rate/position changes: defer via owner-bound UI action. Supported extent<=1000000 pixels/axis checked before explicit mutation, not globally enforced on inherited/native layout. Private native scroll helper stays owned; managed handler-stack APIs reject for this class. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxScrolled::GetVirtualSize (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/scroll-position" :names ("scroll-position" "(setf scroll-position)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF exact pair0..1000000 scroll units." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:scroll-position panel)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF exact pair0..1000000 scroll units.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native view-start pair; writer returns requested list, not clamped result.")) ("Description" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF exact pair0..1000000 scroll units.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. No callback-time fit/rate/position changes: defer via owner-bound UI action. Supported extent<=1000000 pixels/axis checked before explicit mutation, not globally enforced on inherited/native layout. Private native scroll helper stays owned; managed handler-stack APIs reject for this class. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxScrolled::GetViewStart/Scroll (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:scroll-position panel) '(0 10))") (:p "Native clamp/disabled axes can change accepted result; read back actual view-start. No -1 unchanged sentinel or partial setter; list not retained. Native focus/resize can change position later."))))
(:entry "api/scroll-rate" :names ("scroll-rate" "(setf scroll-rate)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF value is exact two-integer list0..256 pixels/unit." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:scroll-rate panel)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF value is exact two-integer list0..256 pixels/unit.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh (x y) pixels/unit pair; writer returns supplied list.")) ("Description" (:p "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF value is exact two-integer list0..256 pixels/unit.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. No callback-time fit/rate/position changes: defer via owner-bound UI action. Supported extent<=1000000 pixels/axis checked before explicit mutation, not globally enforced on inherited/native layout. Private native scroll helper stays owned; managed handler-stack APIs reject for this class. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxScrolled::GetScrollPixelsPerUnit/SetScrollRate (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:scroll-rate panel) '(0 16))") (:p "Zero disables an axis, including both zero. Returns supplied list, not retained; native rate changes may change pixel origin/clamp view. No callback mutation."))))
(:entry "api/scroll-stc-lines" :names ("scroll-stc-lines") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native LineScroll. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:scroll-stc-lines control columns lines)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; COLUMNS native scroll.; LINES native scroll.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native LineScroll. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/scrolled-panel" :names ("scrolled-panel") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary ":parent required, :scroll-rate exact pair0..256 default(0 16), subclass initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:scrolled-panel")) ("Arguments" (:p ":parent required, :scroll-rate exact pair0..256 default(0 16), subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed SCROLLED-PANEL.")) ("Description" (:p ":parent required, :scroll-rate exact pair0..256 default(0 16), subclass initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and valid native lifetime. No callback-time fit/rate/position changes: defer via owner-bound UI action. Supported extent<=1000000 pixels/axis checked before explicit mutation, not globally enforced on inherited/native layout. Private native scroll helper stays owned; managed handler-stack APIs reject for this class. See docs/SCROLLING-PANELS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxScrolled<wxPanel>/wxScrolledWindow (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:scrolled-panel :parent parent :scroll-rate '(0 16))") (:p "WINDOW subtype, not concrete Lisp PANEL; slots/default initargs, native-ready AFTER hooks and managed rollback supported."))))
(:entry "api/search-control" :names ("search-control") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Search query field with native search/cancel command gestures. Lisp WINDOW ancestry only; does not inherit TEXT-CONTROL editing/convenience APIs. Applications implement filtering." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:search-control")) ("Arguments" (:p "Required :parent WINDOW, :value defaults empty string and :hint defaults literal Search, plus subclass initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "Native-backed SEARCH-CONTROL WINDOW subtype.")) ("Description" (:p "Search query field with native search/cancel command gestures. Lisp WINDOW ancestry only; does not inherit TEXT-CONTROL editing/convenience APIs. Applications implement filtering.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and live WINDOW lifetime. Editable single-line copied UTF-8 query/hint, NUL/CR/LF rejected, empty accepted. Fixed native style/icon requests; actual native search/cancel/Enter/default-clear/text event behavior varies by port. Shared Input actual/propagated/composite callbacks and early Destroy guards. No style/menu/button visibility/editing/raw-resource APIs. See docs/SEARCH-CONTROLS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSearchCtrl::Create with wxTE_PROCESS_ENTER, icon requests, GetValue/ChangeValue and descriptive text, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:search-control :parent parent :value \"λ\" :hint \"Find records\")") (:p "Direct subclasses/defaults/native-ready AFTER hooks, one concrete widget kind and managed initialization rollback."))))
(:entry "api/search-hint" :names ("search-hint" "(setf search-hint)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write the placeholder independently of the query. Silent writes use shared Input guard; no notify option. No inference from native text or search/cancel events." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:search-hint control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SEARCH-CONTROL; SETF value is a NUL/CR/LF-free string, including empty.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh native descriptive text string; SETF returns supplied string.")) ("Description" (:p "Read/write the placeholder independently of the query. Silent writes use shared Input guard; no notify option. No inference from native text or search/cancel events.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and live WINDOW lifetime. Editable single-line copied UTF-8 query/hint, NUL/CR/LF rejected, empty accepted. Fixed native style/icon requests; actual native search/cancel/Enter/default-clear/text event behavior varies by port. Shared Input actual/propagated/composite callbacks and early Destroy guards. No style/menu/button visibility/editing/raw-resource APIs. See docs/SEARCH-CONTROLS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSearchCtrl::GetDescriptiveText/SetDescriptiveText, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:search-hint control) \"Find records\")") (:p "Copies input to native descriptive text, rejects same-source callback writes, returns input string. Native presentation remains port-specific."))))
(:entry "api/select-grid-block" :names ("select-grid-block") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request native block selection with zero-based inclusive bounds." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:select-grid-block grid top left bottom right &key add)")) ("Arguments" (:p "GRID, TOP, LEFT, BOTTOM, RIGHT, optional :ADD.")) ("Returns" (:p "GRID.")) ("Description" (:p "Request native block selection with zero-based inclusive bounds.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Owned wxGridStringTable only. Callback and active native editor guards apply to writes. wxWidgets3.2.12 audited semantics; see GRID-EDITING guide. No custom model/editor ownership.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxGrid::SelectBlock"))))
(:entry "api/selection" :names ("selection" "(setf selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read current selection: an index for CHOICE/LIST-BOX/NOTEBOOK, or a canonical managed TREE-ITEM view for TREE-CONTROL, with NIL when no selection exists. Reader NOTIFY is ignored. Writes are silent by default; notifying choice/list writes emit synthetic events, while notebook/tree writes use native vetoable selection. Return of a requested assignment does not prove native acceptance. Populated tree writes require a live same-tree item; NIL is empty-tree no-op only. Root creation and structural edits silently normalize valid selection before idle. RADIO-BOX always has exactly one valid index; its explicit notifying write commits before a native-class command event, without veto or rollback. COMBO-BOX selection writes also set item text; NIL clears both text and selection. Arbitrary text writes do not promise a selected item. LIST-CONTROL is fixed single selection, NIL clears; silent by default, :notify T allows actual native selected/deselected events." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:selection control &key notify)")) ("Arguments" (:p "CONTROL is a live CHOICE, LIST-BOX, RADIO-BOX, COMBO-BOX, NOTEBOOK or TREE-CONTROL; NOTIFY is meaningful for the writer only.")) ("Returns" (:p "Index/NIL for choice/listbox/notebook; non-NIL index for radio-box; canonical TREE-ITEM/NIL for tree-control. COMBO-BOX returns native committed index/NIL, not highlighted popup state.")) ("Description" (:p "Read current selection: an index for CHOICE/LIST-BOX/NOTEBOOK, or a canonical managed TREE-ITEM view for TREE-CONTROL, with NIL when no selection exists. Reader NOTIFY is ignored. Writes are silent by default; notifying choice/list writes emit synthetic events, while notebook/tree writes use native vetoable selection. Return of a requested assignment does not prove native acceptance. Populated tree writes require a live same-tree item; NIL is empty-tree no-op only. Root creation and structural edits silently normalize valid selection before idle. RADIO-BOX always has exactly one valid index; its explicit notifying write commits before a native-class command event, without veto or rollback. COMBO-BOX selection writes also set item text; NIL clears both text and selection. Arbitrary text writes do not promise a selected item. LIST-CONTROL is fixed single selection, NIL clears; silent by default, :notify T allows actual native selected/deselected events.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR. RADIO-BOX: bounded :radio-selection command events; immutable copied index/native label, current borrowed contexts; no owned/synthetic/clone radio events. Fixed2..64 choices, mandatory valid zero-based selection, one row/column orientation. Active GUI session/native lifetime checks for widget operations; no standalone radio buttons, item mutation or full native parity. See docs/RADIO-GROUPS.md. Also specializes on AUI-NOTEBOOK; empty readNIL, nonempty integer writes only. Silent ChangeSelection versus native notifying/vetoable SetSelection; writer returns request, read actual state. Callback writes reject.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxChoice/wxListBox::GetSelection/SetSelection; wxNotebook::GetSelection/ChangeSelection/SetSelection (wxWidgets 3.2.12). wxTreeCtrl::GetSelection/SelectItem in ABI39. wxRadioBox::GetSelection/SetSelection. wxComboBox::GetSelection/SetSelection, wxTextEntry::ChangeValue.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:selection control :notify nil) value)") (:p "For CHOICE: index or NIL for none; silent by default. :NOTIFY T emits one synthetic native choice selection event, including unchanged assignments. For NOTEBOOK: existing integer index only (no NIL); ChangeSelection is silent by default, :NOTIFY T uses native vetoable SetSelection. Same-page notification counts are native/port-dependent. Returns the requested value even when vetoed; read actual selection afterward. LIST-BOX mirrors CHOICE index/NIL behavior, with :LISTBOX-SELECTION text/index/action metadata. Item edits adjust selection silently per LIST-BOX.md. TREE-CONTROL requires a same-tree TREE-ITEM, or NIL only when empty. Native SelectItem is silent by default; :NOTIFY T can be vetoed. Returns the requested view, not proof of acceptance. RADIO-BOX requires a valid non-NIL index; silent by default, :NOTIFY T commits then emits one event even unchanged; same-group callback writes reject, silent other-group writes allowed. COMBO-BOX existing index/NIL only; silent default. :NOTIFY T emits exactly one :COMBO-SELECTION even unchanged/NIL, without extra text notification. Text and selected state commit before callbacks. See docs/COMBO-BOXES.md."))))
(:entry "api/set-stc-save-point" :names ("set-stc-save-point") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native SetSavePoint. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:set-stc-save-point control)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native SetSavePoint. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/set-stc-selection" :names ("set-stc-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native SetSelection. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:set-stc-selection control anchor caret)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; ANCHOR native position.; CARET native position.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native SetSelection. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/set-stc-style-bytes" :names ("set-stc-style-bytes") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Copy and apply native SetStyleBytes at the current StartStyling position; advance the styling cursor. Query STC-END-STYLED for the native styled boundary." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:set-stc-style-bytes control bytes)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL and a simple unsigned-byte 8 vector, one style byte per document byte.")) ("Returns" (:p "The supplied vector.")) ("Description" (:p "Copy and apply native SetStyleBytes at the current StartStyling position; advance the styling cursor. Query STC-END-STYLED for the native styled boundary.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "GUI thread; document byte bounds and 64MiB buffer limit. Same-control innermost STYLENEEDED permits this styling operation; other callback mutations reject. No retained Lisp buffer. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::SetStyleBytes, wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/set-stc-styling" :names ("set-stc-styling") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native GetLength, SetStyling. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:set-stc-styling control length style)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; LENGTH native nonnegative.; STYLE native style.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native GetLength, SetStyling. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/set-web-page" :names ("set-web-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Asynchronously loads HTML with native base URL resolution. JavaScript remains enabled; loading does not sanitize HTML or isolate its network/storage effects." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:set-web-page view html &key (base-url \"about:blank\"))")) ("Arguments" (:p "WEB-VIEW, NUL-free HTML string up to2MiB UTF-8; :base-url defaults \"about:blank\", up to8192 UTF-8 bytes. BASE-URL requires about:blank or an absolute http/https/file URL.")) ("Returns" (:p "Supplied HTML string.")) ("Description" (:p "Asynchronously loads HTML with native base URL resolution. JavaScript remains enabled; loading does not sanitize HTML or isolate its network/storage effects.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Verified macOS wxWidgets3.2.12 WKWebView backend only. Active GUI thread/session and live WEB-VIEW WINDOW container; private browser child has no public handle. JavaScript enabled for trusted development content, not a security sandbox. Known wx native dialogs/upload/popups/printing suppressed, known permission requests denied; no complete OS WebKit security/permission policy claim. Mutations/scripts reject callbacks and protect receiver/ancestors/native reentry; use deferred actions. No managed handler stacks, native backend adoption, owned/synthetic/cloned web events. See docs/WEB-VIEW.md. Explicit URL/base input accepts absolute http/https with host, absolute file paths, or exact about:blank; whitespace/control characters and malformed percent escapes reject. This input policy is not a universal page navigation/network sandbox. Explicit URL navigation/base-URL inputs support about:blank or absolute http/https/file URLs only; native links, redirects and subresource loads are not a complete navigation sandbox. JSON script messages can originate from all frames and origins; receipt does not authenticate the sender or authorize an action. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWebView/WKWebView bounded adapter, wxWidgets3.2.12; system WebKit runtime."))))
(:entry "api/show-modal" :names ("show-modal") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Run the native modal loop. Supported from menu/event callbacks, RUN or a pump; nested public SHOW-MODAL calls reject. Outer event contexts suspend during the modal call and become usable again after it returns; callbacks entered by the modal loop have their own valid innermost contexts. Bare callback errors cancel the modal operation and re-signal the primary condition after unwind. A nested notifying operation whose condition is handled locally can recover without cancelling. Manual RUN/pump/finish and structural menu edits remain guarded. Native close of the current dialog is consumed and cancels it; ancestor close events are consumed while modal. Public CLOSE-WINDOW on a protected ancestor rejects. Generic file UI prompts are redirected to guarded generic message dialogs. Internal prompts suspend borrowed contexts; errors or public cancellation unwind internal-to-outer sequentially. Cancelling an inner prompt normally returns to the outer dialog. Nested public SHOW-MODAL remains forbidden." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:show-modal dialog)")) ("Arguments" (:p "DIALOG is a live supported dialog, not already shown.")) ("Returns" (:p ":OK or :CANCEL; MESSAGE-DIALOG can also return offered :YES/:NO.")) ("Description" (:p "Run the native modal loop. Supported from menu/event callbacks, RUN or a pump; nested public SHOW-MODAL calls reject. Outer event contexts suspend during the modal call and become usable again after it returns; callbacks entered by the modal loop have their own valid innermost contexts. Bare callback errors cancel the modal operation and re-signal the primary condition after unwind. A nested notifying operation whose condition is handled locally can recover without cancelling. Manual RUN/pump/finish and structural menu edits remain guarded. Native close of the current dialog is consumed and cancels it; ancestor close events are consumed while modal. Public CLOSE-WINDOW on a protected ancestor rejects. Generic file UI prompts are redirected to guarded generic message dialogs. Internal prompts suspend borrowed contexts; errors or public cancellation unwind internal-to-outer sequentially. Cancelling an inner prompt normally returns to the outer dialog. Nested public SHOW-MODAL remains forbidden.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice/generic-message/generic-file scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides. Native validity includes the receiver and all native ancestors: bridge pending-destruction markers and the public wxApp scheduled-deletion list reject use even before IsBeingDeleted becomes true. SHOW-MODAL preflight must not enter a loop beneath an ancestor already queued for deletion. ABI37 rejects entry during notebook navigation/page callbacks; defer to later application work. ABI38 also rejects entry while a list-origin selection/activation callback is active. ABI39 also defers entry during tree operations/selection callbacks.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxDialog::ShowModal with bounded callback/lifetime bridge."))))
(:entry "api/show-stc-autocomplete" :names ("show-stc-autocomplete") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Show native autocomplete list using configured separator; applications supply items and acceptance policy." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:show-stc-autocomplete control length-entered items)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Byte prefix length within current caret and boundary; NUL-free separator-delimited ITEMS string<=1MiB.")) ("Returns" (:p "Supplied ITEMS.")) ("Description" (:p "Show native autocomplete list using configured separator; applications supply items and acceptance policy.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::AutoCompShow, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/show-stc-call-tip" :names ("show-stc-call-tip") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Show native call tip; applications supply content." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:show-stc-call-tip control position text)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Existing byte POSITION boundary; NUL-free TEXT<=1MiB.")) ("Returns" (:p "Supplied TEXT.")) ("Description" (:p "Show native call tip; applications supply content.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::CallTipShow, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/show-stc-lines" :names ("show-stc-lines") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native ShowLines. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:show-stc-lines control first last)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; FIRST native line.; LAST native line.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native ShowLines. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/show-window" :names ("show-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Show with true SHOW, hide with NIL. Existing one-argument calls still show the window and return it as their primary value." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:show-window window &optional (show t))")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is live; optional SHOW is a generalized boolean (default T).")) ("Returns" (:p "WINDOW, then a boolean indicating whether its shown state changed.")) ("Description" (:p "Show with true SHOW, hide with NIL. Existing one-argument calls still show the window and return it as their primary value.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR. Supported dialogs are modal-only: SHOW-WINDOW and SHOWN-P SETF reject them; use SHOW-MODAL. SHOWN-P reader remains available. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::Show(bool) / Hide() equivalent (wxWidgets 3.2)."))))
(:entry "api/shown-p" :names ("shown-p" "(setf shown-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the window's own shown flag. A hidden ancestor does not change this flag; it does not report effective screen visibility." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:shown-p window)")) ("Arguments" (:p "WINDOW is live.")) ("Returns" (:p "T or NIL.")) ("Description" (:p "Read the window's own shown flag. A hidden ancestor does not change this flag; it does not report effective screen visibility.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active GUI session on the process main thread. Invalid/destroyed handles or unsupported native arguments signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp argument/type errors remain Lisp conditions. One GUI session per process. Widget behavior uses CLOS generic dispatch. Wrong receiver types signal Lisp dispatch conditions; native handle/state failures signal NATIVE-ERROR. Supported dialogs are modal-only: SHOW-WINDOW and SHOWN-P SETF reject them; use SHOW-MODAL. SHOWN-P reader remains available. LIST-CONTROL inherits supported WINDOW operations; owner/ancestor writes defer during native virtual providers.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxWindow::IsShown (wxWidgets 3.2).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:shown-p window) new-value)") (:p "Assign the own shown flag; return the supplied value and a second native changed-state flag. Writers are generic functions with VALUE first, followed by the receiver."))))
(:entry "api/single-choice-dialog" :names ("single-choice-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a modal-only native single-choice dialog. Selection is always an in-range nonnegative index; NIL is not a choice. Strings are Unicode without NUL; empty strings are accepted. Defaults/subclass slot initargs and AFTER hooks use the native-backed CLOS protocol. Failed managed initialization destroys newly created resources; it does not reverse arbitrary external mutations." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:single-choice-dialog")) ("Arguments" (:p "Optional :PARENT window(default NIL), :MESSAGE(default \"Choose an item:\"), :TITLE(default \"Choose\"); required nonempty :ITEMS list/vector of strings and :SELECTION(default0) valid index.")) ("Returns" (:p "New native-backed dialog.")) ("Description" (:p "Construct a modal-only native single-choice dialog. Selection is always an in-range nonnegative index; NIL is not a choice. Strings are Unicode without NUL; empty strings are accepted. Defaults/subclass slot initargs and AFTER hooks use the native-backed CLOS protocol. Failed managed initialization destroys newly created resources; it does not reverse arbitrary external mutations.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Requires an active main-thread GUI session and a live managed dialog. Invalid native handles/state signal NATIVE-ERROR; invalid Lisp types/receivers signal Lisp conditions. Modal-only text-entry/single-choice scope; no arbitrary native adoption, GC finalizer or native virtual Lisp overrides. Native validity includes the receiver and all native ancestors: bridge pending-destruction markers and the public wxApp scheduled-deletion list reject use even before IsBeingDeleted becomes true. SHOW-MODAL preflight must not enter a loop beneath an ancestor already queued for deletion.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSingleChoiceDialog constructor (wxWidgets 3.2.12 baseline).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:single-choice-dialog :items '(\"One\" \"Two\") :selection 0)") (:p "Direct subclass construction is supported with DEFAULT-INITARGS and inherited native initialization. Native properties exist in subclass AFTER hooks. Standard DESTROY-WINDOW/native parent ownership governs cleanup. Construction is permitted on the GUI thread inside callbacks/RUN/pumps, so menu actions can create dialogs; menu structural-edit guards do not apply to dialog construction. The bridge normalizes the actual native parent to the explicitly requested window or NIL, retaining even a hidden requested parent. NIL means truly parentless rather than native automatic parent selection."))))
(:entry "api/slider" :names ("slider") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed slider, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0, :orientation :horizontal or :vertical." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:slider")) ("Arguments" (:p "Native-backed slider, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0, :orientation :horizontal or :vertical.")) ("Returns" (:p "Concrete native-backed widget.")) ("Description" (:p "Native-backed slider, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0, :orientation :horizontal or :vertical.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSlider (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:slider :parent parent :minimum 0 :maximum 100 :value 0)") (:p "Supports subclass slot/default initargs, native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure rollback. Parent and valid bounds/value required."))))
(:entry "api/slider-orientation" :names ("slider-orientation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SLIDER. Immutable constructor orientation." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:slider-orientation slider)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SLIDER. Immutable constructor orientation.")) ("Returns" (:p "Keyword :horizontal or :vertical.")) ("Description" (:p "SLIDER. Immutable constructor orientation.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSlider style (wxWidgets3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/spin-control" :names ("spin-control") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed decimal integer spin, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:spin-control")) ("Arguments" (:p "Native-backed decimal integer spin, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0.")) ("Returns" (:p "Concrete native-backed widget with arrows and editable native text.")) ("Description" (:p "Native-backed decimal integer spin, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session; native handle/type/lifetime checks. Supported endpoints±1000000 with minimum<maximum. Same-control numeric writes and protected lifetime/modal/clipboard/pump entry defer during source numeric/forwarded text callbacks. See docs/NUMERIC-INPUT.md for intermediate spin edits, supported scope and unverified ports.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSpinCtrl (wxWidgets3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:spin-control :parent parent :minimum 0 :maximum 100 :value 0)") (:p "Supports subclass slot/default initargs, native-ready AFTER hooks and managed failure rollback. Parent and valid bounds/value required."))))
(:entry "api/split-notebook-page" :names ("split-notebook-page") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Call existing wxAuiNotebook::Split to arrange a page in a native private tab group without reparenting or changing its wrapper/bridge ID/global catalogue index. A sole-page source group can be replaced rather than increasing group count. Geometry is native policy; selection veto can prevent final selection but does not undo committed split structure." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:split-notebook-page book index direction)")) ("Arguments" (:p "AUI-NOTEBOOK, current global page INDEX, DIRECTION :left/:right/:top/:bottom; at least2 pages.")) ("Returns" (:p "BOOK after native request.")) ("Description" (:p "Call existing wxAuiNotebook::Split to arrange a page in a native private tab group without reparenting or changing its wrapper/bridge ID/global catalogue index. A sole-page source group can be replaced rather than increasing group count. Geometry is native policy; selection veto can prevent final selection but does not undo committed split structure.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread GUI session and checked native lifetimes. All AUI writes reject callbacks; structural edits require quiescence or owner-bound deferred action. Canonical PANEL roots precede publication; remove retains hidden same-parent child, delete invalidates by native destruction. Full native tab-event spans protect book/pages/ancestors and block nested GUI/modal/clipboard entry. Top tabs with native programmatic Split, one-group mouse movement and active close; external transfer, mouse drag splitting, icons/art providers and managed handler-stack access remain unbound. Requires wxUSE_AUI and aui component. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md. Programmatic SPLIT-NOTEBOOK-PAGE preserves page parents and global catalogue identities; native selection may notify/veto after group structure commits. Split books use checked programmatic MOVE: native mouse movement is disabled until only one private group remains, with native drag hint/cursor cleanup. All mutations also reject an active native tab gesture/capture. Pinned3.2.12 has501 private tab-group ID allocations per book lifetime; split or empty-book insertion refuses exhaustion before creating unusable native tabs. Private group-local PAGE_CHANGING callbacks are filtered; public EVENT-SELECTION uses native global catalogue indices, while old-selection keeps native semantics (CLOSE can be group-local).")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxAuiNotebook::Split, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/split-window" :names ("split-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER FIRST SECOND: attach distinct fully initialized panel children once, outside RUN/pumps/callbacks. Returns T." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:split-window splitter first second)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER FIRST SECOND: attach distinct fully initialized panel children once, outside RUN/pumps/callbacks. Returns T.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER FIRST SECOND: attach distinct fully initialized panel children once, outside RUN/pumps/callbacks. Returns T.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope. ABI43 safe deferred UI actions are explicit structural boundaries even under RUN/poll; nested RUN/pumps remain rejected. See docs/DEFERRED-UI-ACTIONS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-minimum-pane-size" :names ("splitter-minimum-pane-size" "(setf splitter-minimum-pane-size)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: positive pixel minimum; generic SETF accepts 1..536870911, returns supplied value." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:splitter-minimum-pane-size splitter)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER: positive pixel minimum; generic SETF accepts 1..536870911, returns supplied value.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER: positive pixel minimum; generic SETF accepts 1..536870911, returns supplied value.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:splitter-minimum-pane-size object) value)") (:p "SPLITTER: positive pixel minimum; generic SETF accepts 1..536870911, returns supplied value."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-orientation" :names ("splitter-orientation" "(setf splitter-orientation)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: immutable :vertical (left/right) or :horizontal (top/bottom)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:splitter-orientation splitter)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER-WINDOW; SETF accepts :vertical or :horizontal.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER: immutable :vertical (left/right) or :horizontal (top/bottom).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope. Active main-thread GUI session and quiescent structural boundary or safe owner-bound deferred action; callback use rejects. Native-backed SPLITTER-WINDOW and fully initialized direct unsizered PANEL children. Canonical roots precede native sizing/focus work; old/new/attached pane and ancestor lifetime guards apply. Retained hidden panels remain native children and die with parent. No raw adoption, dynamic event/virtual hooks or editor layout abstraction. See docs/AUI-NOTEBOOK.md and docs/SPLITTER.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:splitter-orientation splitter) :horizontal)") (:p "Retile existing panes with native geometry; requires safe structural boundary, returns supplied orientation."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-pane" :names ("splitter-pane") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER INDEX (0 or 1): canonical panel wrapper, or NIL before attachment." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:splitter-pane splitter index)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER INDEX (0 or 1): canonical panel wrapper, or NIL before attachment.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER INDEX (0 or 1): canonical panel wrapper, or NIL before attachment.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-sash-gravity" :names ("splitter-sash-gravity" "(setf splitter-sash-gravity)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: native double gravity; generic SETF accepts real [0,1], returns supplied value." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:splitter-sash-gravity splitter)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER: native double gravity; generic SETF accepts real [0,1], returns supplied value.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER: native double gravity; generic SETF accepts real [0,1], returns supplied value.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:splitter-sash-gravity object) value)") (:p "SPLITTER: native double gravity; generic SETF accepts real [0,1], returns supplied value."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-sash-position" :names ("splitter-sash-position" "(setf splitter-sash-position)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: native pixel position; generic SETF accepts 0..536870911, returns supplied value. Native centering/clamping/deferred geometry applies." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:splitter-sash-position splitter)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER: native pixel position; generic SETF accepts 0..536870911, returns supplied value. Native centering/clamping/deferred geometry applies.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER: native pixel position; generic SETF accepts 0..536870911, returns supplied value. Native centering/clamping/deferred geometry applies.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:splitter-sash-position object) value)") (:p "SPLITTER: native pixel position; generic SETF accepts 0..536870911, returns supplied value. Native centering/clamping/deferred geometry applies."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-split-p" :names ("splitter-split-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: boolean native split state." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:splitter-split-p splitter)")) ("Arguments" (:p "SPLITTER: boolean native split state.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "SPLITTER: boolean native split state.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/splitter-window" :names ("splitter-window") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed fixed two-panel window; :parent, :orientation, :sash-position, :minimum-pane-size and :sash-gravity initargs." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:splitter-window")) ("Arguments" (:p "Native-backed fixed two-panel window; :parent, :orientation, :sash-position, :minimum-pane-size and :sash-gravity initargs.")) ("Returns" (:p "See arguments and supported behavior.")) ("Description" (:p "Native-backed fixed two-panel window; :parent, :orientation, :sash-position, :minimum-pane-size and :sash-gravity initargs.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Fixed panes; guarded lifetimes and callback reentry. Invalid/native stale operations signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. CHANGING must be handled to honor edits/veto; CHANGED is observational. See docs/SPLITTER.md for full scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxSplitterWindow / wxSplitterEvent, wxWidgets 3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:splitter-window :parent parent :orientation :vertical :sash-position 0 :minimum-pane-size 20 :sash-gravity 0.5d0)") (:p "Supports subclass slots/default initargs and AFTER hooks with managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/start-stc-styling" :names ("start-stc-styling") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Invoke native StartStyling. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:start-stc-styling control position)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL; POSITION native position.")) ("Returns" (:p "The control.")) ("Description" (:p "Invoke native StartStyling. Arguments use the checked native domains described in the styled-text guide.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md. Checked UTF-8 byte positions/native indices and GUI-thread lifetime. Native synchronous notifications protected. Read-only coordinate/marker queries are callback-safe. Mutations reject event callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the current innermost STYLENEEDED callback; use owner-bound deferred actions otherwise. No editor policy or custom native object adoption.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
(:entry "api/start-ui-timer" :names ("start-ui-timer") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Start periodic or one-delivery safe UI work. Native Notify marks one due tick, not a Lisp callback. Initial lower-bound filtering guards reused native IDs. Due work merges fairly with deferred actions." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:start-ui-timer function milliseconds &key owner one-shot)")) ("Arguments" (:p "FUNCTION of no arguments, MILLISECONDS integer1..86400000, optional :OWNER window/NIL and :ONE-SHOT truth value (default NIL).")) ("Returns" (:p "New immutable UI-TIMER ticket; function values ignored.")) ("Description" (:p "Start periodic or one-delivery safe UI work. Native Notify marks one due tick, not a Lisp callback. Initial lower-bound filtering guards reused native IDs. Due work merges fairly with deferred actions.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active main-thread session. Interval1..86400000ms, at most256 logical registrations; periodic default/optional one-shot, weak window owner or session lifetime. Coalesced safe-idle delivery under RUN/full polling, excluded from nested modal/native/callback/other safe work. wxUSE_TIMER required; OSX start currently verified only for wxWidgets3.2.12. See docs/UI-TIMERS.md. Invalid Lisp arguments signal Lisp errors; native/unavailable/start failures signal NATIVE-ERROR and release the prepared root. No inline function delivery, restart, interval setters or catch-up count.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxTimer default constructor/Start(continuous)/Notify/Stop plus bridge logical one-shot policy."))))
(:entry "api/static-bitmap" :names ("static-bitmap") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native wxStaticBitmap WINDOW with PARENT/BITMAP and native-backed subclass construction." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:static-bitmap")) ("Arguments" (:p "Native wxStaticBitmap WINDOW with PARENT/BITMAP and native-backed subclass construction.")) ("Returns" (:p "A native-backed instance.")) ("Description" (:p "Native wxStaticBitmap WINDOW with PARENT/BITMAP and native-backed subclass construction.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI/main-thread session and checked native lifetime. Image/bitmap values are session-owned and explicitly disposable; no raw pointers/finalizers. Native reads are callback-safe; writes, file IO, allocation/conversion, disposal and BITMAP-VALUE copying reject callback execution. Copied channels,256 resources/64Mi pixel aggregate,1..4096 pixel axes; PNG24 bytes..64MiB encoded. Native bitmap alpha/DPI conversion can change pixels. Invalid bounds/types/stale handles and native failures signal errors. See docs/IMAGES-DISPLAYS.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStaticBitmap, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:static-bitmap :parent parent :bitmap bitmap)") (:p "Concrete native-backed resource/control; subclass initargs/defaults/native-ready AFTER hooks and managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/status-bar" :names ("status-bar") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Concrete frame-owned status bar with :fields 1..16 (default 1)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "wxlambda:status-bar")) ("Arguments" (:p "Concrete frame-owned status bar with :fields 1..16 (default 1).")) ("Returns" (:p "A managed status bar with empty native text fields.")) ("Description" (:p "Concrete frame-owned status bar with :fields 1..16 (default 1).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Use :parent frame; fixed field count, equal relative widths, app-owned text. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStatusBar (wxWidgets 3.2.12).")) ("Construction" (:code-block "lisp" "(make-instance 'wxlambda:status-bar :parent frame :fields 1)") (:p "Concrete native-backed construction supports subclass slots/default initargs/AFTER hooks and managed rollback."))))
(:entry "api/status-field-count" :names ("status-field-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "STATUS-BAR." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:status-field-count bar)")) ("Arguments" (:p "STATUS-BAR.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fixed integer field count.")) ("Description" (:p "STATUS-BAR.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active live bar; field count cannot be changed. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStatusBar::GetFieldsCount (wxWidgets 3.2.12)."))))
(:entry "api/status-text" :names ("status-text" "(setf status-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "STATUS-BAR and optional zero-based FIELD (default 0)." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:status-text bar &optional (field 0))")) ("Arguments" (:p "STATUS-BAR and optional zero-based FIELD (default 0).")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied UTF-8 string. SETF returns supplied string.")) ("Description" (:p "STATUS-BAR and optional zero-based FIELD (default 0).")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Generic SETF accepts empty/Unicode string, rejects NUL and invalid/stale indices. App-owned text; automatic frame help disabled. Native errors signal NATIVE-ERROR; Lisp type/range errors remain Lisp conditions. See docs/FRAME-ACTIONS.md for backend, ownership and complete supported scope.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStatusBar::GetStatusText / SetStatusText (wxWidgets 3.2.12).")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:status-text status-bar) value)
(setf (wxlambda:status-text status-bar field) value)") (:p "Generic SETF accepts empty/Unicode string, rejects NUL and invalid/stale indices. App-owned text; automatic frame help disabled."))))
