(:entry "api/stc-point-from-position" :names ("stc-point-from-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native geometry conversion, not DIP or logical text columns." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:stc-point-from-position control position)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Existing UTF-8 byte POSITION boundary.")) ("Returns" (:p "Fresh (x y) native client pixel coordinates.")) ("Description" (:p "Native geometry conversion, not DIP or logical text columns.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::PointFromPosition, wxWidgets3.2.12."))))
