(:entry "api/stc-style-font" :names ("stc-style-font" "(setf stc-style-font)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Get/set native font face for a style. Exact installed face/fallback and glyph metrics remain native policy." :sections (("Syntax" (:code-block "lisp" "(wxlambda:stc-style-font control style)")) ("Arguments" (:p "Control, STYLE0..255; SETF NUL-free font face string<=1MiB.")) ("Returns" (:p "Copied native face name; writer returns supplied name.")) ("Description" (:p "Get/set native font face for a style. Exact installed face/fallback and glyph metrics remain native policy.")) ("Errors and scope" (:p "Active GUI thread/session and checked native STYLED-TEXT-CONTROL lifetime. UTF-8 byte offsets, never Lisp string indices; position arguments must be codepoint boundaries. Initial/replacement UTF-8 text supports embedded NUL and total<=64MiB; font/assist strings are NUL-free<=1MiB. Integer/index domains are bounded by the adapter. Mutations reject callbacks except same-control StartStyling/SetStyling/SetStyleBytes in the exact innermost native STYLENEEDED callback. Native synchronous events and source/ancestor lifetime/native-entry guards apply; use owner-bound deferred actions for other writes. No raw SendMsg, pointer/document adoption, lexer/resource ownership, worker calls or application editor abstractions. Requires wxUSE_STC and stc component. See docs/STYLED-TEXT.md.")) ("wxWidgets" (:p "wxStyledTextCtrl::StyleGetFaceName/StyleSetFaceName, wxWidgets3.2.12.")) ("SETF" (:code-block "lisp" "(setf (wxlambda:stc-style-font control style) value)") (:p "Return supplied value; copied native mutation with lifetime/domain/callback guards."))))
